	quest.00257563AF1401AC.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.00257563AF1401AC.title: "&eAdvanced Filter Upgrade"
	quest.00A6A28B51CE52D5.quest_desc: [
		"Just like the &cCharm of Life I&r, the &eCharm of Life II&r is consumed to prevent your death. When consumed, you'll regen all of your health and be given Regen IV, Resistance, and Fire Resistance for 30 seconds."
		""
		"These can be crafted with 4 &cCharms of Life I&r."
	]
	quest.00A6A28B51CE52D5.title: "&eCharm of Life II"
	quest.014CA5422B8D33AF.quest_desc: ["The &eEye of Desert&r will take you to the &eCursed Pyramid&r to fight the &e&lAncient Remnant&r."]
	quest.014CA5422B8D33AF.title: "&eEye of Desert&r"
	quest.01539CBEF77B9FA2.quest_desc: ["Adds a Furnace GUI to the Backpack."]
	quest.017CDF0FFBC52A94.quest_desc: [
		"Once you use the &bBurning Ashes&r on the &bAlter of Flame&r you'll get the &b&lIgnis&r."
		""
		"He has 11,250 &4Hearts&r and has a massive &bSword &fand &bShield&r."
		""
		"The &bShield&r will block damage you give and the &bSword&r can be used to slice and stab you. Once stabbed, you can't move, you can only attack. "
		""
		"He can also pounce on you, when he does, he will slam his &bShield&r down, making a Shockwave which will toss Blocks and you into the Air. He can do the same with his &bSword&r just without the need to pounce. "
		""
		"Another attack he has is &bFireballs&r. He will throw 3 &bFireballs&r into the Air, then they will be sent flying toward you! Hit them back at him as if they were a Ghast Fireball."
		""
		"Once you beat his &4Health&r to around 7,500 &4Hearts&r he will change colors to a &bLight Blue color&r. Now he will Attack quicker, deal more Damage, and get Lifesteal."
		""
		"His &bFireballs&r will also not be able to be reflected and he can now make different types of Shockwaves!"
	]
	quest.017CDF0FFBC52A94.title: "&b&lIgnis&r"
	quest.017CE47F7AB38F8D.quest_desc: [
		"A purple Bog!"
		""
		"These have Ink Mushrooms and Virulent Mix all over!"
	]
	quest.017CE47F7AB38F8D.title: "Ink Mushroom Bog"
	quest.01E58FC79DFC5765.quest_subtitle: "No battle effect. Increases the holder's friendship earned by 50%."
	quest.02040D0FBA685DC4.quest_subtitle: "The holder loses 1/8 of max HP per turn. Transfers to other Pokémon on contact."
	quest.0205615026CD000D.quest_desc: [
		"The &bIgnited Revenant&r stands in our way to kill the &b&lIgnis&r."
		""
		"The &bRevenant&r looks and acts like a Blaze, but instead of being Rods, he has Shields!"
		""
		"These Shields make him invunerable to all attacks, you'll need to wait for him to lift them, to attack him!"
		""
		"He has 1200 &4Hearts&r and has 2 attacks: one where he lifts in the air and throws Blaze Rods all around him, and the other where he spins his Shields"
		""
		"On death he will drop the &bBurning Ashes&r."
	]
	quest.0205615026CD000D.title: "&bIgnited Revenant&r"
	quest.028F8C54A65F93C9.quest_desc: [
		"The &eKhopesh&r is the Weapon and Drop of &eKoboletons&r."
		""
		"It does the same damage as an Iron Sword and can't be Enchanted or Repaired."
	]
	quest.028F8C54A65F93C9.title: "&eKhopesh"
	quest.02C334609FDAB091.quest_desc: [
		"The &bIncinerator&r can be used just like a normal Sword and Enchanted like one!"
		""
		"But when Holding Right Click it does something no normal Sword does. When you Hold and let go of Right Click for a few seconds, massive flames will strike out of the ground in the direction you are looking at, then they will explode."
	]
	quest.02C334609FDAB091.title: "&bThe Incinerator"
	quest.030699A548989DF0.title: "&l&9Twilight Forest Bounty:&r&e Spider"
	quest.0337A39115C9D9F1.quest_desc: ["Found in the &bAurora Palace&r, the &3Ice Sword&r will give enemies &bFrosted&r for 10 seconds when damaged."]
	quest.0337A39115C9D9F1.title: "&3Ice Sword"
	quest.03A3D3B7B8D11D3B.quest_subtitle: "Bring back a prehistoric predator!"
	quest.03A3D3B7B8D11D3B.title: "The Relic Claw"
	quest.044762E51D47F21A.quest_desc: [
		"&9Reinforced Echo Shard&r is a Crafted Item that requires a few Items."
		""
		"First, and easiest to obtain are &7Phantom Membrane&r! &7Phantoms&r will spawn after the Player hasn't slept in a few days. The more restless nights, the more &7Phantoms&r!"
		""
		"Second, is the &9Echo Shard&r. These can be found in quite a few ways but easiest is Looting in &6Ancient Cities&r."
		""
		"The last is the &9Warden Carapaces&r. These are Drops from the &9&lWarden&r on death. Don't worry he usually drops more than one!"
	]
	quest.044762E51D47F21A.title: "&9Reinforced Echo Shard"
	quest.048AA5DD8BFB083A.quest_subtitle: "Raises the holder's Sp. Atk when using a sound-based move."
	quest.04B7CF5E0AB3FD50.quest_desc: [
		"The &4Laser Gatling&r is a weapon you can make from &4Witherite&r."
		""
		"By using Redstone in your inventory, you can shoot Lasers which start fires and do 3 and a half &4Hearts&r of damage. "
		""
		"It shoots 50 Lasers per 1 redstone which I think is a good deal."
	]
	quest.04B7CF5E0AB3FD50.title: "&4Laser Gatling"
	quest.04DC26E9A0C1F48E.quest_desc: [
		"You ever wish you, yourself can use the &9&lWardens&r &bSonic Blast&r?"
		""
		"Well with the &bSonorous Staff&r you can! Just simply Hold Right Click to charge it up, then release to send a &bSonic Blast&r."
		""
		"There is a slight cooldown to it and it does have Durability, so use with risk!"
		""
		"To Craft one you'll need a &9Heart of the Deep&r from the &9&lWarden&r, 2 &3Soul Crystals&r from the &3&lStalker&r, and 2 &3Sculk Bones &ffrom &3Shattereds&r."
	]
	quest.04DC26E9A0C1F48E.title: "&bSonorous Staff"
	quest.05E887807DF3EAEC.quest_desc: [
		"Combine an &cInfernal Forge&r with a &dVoid Core&r to make the &dVoid &cForge&r!"
		""
		"It is still a Pickaxe, with same Mining Tier and Speed. "
		""
		"Just now we can Right Click with it, on the ground to summon &dVoid Runes&r in a fan shape, to hurt all Mobs with it."
		""
		"They really don't focus much on the Pickaxe part do they?"
	]
	quest.05E887807DF3EAEC.title: "&dVoid &cForge"
	quest.068415A8CAEEAFC3.quest_desc: ["More Options"]
	quest.068415A8CAEEAFC3.title: "&eAdvanced Jukebox Upgrade"
	quest.06A166A7F54D9150.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the holder's Accuracy."
	quest.06B7F9591678F57E.title: "&l&cNether Bounty:&r&e Blazes"
	quest.0759CA52EECF3B49.quest_desc: ["The &6Mechanical Plough&r will plough through anything in its way! Well, that it can move atleast. \\n\\nBlocks with weak connections will immediately break when the &6Plough&r hits them. Blocks like Torches, Buttons, and Vines. \\n\\nWhen used above Dirt or Grass, it will make Farmland! Perfect for Mega-Farms! \\n\\nYou can also use the &6Plough&r to move Mobs without killing them. Well the &6Plough&r won't kill them, whatever they hit might."]
	quest.0759CA52EECF3B49.title: "&6Mechanical Plough"
	quest.075CD7715AC7DBFB.quest_desc: [
		"Using the &cScepter of Life Draining&r, you can drain the life of your enemies!"
		""
		"To recharge the scepter, combine it with &cFermented Spider Eyes&r in a crafting grid."
	]
	quest.075CD7715AC7DBFB.quest_subtitle: "Drains Life"
	quest.075CD7715AC7DBFB.title: "&cScepter of Life Draining"
	quest.076C22B984F26F67.quest_desc: [
		"&5&lThe Leviathan&r is the reason people fear the Ocean."
		""
		"She has 30,000 &4Hearts&r, sharp teeth, and strong tentacles and is invincible outside of &9Water&r."
		""
		"She has a huge array of powers she will use against you. She can summon underwater &5Mines&r, shoot a Godzilla like &5Atomic Beam&r, and even just chomp on you."
		""
		"She can use her tentacles to break open a &5Water Vortex&r which will suck in all Entities nearby as bait for her. She can also summon &5Lasers&r from &5vortexs&r on the Ocean floor which will shoot upward. "
		""
		"Once you bring her beneath half &4Health&r she will become enraged! When enraged she will use her &5Lasers&r much more than before."
	]
	quest.076C22B984F26F67.title: "&5&lThe Leviathan&r"
	quest.078C5B50CDC174CB.quest_desc: ["&aMechanical Bearings&r are the most simple forms of &aContraption&r movement. \\n\\nWhen given &dRotational Power&r from their bottom, they will rotate any Blocks above at the same Speed and Direction. \\nBlocks will automatically be &aGlued&r to the &aMechanical Bearing&r, but any other Blocks will need to be &aGlued&r to that Block to move as well! \\n\\nIf you use a &aMechanical Bearing&r within a &aContraption&r itself, it will try and keep the Block attached still instead of Rotating."]
	quest.078C5B50CDC174CB.title: "&aMechanical Bearing"
	quest.07922AC8EDF987D2.quest_desc: ["Upgrade your &7Cloggrum Battleaxe&r to make the greatest weapon &2&lUndergarden&r can give!"]
	quest.07922AC8EDF987D2.title: "Ultimate Weapon!"
	quest.07AFC13EB2EA5EDE.quest_desc: [
		"With Magic Beans and Uberous Soil, you'll want to look for a large cloud in the highland biomes."
		""
		"Plant the magic beans in the soil to grow a beanstalk all the way up. Here, you'll find the Giants."
		""
		"You'll need to kill the Miner Giant and get their pickaxe to continue on."
	]
	quest.07C7CA9CEBD98A17.quest_desc: [
		"&9Hippocamtus&r are powerful Sea Horse warriors who guard &9Acropolis&r."
		""
		"They wear lots of Armor and hold a Spear and Shield. "
		""
		"They have 85 &4Hearts&r and 18 Armor Points."
		""
		"Their Shield will protect from Damage and their Spear will be used to Kill you. They can swing, stab, and even do a special move on you. This move will lock you into place where the &9Hippocamtus&r will repeatedly stab you."
		""
		"Like the &9Cindaria&r, these will Drop &9Lacrima&r."
	]
	quest.07C7CA9CEBD98A17.title: "&9Hippocamtus"
	quest.07D0F0D895D28D86.quest_desc: [
		"Stand before the &b&lValkyrie Queen&r&f, the relentless guardian of the &7&lSilver Dungeon&r&f."
		""
		"She has &c&l500 health&r&f and can fly.  "
		""
		"Prove your worth by defeating her and claim your &7&lSilver Key&r&f, &a&l4 levels of experience&r&f, and &6&l1 Golden Sword&r&f as proof of your victory. "
	]
	quest.07D0F0D895D28D86.quest_subtitle: "&f&lDefeat the &b&lValkyrie Queen&r&f&l in the &7&lSilver Dungeon&r&f&l"
	quest.07D0F0D895D28D86.title: "&7&lQuest: Defeat the Silver Boss"
	quest.081BE8D0103B8D21.title: "&l&9Overworld Bounty:&r&e Witches"
	quest.087F6C09CB5B2D1A.quest_desc: ["&bSmart Fluid Pipes&r will give us Filtering for &bFluid Pipes&r. \\n\\nWhen put on the Machine that the &bPipes&r are extracting from, it can be set to only take out the one &bFluid&r. This is set by adding a Bucket full of that &bLiquid&r in the Filter Slot. \\n\\nYou can place the &bSmart Fluid Pipe&r later in the &bPipe system&r to only send that certain &bFluid&r through the &bPipes&r after it. \\n\\nThis is helpful for mass sorting a bunch of &bFluid Tanks&r!"]
	quest.087F6C09CB5B2D1A.title: "&bSmart Fluid Pipe"
	quest.08A80DAD6F3D77BB.quest_subtitle: "Prevents the holder from being hit by Ground-type moves. Breaks if hit by another type of damaging move."
	quest.08B660E2383F2E17.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Cursed Bow&r works similar to a Bow with the Multishot Enchantment!"
		""
		"With normal Arrows, it will shoot 3 at a time! With special Arrows it will only shoot 2. "
	]
	quest.08B660E2383F2E17.title: "&3Cursed Bow"
	quest.093F798E6331F464.quest_desc: [
		"With our Wooden Pickaxe, stone shouldn't be a problem to break!"
		""
		"&3Cobblestone&r unlocks the next part of progression by allowing you to craft a Furnace to smelt our ores."
		""
		"You'll also want to upgrade your pickaxe to stone to mine better ores like &bIron&r!"
	]
	quest.093F798E6331F464.title: "Stone Age"
	quest.09568B75885EE990.quest_subtitle: "Switches out the holder if any stats are lowered. Consumed after use."
	quest.098FD8DB679C1A86.quest_desc: ["Small Yetis and Winter Wolves drop Arctic Fur, which can be used to make &6Arctic Armor&r."]
	quest.098FD8DB679C1A86.quest_subtitle: "It's Dyable!"
	quest.098FD8DB679C1A86.title: "&6Arctic Armor"
	quest.09936F8FCEA72C5C.quest_desc: [
		"The &aCart Assembler&r can be placed on tracks. Anything you build on top of it will be picked up by a &7Minecart&r if the &aAssembler&r has a &4Redstone signal&r."
		""
		"The Blocks must be &aGlued&r together and any Blocks requiring &dRotational Power&r will automatically be working."
		""
		"To \"unmount\" the Blocks from the &7Minecart&r, simply turn off the &4Redstone signal&r and let the &7Minecart&r ride through."
	]
	quest.09936F8FCEA72C5C.title: "&aCart Assembler"
	quest.09E34E1F9C751458.quest_desc: ["The &dVertical Gearbox&r is just like the normal &dGearbox&r if someone rotated it. \\n\\nIt has 4 internal &8Shafts&r just this time instead of the Cardinal Directions, they are (from where you place it) Front, Back, Up, and Down. \\n\\nAlso like the normal &dGearbox&r, it will keep the Speed and Stress Units from the original &8Shaft&r!"]
	quest.09E34E1F9C751458.title: "&dVertical Gearbox"
	quest.09E8D606123A1D43.quest_desc: [
		"The Chitin Claw is a Drop from the Clawdian."
		""
		"When worn you will get increased Block Reach and Entity Reach. So you can place Blocks farther and smack Mobs farther as well!"
	]
	quest.09E8D606123A1D43.title: "&9Chitin Claw"
	quest.0A126BE271E8D573.quest_desc: [
		"The &3&lMaledictus&r can be brought back from Valhalla or whatever the Norse version of Hell is, by Right Clicking the &3Cursed Tombstone&r."
		""
		"He has 50,400 &4Hearts&r and massive Wings."
		""
		"He will swing at you with his 2 &3Annihilators&r and can even ground pound you with them, making a Shockwave of course!"
		""
		"His Wings allow him to manevure and do many more attacks. He can charge at you, breaking all Blocks in his way or even dodge attacks!"
		""
		"He can fly into the air and from there can either shoot at you with his &3Cursed Bow&r or drop down with his &3Soul Render&r. The &3Cursed Bow&r will shoot 4 Arrows at you. With his &3Soul Render&r he will bring a shower of &3Phantom Halberds&r down on you."
	]
	quest.0A126BE271E8D573.title: "&3&lMaledictus"
	quest.0A2D54A5D365F0AA.quest_subtitle: "Revive an ancient plant Pokémon!"
	quest.0A2D54A5D365F0AA.title: "Roots of the Past"
	quest.0A3E99A157BC29D7.quest_desc: ["In the &cNether&r, you'll run into &6Ancient Debris&r. This can be smelted down into Scraps that can be combined with Gold to create &6Netherite Ingots&r, which is an endgame metal used to craft some of the strongest tools and armor in the game."]
	quest.0A3E99A157BC29D7.title: "&dAncient Metals"
	quest.0A4962728C98DAD9.quest_desc: ["&eItem Vaults&r, while not new, will be used a ton in the new Update! \\n\\n&eItem Vaults&r will act like Chests, just we can't put &eItems&r in or out as easily as Chests... \\n\\nIn order to move &eItems&r we'll need to use &eFunnels&r! Attach them to the &eVaults &fto send &eItems&r in and out. Preferably &eBrass Funnels&r for more &eItem&r Filtering. \\n\\nEach &eVault&r has a ton of storage but we can also place them next to each other to combine their Inventories. \\n\\nWe can place them in 1x1, 2x2, or 3x3 and their length can be up to 3 times their width! So the biggest we can have is 3x3x9."]
	quest.0A4962728C98DAD9.title: "&eItem Vaults"
	quest.0A9004B18A1DC59D.quest_desc: ["Evolve six of your Pokémon to unlock their hidden potential and boost your team's strength. Embrace the transformative power of evolution and discover new abilities and stats that will elevate your battle strategy."]
	quest.0A9004B18A1DC59D.quest_subtitle: "Enhance Your Team"
	quest.0A9004B18A1DC59D.title: "6 Evolutions Challenge"
	quest.0AA2D3DEECFD22EF.quest_desc: ["Adds a filter for items being pumped in or out of the Backpack."]
	quest.0B4CDE25CAECA1B3.quest_desc: [
		"&bGwiblings&r are friendly fish in the Seas."
		""
		"They are smaller than &bGwibs&r and act like Vanilla Fish!"
	]
	quest.0B4CDE25CAECA1B3.title: "&bGwibling&r"
	quest.0B611C9BC3314E30.quest_desc: ["Just combine an &bIgnitium Chestplate&r with an Elytra... that simple!"]
	quest.0B611C9BC3314E30.title: "&bIgnitium Elytra Chestplate"
	quest.0B9BDC6F0BAE1C1C.quest_desc: [
		"You can combine a Netherite Upgrade Template, a Netherite Helmet, and a &cMonstrous Horn&r to make the &cMonstrous Helm&r."
		""
		"It has the same stats but when you're at half health it'll Knockback everything close to you and increase defense stats."
	]
	quest.0B9BDC6F0BAE1C1C.title: "&cMonstrous Helm"
	quest.0C7A448E772D2441.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.0C7A448E772D2441.title: "&eAdvanced Tool Swapper Upgrade"
	quest.0C82374C9DFAFB9B.quest_desc: [
		"&cGloomslate&r replaces &3Sculk Stone&r in the &cOvercast Columns&r."
		""
		"It works just like &3Sculk Stone&r, just more Brown."
	]
	quest.0C82374C9DFAFB9B.title: "&cGloomslate"
	quest.0CA4DA51226FE25B.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Hydra&r is the infamous multi-headed beast from Greek Mythology."
		""
		"Ranged attacks aren't as effective, meaning you'll need to get up close and personal."
		""
		"Once defeated, you'll be able to find the next boss in the &2Dark Forest&r."
	]
	quest.0CA4DA51226FE25B.quest_subtitle: "The Firey Swamp"
	quest.0CA4DA51226FE25B.title: "&9Hydra Slayer"
	quest.0CB86F0766F9CFFE.quest_desc: [
		"&bIce Lilies&r are Plants that grow on the &9Water Ponds&r within the &bBlooming Caverns&r"
		""
		"There's 2 parts to the Plant, the &bLily&r and the &bIce Flower&r. The &bLily Pad&r is what floats on &9Water&r and allows you to walk on it. The &bIce Flower&r lies on top of the &bLily Pad&r and looks pretty!"
		""
		"You'll need Shears."
	]
	quest.0CB86F0766F9CFFE.title: "&bIce Lilies"
	quest.0CEE0A3F61F5B8C3.quest_desc: ["The &5Eye of Abyss&r will take you to the &5Sunken City&r to fight the &5&lLeviathan&r."]
	quest.0CEE0A3F61F5B8C3.title: "&5Eye of Abyss&r"
	quest.0CF69DBA9573A7B3.quest_desc: [
		"The Schematic Table will read and write structures to/from your schematics."
		""
		"You can use it to copy buildings or to share them with others!"
	]
	quest.0D6CE8121E28B890.quest_desc: ["Adds a Smoker GUI to the Backpack."]
	quest.0D85CFF537BB89CE.quest_desc: [
		"With 2 &9Essence of the Storm&r and 3 &9Lacrima&r we can make &9Astrape&r."
		""
		"&9Astrape&r is a combination of the Weapons used by the &9Hippocamtus&r and &9Cindaria&r."
		""
		"It can stab like a Trident, just with more Damage and Range. Plus you can Hold Right Click to send &9Lightning Spears&r, just like &9Cindaria&r!"
		""
		"The &9Lightning Spears&r still bounce off Walls! Just now with a Cooldown..."
	]
	quest.0D85CFF537BB89CE.title: "&9Astrape"
	quest.0DA99C2ADAF5EA8A.quest_desc: ["Elegant and calm, Erika runs a perfume shop and teaches flower arrangement — but don't let her grace fool you, her Grass-types pack a punch."]
	quest.0DA99C2ADAF5EA8A.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 44"
	quest.0DA99C2ADAF5EA8A.title: "Erika"
	quest.0DBD6ECBB791C481.quest_subtitle: "Prevents the holder's ability from being changed or suppressed."
	quest.0DCEE9EBB77CFF6C.quest_desc: [
		"Press (default: &cI&r) to open the skill tree."
		""
		"There are 3 trees (Combat, Mining, Chopping wood). The Combat tree starts with 3 different paths to choose Which divide into 6 Paths. After choosing one path, the others will be blocked."
		""
		""
		"&n&lThe Combat paths are: &r&r"
		""
		"- &4Melee&r [Melee dmg, Hp, Att speed, Healing]."
		""
		"- &6Ranged&r [Ranged dmg, Jump boost, Att speed, Stamina]."
		""
		"- &2Physical Strength&r [Luck, Sprinting speed, Jump boost, Hp]."
		""
		"The 6 other paths are combinations of the 3 previous ones."
		""
		""
		"&n&lThe Mining tree contains: &r&r"
		""
		"- Mining speed"
		"- Pickaxe speed"
		"- Anvil repair cost"
		"- Fortune "
		""
		""
		"&n&lThe Wood chopping tree contains:&r&r "
		""
		"- Axe speed"
		"- Mining speed"
		"- Knockback  "
		""
		""
		"&n&lHow to play? Earn skill xp by:&r&r"
		""
		"- Killing mobs - (for Combat tree)"
		"- Mining ores - (for Mining tree)"
		"- Chopping wood - (for Wood chopping tree)"
		""
		"With enough xp you will get a skill point to spend on a skill. "
	]
	quest.0DCEE9EBB77CFF6C.quest_subtitle: "choose your own path"
	quest.0DEC2D839F26A27E.quest_subtitle: "Burns the holder."
	quest.0EDAF6EAA0A47A94.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 56"
	quest.0EDAF6EAA0A47A94.title: "Boss Giovanni"
	quest.0EDEEF6E3633F339.quest_subtitle: "When the holder successfully inflicts damage, the target may also flinch."
	quest.0F0D13C7F365C69B.quest_desc: [
		"Another structure to cover the barreness of &5The End&r, the &dRuined Citadel&r."
		""
		"The &dRuined Citadel&r is a Palace of &5Obsidian&r, Endstone, and &dPurpur&r."
		""
		"In the palace you'll find Chests, Shulker Boxes, Shulkers, and even the unique &dVoid Stone&r!"
		""
		"Just be careful of the afformentioned Shulkers, &dEndermaptera&r, and &dEnder Golems&r."
	]
	quest.0F0D13C7F365C69B.title: "&dRuined Citadel&r: Home of the &d&lEnder Guardian&r"
	quest.0F16498769DFB3B0.quest_desc: ["What will we need all that &8Andesite&r for? We'll need &8Andesite Alloys&r! \\n\\n&8Andesite Alloys&r are made by combining 2 &8Andesite&r with either 2 &7Iron Nuggets&r or 2 &7Zinc Nuggets&r. \\n\\n&8Andesite Alloys&r don't do much on their own, rather they are the Crafting Ingrediant for almost all Machines and Items. So yeah, we'll need a few."]
	quest.0F16498769DFB3B0.title: "&8Andesite Alloys"
	quest.0F8FF5B3FE587D40.quest_subtitle: "Revive a Pokémon lost to the waves!"
	quest.0F8FF5B3FE587D40.title: "The Deep-Sea Guardian"
	quest.0FCC0A420BF84BFF.quest_subtitle: "Raises the holder's Attack by one stage when hit by a damaging Electric-type move."
	quest.0FCED4C94B9840CA.quest_desc: [
		"&9Angler Fish&r spawn in &9Water Ponds&r within &bBlooming Caverns&r."
		""
		"They act like normal Fish, obviously needing &9Water&r to breathe."
		""
		"They have 3 &4Hearts&r and will attack you when you are near. "
		""
		"They don't drop anything on death."
	]
	quest.0FCED4C94B9840CA.title: "&9Angler Fish"
	quest.106748D789E788CD.quest_desc: [
		"This tutorial will walk you through some basic features. Rest assured, it won't take too long!"
		""
		"To begin, click the checkmark below the word \"Tasks,\" and then claim your quest reward. New quests will start to appear!"
		""
		"If new quests don't appear, try relaunching your world."
	]
	quest.106748D789E788CD.quest_subtitle: "To start the tutorial, click on this quest and read the description."
	quest.1070FE015DFD410C.quest_desc: [
		"I guess the &3Draugrs&r really wanted to keep the &3Cursed Tombstone&r safe because they Locked it! "
		""
		"The &3Door of Seal&r, yeah a really creative name, blocks us from getting to it. We'll need a &3Strange Key&r to open it."
		""
		"Again, they really want it locked up because they gave the &3Strange Key&r to the &3Aptrgangr&r. Only the toughest guys in the &3Frosted Prison&r who are still alive!"
	]
	quest.1070FE015DFD410C.quest_subtitle: "Unlocking access to the Maledictus"
	quest.1070FE015DFD410C.title: "&3Strange Key"
	quest.10789FAF11E94116.quest_desc: [
		"&3Sculk Snappers&r are tiny but angry Mobs!"
		""
		"I've seen them spawn in &9Deeplands &fand &cBlooming Caverns&r."
		""
		"They have 6 &4Hearts&r and will drop &3Soul Dust&r on Death."
	]
	quest.10789FAF11E94116.title: "&3Sculk Snapper"
	quest.108E4854F42B0D97.quest_subtitle: "Increases damage inflected by the holder's binding moves in between turns from 1/8 to 1/6 of target's HP."
	quest.10900FC0120025F0.quest_desc: [
		"&f&d&lZanite Gemstones&r&f are precious crystals found deep within the floating islands of the &b&lAether&r&f."
		""
		"&fThese beautiful purple gems grow stronger as their wearers’ tools and armor weaken, a curious magic of the skies."
		""
		"&fMine them from the Aether’s caverns and keep one in your inventory to begin harnessing the power of the clouds."
		""
		"&f&lTip"
		""
		"&f&d&lZanite&r&f is often found in caves and mountains, bring a pickaxe and explore the glowing depths."
	]
	quest.10900FC0120025F0.quest_subtitle: "&f&lHave a &d&lZanite Gemstone&r&f in your inventory"
	quest.10900FC0120025F0.title: "&7&lQuest: A Gem of the Skies"
	quest.10B25C0A0717D12F.quest_desc: [
		"&fThe &b&lPale Oak Tree&r&f is the heart of the Pale Garden. &a&lHarvest its wood&r&f to craft new blocks, planks, fences, and more, expanding your building possibilities."
		""
		"&fIts leaves drop &b&lPale Oak Saplings&r&f, which can be planted in a 2x3 formation to grow your own trees. &d&lCollect Pale Oak Logs&r&f and bring this eerie beauty to your home."
	]
	quest.10B25C0A0717D12F.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain &b&lPale Oak Logs&r&f&l from the &a&lPale Garden"
	quest.10B25C0A0717D12F.title: "&6&lQuest: Collect Pale Oak Logs"
	quest.10D50B0277AD0878.quest_subtitle: "If the holder is a Poison type, its HP is gradually restored throughout a battle. It damages any other type."
	quest.111DA3BA053A4F1B.quest_subtitle: "Extends the duration of sandstorms from 5 to 8 turns."
	quest.113FD1AA46E58642.quest_desc: [
		"Deep within the &6&lBronze Dungeon&r&f lies the &6&lSlider&r&f, a massive ancient guardian forged entirely from stone. "
		""
		"It has &c&l400 health&r&f and can only be damaged with a &7&lpickaxe&r&f, so come prepared. "
		""
		"Defeat this powerful foe to claim your &6&lBronze Key&r&f, &a&l4 levels of experience&r&f, and &7&l8 Carved Stone&r&f as proof of your victory."
	]
	quest.113FD1AA46E58642.quest_subtitle: "&f&lDefeat the &6&lSlider&f, the boss of the &6&lBronze Dungeon&f"
	quest.113FD1AA46E58642.title: "&7&lQuest: The First Challenge, The Bronze Dungeon!"
	quest.1148EFA0026B8B47.quest_desc: [
		"Rotten Blisterberries can't be thrown but when made into Blisterbombs they can be!"
		""
		"You can even go farther and make Boomgourds which will act like TNT that throws Blisterberries everywhere."
	]
	quest.1148EFA0026B8B47.title: "Explosives!!!"
	quest.11521D1F4128D864.quest_desc: [
		"&fThrough mastery of the &e&lGold Dungeons&r&f and the discovery of the &7&lStratus Smithing Template&r&f, you can ascend beyond Gravitite and forge armor worthy of the heavens themselves."
		""
		"&fUpgrade your &d&lGravitite Armor&r&f or uncover this divine set through your conquests, become one with the skies, clad in the power of the &7&lStratus&r&f."
	]
	quest.11521D1F4128D864.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain a full set of &7&lStratus Armor&r&f"
	quest.11521D1F4128D864.title: "&7&lQuest: Skyforged Ascension"
	quest.120F617060EE90D0.quest_desc: ["The PC can be interacted with to access the Pokémon Storage System. This system allows players to withdraw or deposit Pokémon in Boxes, with any caught Pokémon being transferred automatically to the Pokémon Storage System if the player currently has a full party."]
	quest.120F617060EE90D0.quest_subtitle: "Build A PC"
	quest.1220680082B454E7.quest_desc: [
		"In &dThe End&r, you'll find the final boss of Vanilla Minecraft: The &5Ender Dragon&r."
		""
		"At the top of each pillar of Obsidian, you'll find an End Crystal that heals the Dragon. Make sure to take those out first! They also deal a lot of damage when they explode, so make sure to create some distance!"
		""
		"Once defeated, a &dDragon Egg&r spawns at the top of the Exit Portal. This cannot be mined like normal blocks, but is affected by gravity."
	]
	quest.1220680082B454E7.title: "&5The End"
	quest.12274935C3D20C74.quest_desc: ["There is tons of different Building Blocks you can use, lots of the &6&lCreate&r Casings look clean and Concretes can help give a more slick look. \\n\\nYou can also use Doors and Trapdoors within the &5Train&r which can also be used when the &5Train&r is moving. \\n\\nWhat about making it look pretty? Well Stairs, Slabs, and Trapdoors help give Shape to it as well as the Flywheel or &dCogs&r give nice round edges. \\n\\nHeck you can even put a Campfire on it to make a Steam Engine!"]
	quest.12274935C3D20C74.title: "Decorating your &5Train&r"
	quest.127F9EAC7C305BF5.quest_desc: ["Trust me when I say, you'll need a &6Wrench&r! \\n\\nThe &6Wrench&r is the perfect Swiss Army Knife like Tool for &6&lCreate&r. You can rotate Blocks, break them, set their configs, what can't you do with it! \\n\\nTo break Blocks just Shift Right Click any &6&lCreate&r Block and it'll break them. \\n\\nTo Rotate a Block just normal Right Click them with the &6Wrench&r. Unfortunately this doesn't give us free &dRotational Power&r, but it is still useful for slip ups! \\n\\nIt will also be useful for setting up &aContraptions&r, but that is for later."]
	quest.127F9EAC7C305BF5.title: "&6Wrench"
	quest.129F0A5B901542A5.quest_subtitle: "Restore an ancient protector!"
	quest.129F0A5B901542A5.title: "The Shield of Time"
	quest.12D2E4DB593E6122.quest_subtitle: "Allows the holder to mirror an opponent's stat increases to boost it's own stats. Consumed after use."
	quest.12D8CD7EAAC2B7DB.quest_desc: [
		"&bFroststeel&r Armor is slightly worse than Diamond Armor but it also gives big Knockback Resistance."
		""
		"It also gives Speed debuff though"
	]
	quest.12D8CD7EAAC2B7DB.title: "&bFroststeel&r Armor"
	quest.133CA315A1443A49.quest_desc: ["&bMechanical Pumps&r will use Rotational Power to move &bFluids&r through &bPipes&r. \\n\\nFirst, replace a &bPipe&r with the &bMechanical Pump&r. Then, make sure it is facing the right way you want &bFluids&r to be moved. The Arrows next to the internal &6Cog&r will tell which direction it will move, you can change that with a Wrench. \\n\\nThen, feed it &dRotational Power&r with a &6Cog&r near it. The direction does not change anything, but the Speed will effect how quickly &bFluids&r are moved. \\n\\n&bMechanical Pumps&r will also be needed for other Machines like the &bHose Pulley&r!"]
	quest.133CA315A1443A49.title: "&bMechanical Pump"
	quest.135D1FAF4F3CBB61.quest_desc: [
		"&4The Ancient Factory&r lies deep underground in the &2Overworld&r."
		""
		"You'll find many Redstone Items like Levers, Powered Rails, and EMPs... I wonder if those will be useful soon? "
		""
		"You'll also find some Redstone Machines trying to kill you! Like the &4Watchers &fand &4Prowlers&r!"
		""
		"Even with the danger there's still tons of Loot and Blocks you can steal from here, especially Redstone."
	]
	quest.135D1FAF4F3CBB61.title: "&4Ancient Factory&r: Home of &4&lThe Harbinger&r"
	quest.13ABF11D9A6C3935.quest_desc: [
		"Cave Spider - Spawn in Mineshafts. "
		""
		"Hedge Spider - Spawn in Twilight Forest Hedge Maze."
		""
		"King Spider - Spawn in Twilight Forest Dark Forests."
		""
		"Swarm Spider - Spawn in Twilight Forest Hollow Hiils, Leaf Dungeons, and Hedge Maze."
	]
	quest.13ABF11D9A6C3935.title: "Spider Variants"
	quest.13AEBC331F29BC3D.quest_desc: ["&eItem Logistics&r is important to &6&lCreate&r. &6Millstones&r need &eItems&f, &6Deployers &fneed &eItems&f, &6Mechanical Mixers&f need &eItems&r, and so on. \\n\\nNow how does &6&lCreate&r want us to move &eItems&r? With &eBelts&r! \\n\\n&eBelts&r can be attached to two &8Shafts&r to connect and move with them. If the first &8Shaft&r is moving &e&oClockwise&r, the second will move same Speed and Direction. \\n\\nSame with the &eBelts&r that are placed on those &8Shafts&r, they will move same Speed and Direction as the &8Shafts&r they are placed between. \\n\\nWith placing &8Belts&r they can be placed perfectly Horizontal, Vertical, or diagonal at 45% angles. \\n\\nOnce placed and move, any &eItems&r or Entities will be moved with the &eBelt&r. Entities can walk off the &eBelts&r though so careful with that. Thankfully &eItems&r can't walk off or even despawn when on it! \\n\\nThe &eItems&r will then be taken to wherever the &eBelt&r goes. If it abruptly ends, the &eItems&r will just be Dropped. If it goes to a &eDepot&r, the &eItem&r will be placed in a &eDepot&r. If it goes below a &6Machine&r, the&6 Machine&r will use it. \\n\\nIf you want to take &eItems &foff the &eBelt&r you can just Right Click it!"]
	quest.13AEBC331F29BC3D.title: "&e&lItem Logistics"
	quest.13B2E058B06DCD16.quest_desc: [
		"Using the &cFiery Blood&r from the Hydra, you can make a couple of tools."
		""
		"The Fiery Sword comes with Fire Aspect II."
		""
		"The Fiery Pickaxe comes with auto-smelt."
	]
	quest.13B2E058B06DCD16.title: "&cFiery Tools"
	quest.148BE142DCD4072B.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Frosted Prison&r is a massive Castle like structure on top and within the Snowy Mountains."
		""
		"Within you will find dozens of cells, armories, and a great room which the &3Cursed Tombstone&r lies."
		""
		"You can find plenty of Chests full of Loot, including Black Steel. There's Decorated Pots everywhere for the taking!"
		""
		"And of course Mobs enemies to stand in your way: &3Draugrs&r and &3Aptrgangr&r."
	]
	quest.148BE142DCD4072B.title: "&3Frosted Prison&r: Home of the &3&lMaledictus"
	quest.15482DAFABF6F833.quest_desc: [
		"&fPause your current series and enter &dFreeroam Mode&f.  "
		"In this mode, &ayour Pokémon can freely reach Level 100&f, with no level cap restrictions.  "
		""
		"&cImportant:&f Freeroam temporarily suspends your current series  "
		"progression. While in Freeroam, you will not advance in any storyline or unlock new milestones.  "
		""
		"You can return to your previous series at any time by:  "
		""
		"&fClicking the dedicated button in the Trainers section."
	]
	quest.15482DAFABF6F833.title: "&dFreeroam Mode"
	quest.15AE0323F244177F.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Ender Bow&r is found rarely in the &bAurora Palace&r."
		""
		"When an enemy is hit with an arrow from this bow, you will swap places with them. Be careful shooting things out of the sky!"
	]
	quest.15AE0323F244177F.title: "&3Ender Bow"
	quest.15B9B1001D0EA1A1.quest_desc: [
		"Legends tell of the &6&lHammer of Kingbdogz&r&f, a powerful relic once wielded by the ancient ruler of the &b&lAether&r&f."
		""
		"This mighty weapon can only be earned as a reward in the &6&lBronze Dungeon&r&f after defeating the &6&lSlider&r&f, so be ready for a real fight."
		""
		"Claim it as your own and wield the power of the Aether’s first champion."
	]
	quest.15B9B1001D0EA1A1.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain the &6&lHammer of Kingbdogz&r&f&l from the &6&lBronze Dungeon&r&f&l"
	quest.15B9B1001D0EA1A1.title: "&7&lQuest: Relic of the Sky King"
	quest.15FEB3C99967B417.quest_desc: [
		"Similar to Iron Tools just all of these slow down whoever is hit by them."
		""
		"Well besides the Hoe"
	]
	quest.15FEB3C99967B417.title: "&bFroststeel&r Tools"
	quest.16216F5BC7A8E70B.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's physical moves."
	quest.166CA51A7BD66AA7.quest_desc: [
		"Find the &cQ&6u&ee&2s&3t&9i&5n&cg &6R&ea&2m&r, for it bestows wealth to those who give it &cR&6a&ei&2n&3b&9o&5w &6W&eo&2o&3l&r (16 colors)."
		""
		"Hint: There's a Dispenser above your head in the ruins where the Ram is. It might prove useful."
	]
	quest.166CA51A7BD66AA7.quest_subtitle: "Quests?"
	quest.166CA51A7BD66AA7.title: "&cR&6a&em&2i&3f&9i&5c&ca&6t&ei&2o&3n"
	quest.167D2F812694ECF3.quest_desc: ["Fossils are ancient Pokémon remains buried deep within the world. Use a brush on Suspicious Sand or Suspicious Gravel in fossil structures to uncover them!"]
	quest.167D2F812694ECF3.quest_subtitle: "Uncover the past hidden in sand and gravel!"
	quest.167D2F812694ECF3.title: "Buried Secrets"
	quest.16A2A2F46575CC2A.quest_desc: ["&2Phantom Armor&r has a chance of being found in &2Knight Phantom&r chests."]
	quest.16A2A2F46575CC2A.title: "&2Phantom Armor"
	quest.16B0C1F7B951C19D.quest_desc: ["Now we have our &ePackager&r we can now have &ePackages&r! \\n\\nThere is 4 varients but that doesn't change anything with them besides apperance. It is entirely random which one you get. \\n\\n&ePackages&r are &eItems&r and when Placed on the Ground will become Entities. You can Right Click them after they were Placed to Pick them up, or Break them to get the &eItems&r out. You can also move them like any other Entity! \\n\\n&ePackages&r can also be used to interact with other &6Machines&r. Like being placed on &8Chain Conveyors&f or &eBelts&r!"]
	quest.16B0C1F7B951C19D.title: "&eCardboard Packages"
	quest.1712C3B3CF158843.quest_desc: ["To make the &ePrecision Mechanism&r we'll need 3 &6Deployers&r, 3 &eDepots&f/&eBelts&r, 1 &eGold Plate&r, 5 Cogs, 5 Large Cogwheels, and 5 &7Iron Nuggets&r, as well as luck! \\n\\nTake your &eGold Plate&r (which can be made from Pressing a Gold Ingot) and place it beneath each of the Deployers in order. \\n\\nThe first will need a Cog, the second will need a Large Cog, and the third will need an Iron Nugget. \\n\\nThen, once it has been processed through all 3 of them, repeat it! And do it 5 times in a row. \\n\\nAt the end, there is only an 80% chance it will actually make it. The other 20% will see all your work going POOF!"]
	quest.1712C3B3CF158843.title: "&ePrecision Mechanism"
	quest.1718213AAF7DC34D.quest_desc: [
		"The &9&lWarden&r will drop quite a few Items but the &9Heart of the Deep&r is most important. "
		""
		"We can use the &9Heart of the Deep&r on a frame of &8Reinforced Deepslate&r to get our Portal to the &3&lOtherside&r. There can't be any Blocks blocking the Portal Frame or else it won't work."
		""
		"He also drops &9Warden Carapace&r and &9Echo Shards&r, both will be useful for Crafting other Items!"
	]
	quest.1718213AAF7DC34D.title: "&9Heart of the Deep"
	quest.177C22CE7237995F.quest_subtitle: "Extends the duration of harsh sunlight from 5 to 8 turns."
	quest.17B04BBA4196F123.quest_desc: [
		"The &e&lAncient Remnant&r is master of his domain, of &eSand&r."
		""
		"He has 3,600 &4Hearts&r and is aided with a &eWadjet&r and a &eKobolediator&r."
		""
		"He has a few moves and attacks! He can swing his bony tail at you, bite you, or he might stomp on the ground, producing Shockwaves."
		""
		"He can also summon &eSandstorms&r with a mighty ROAR and even drop &eSand Traps&r on your head."
		""
		"Another attack he may use to get closer to you is his charge. His charge will hurt you and your FPS as it destroys every Block in his path."
		""
		"He does have a weakness, the very thing that ressurected him! If you hit his &eNecklace&r he will be knocked down for a little bit, giving you the perfect chance to strike him down and return him to the grave!"
	]
	quest.17B04BBA4196F123.title: "&e&lAncient Remnant&r"
	quest.17CA5ADF297AB838.quest_desc: [
		"&fDeep within Pale Oaks lies the &c&lCreaking Heart&r&f, a \"living\" block that pulses at night. &a&lYou can craft one using Resin and &b&lPale Oak Logs&r&f, or find it naturally in the Pale Garden."
		""
		"&fWhen destroyed, it drops &b&lResin Clumps&r&f on which experience thrives. &d&lDiscover the Creaking Heart&r&f and feel its eerie rhythm."
	]
	quest.17CA5ADF297AB838.quest_subtitle: "&f&lFind or craft a &c&lCreaking Heart&r&f&l block"
	quest.17CA5ADF297AB838.title: "&6&lQuest: Find a Creaking Heart"
	quest.180309A0F29ACE9E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Forgottens&r are warriors that spawn within the Catacomb Structure."
		""
		"They wear Ancient Armor and hold Cloggrum Tools, all which can be dropped upon death. "
		""
		"They will also target and kill &cRot Mobs&r."
	]
	quest.180309A0F29ACE9E.title: "&7Forgotten&r"
	quest.180B7A40DD873119.quest_desc: [
		"Hidden deep within the &6&lBronze Dungeon&r&f rests a relic of divine craftsmanship: the &b&lValkyrie Lance&r&f. "
		""
		"This elegant yet deadly weapon is proof that you are ready for far greater trials ahead. "
		""
		"With it in hand, steel yourself… it is time to challenge the &7&lSilver Dungeon&r&f."
	]
	quest.180B7A40DD873119.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain the &b&lValkyrie Lance&r&f&l from the &6&lBronze Dungeon&r&f&l"
	quest.180B7A40DD873119.title: "&7&lQuest: The Valkyrie’s Challenge"
	quest.180CF25107BF83F2.quest_desc: ["Your fossil is now fully analyzed, and you’re one step closer to reviving a prehistoric Pokémon! The Restoration Tank is the final step in this incredible process."]
	quest.180CF25107BF83F2.quest_subtitle: "Bringing ancient Pokémon back to life!"
	quest.180CF25107BF83F2.title: "The Restoration Process"
	quest.18914FDF9CF9EEA8.quest_desc: ["&aClockwork Bearings&r will move based on the Time of Day when given &dRotational Power&r. \\n\\nThe Block in front of the &aClockwork Bearing&r will automatically &aGlue&r to it, but other Blocks can be &aGlued&r to that Block to join it! \\n\\nIf you want more Hands to your &aClock&r, add more Blocks in front of the first Block, but make sure these aren't &aGlued&r together. \\n\\nYou can change which Hands are which by Holding on the &aBearing&r to change whether the first Hand (closest Block) is the Hour or Minute Hand. "]
	quest.18914FDF9CF9EEA8.title: "&aClockwork Bearing"
	quest.18D9BF0C96A9007B.quest_subtitle: "Boosts Clamperl's Sp. Atk stat."
	quest.18FA7D1714C05034.quest_desc: [
		"At the bottom left of the inventory screen, you may have noticed a search bar."
		""
		"This is the &dJust Enough Items&r, or &dJEI&r, search bar."
		""
		"If you type \"Wood\", for example, the &dJEI &ritem list at the right of the screen will show all items with \"Wood\" in the name."
		""
		"Adding a @ at the start of the search query will show the items from a specific mod, for example @Cobblemon"
	]
	quest.18FA7D1714C05034.quest_subtitle: "Read my description!"
	quest.1936DA80AFEFE1B5.quest_subtitle: "At full HP, guarantees the holder survives a hit that would KO it, leaving it with 1 HP."
	quest.195754CBC2AC8084.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's moves, but causes recoil damage."
	quest.197537F2D0EB6A96.quest_desc: [
		"The &dGauntlet of &eMaelstorm&r is made with the &dGauntlet of Guard&r and &eSandstorm in a Bottle&r in a &4Mechanical Fusion Anvil&r."
		""
		"This one is unique from all Weapons I've seen from &4&lCataclysm&r."
		""
		"When you Hold Right Click, a &dVoid &eVortex&r will spawn where you are aiming."
		""
		"The &dVoid &eVortex&r will suck in all Entities nearby, then after a few seconds, it will close and explode! Dealing Damage to all near it."
	]
	quest.197537F2D0EB6A96.title: "&dGauntlet of &eMaelstorm"
	quest.19A6CB66421E9EEE.quest_subtitle: "Prevents the effects of traps set on the battlefield."
	quest.19DA0A92BAD9B62C.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have an Iron or better tier Pickaxe, you'll be able to mine &cRedstone&r. "
		""
		"Redstone starts your journey into many technical mods, like creating power or making fancy gadgets. "
		""
		"This is a resource you will want a lot of!"
	]
	quest.19DA0A92BAD9B62C.title: "&cRedstone&r"
	quest.1A118D1B422077D4.quest_desc: [
		"The &2Hyrda&r drops &cFiery Blood&r that can be used to craft &cFiery Armor&r."
		""
		"When wearing the full set, enemies that attack you will be set on fire for 10 seconds."
	]
	quest.1A118D1B422077D4.title: "&cFiery Armor"
	quest.1AC1AA4323A3A47C.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrade &7Cloggrum&r Tools with &aForgotten Ingots&r and a Smithing Template."
		""
		"These are the best Tools you can get, they come with Efficiency on them already just for &2&lUndergarden&r Blocks."
		""
		"And the Sword and Axe will deal more damage to all &2&lUndergarden&r Mobs but the &cRot Beast&r and &aForgotten Guardian&r!"
	]
	quest.1AC1AA4323A3A47C.title: "&aForgotten&r Tools"
	quest.1AC818C19FF447CB.quest_desc: [
		"Frostfields are one of the cold Biomes in the &2&lUndergarden&r. You can tell it is cold by the massive icesicles, Powdered Snow, and Frozen Deepturf!"
		""
		"Also here instead of the usual Depthrock underground you will find Shiverstone."
		""
		"Shiverstone acts more like Ice than real Stone. Well atleast when standing on it!"
	]
	quest.1AC818C19FF447CB.title: "Frostfields"
	quest.1B182A30604655E2.quest_desc: ["&cBlaze Burners&r are pretty easy to Craft, you'll just need some &7Iron Plates&r with a singular Block of &4Netherrack&r. \\n\\nThen you'll need to use a &oMysterious Conversion&r to make it less Empty! That is just Right Clicking a &cBlaze&r with your &cEmpty Blaze Burner&r. \\n\\nWhen we place him though, he seems a little small and... lukewarm... \\n\\nWe'll need to feed him! No, not Steak, &cBlazes&r don't like Steaks. He'll need either Furnace Fuels like Wood or Coal, or his favorite: the &cBlaze Cakes&r! \\n\\nThe Furnace Fuel will get them only a bit Heated, but the &cBlaze Cakes&r will make them &bSuper-Heated&r! Yes, &bSuper-Heated&r is hotter than &6Orange&r Hot. \\n\\nSome Recipes and &6Machines&r will need to be Heated, like &6Automated Brewing&r, &6Mixing&r, and the Steam Boiler will! "]
	quest.1B182A30604655E2.title: "&cBlaze Burner"
	quest.1B40AE95FD50CFB0.quest_desc: [
		"The &dEnder Golem&r keeps guard of the &dRuined Citadel&r, well multiple of them do."
		""
		"Technically you don't need to fight them to fight the &dEnder Guardian&r but you definitely should to get the &dVoid Core&r."
		""
		"The &dEnder Golem&r has 5250 &4Hearts&r and will regenerate them when left alone."
		""
		"He has a few attacks like being able to punch you and smashing the ground. When he smashing the ground, &dVoid Runes&r will spawn, hurting any Player or Mob that touches them."
	]
	quest.1B40AE95FD50CFB0.title: "&dEnder Golem&r"
	quest.1B5C6621158F1F28.quest_desc: [
		"&fTo tame your own &a&lMoa&r&f companion, you must first incubate a &b&lMoa Egg&r&f obtained from dungeons or adult moas."
		""
		"&fOnce hatched, the baby moa will occasionally get hungry, you will notice it when angry particles appear."
		""
		"&fFeed it &d&lAechor Petals&r&f three times to help it grow into an adult. When fully grown, you can saddle it and soar across the Aether skies."
	]
	quest.1B5C6621158F1F28.quest_subtitle: "&f&lIncubate a &b&lMoa Egg&r&f &luntil it hatches"
	quest.1B88DC71CFAE9D0B.quest_desc: ["&f&b&lHolystone&r is &f&b&lThe Aether’s&r counterpart to regular stone. Alongside &f&b&lAether Dirt&r, it is one of main blocks comprising &f&b&lThe Aether’s&r floating islands."]
	quest.1B88DC71CFAE9D0B.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain &b&lHolystone&r&f"
	quest.1B88DC71CFAE9D0B.title: "&7&lQuest: Obtain Holystone"
	quest.1B9FC5B83A9A8DE3.quest_desc: [
		"&cThe Soul BlackSmith&r resides in the Nether&r. Don't overlook it thinking it is a Bastion, it's much worse."
		""
		"You can find Gold, Blackstone, and Netherite here. "
		""
		"The only hostile Mobs that spawn here is the boss... the &c&lNetherite Monstrosity&r!"
	]
	quest.1B9FC5B83A9A8DE3.title: "&cSoul BlackSmith&f: Home of the &c&lNetherite Monstrosity&r"
	quest.1BA11428DF7541AD.quest_desc: ["Because the &eSequenced Gearshift&r uses much fancier &eItems&r it is clearly a much fancier &6Machine&r! \\n\\nJudging by how confusing its GUI is, I'd say so... Hopefully I can help make it less confusing! No promises though. \\n\\nLike the normal &dGearshift&r it will need a &4Redstone Signal&r to do whatever is designed. We'll need to configure its GUI to make a \"script\". \\n\\nFirst, is the Instructions, these are the actual tasks it will preform. Here it can turn its &8Shaft&r, effect a Pulley, wait, or just stop. It will need to stop at the end, it is inevitable. \\n\\nNext, is the Angle. The Angle that either the &8Shaft&r or Pulley will turn. From 360 to 1 degree! \\n\\nLast is the Speed and Direction. It changes how quickly the Shaft or Pulley move and either &e&oClockwise&r or &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r."]
	quest.1BA11428DF7541AD.title: "&eSequenced Gearshift"
	quest.1BEC6BA29915D6E8.quest_desc: [
		"&f&d&lGravitite Armor&r&f is one of the strongest armors in the &b&lAether&r&f, crafted from enchanted Gravitite."
		""
		"&fWhen equipped, it grants incredible protection and the ability to float gracefully through the air."
		""
		"&fGather enough enchanted Gravitite to forge the full set and harness its powerful, weightless energy."
	]
	quest.1BEC6BA29915D6E8.quest_subtitle: "&f&lHave a full set of &d&lGravitite Armor&r&f &lin your inventory"
	quest.1BEC6BA29915D6E8.title: "&7&lQuest: Full Gravitite Power!"
	quest.1C2309DB4B890E71.quest_desc: ["&bSpouts&r are used with systems to fill &eItems&r with &bFluid&r. \\n\\nFirst, you'll need to fill the &bSpout&r by &bPiping Fluid&r into it! \\n\\nThen, if there is a &bFluid&r Holding &eItem&r: Bucket or Bottle, then it will be filled with the &bFluid&r in the Spout. \\n\\nIt will automatically fill it, it doesn't need Rotational Power it uses Gravity!"]
	quest.1C2309DB4B890E71.title: "&bSpout"
	quest.1C82B8EA4AB15FA8.quest_desc: ["Adds a filter that allows you to tell the Backpack which items it should keep stocked. Shift right-clicking an inventory will refill it."]
	quest.1CB4895673096FA8.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 21"
	quest.1CB4895673096FA8.title: "Rival Terry"
	quest.1CC4F1C3B6F2BC2B.quest_desc: [
		"&e&lPokémon Level Cap:&r"
		""
		"- Your Pokémon cannot exceed the current level cap shown on your &fTrainer Card&r."
		""
		"- Once a Pokémon reaches this cap, it will stop gaining experience until you progress further."
		""
		"- Trainers will refuse to battle you if any Pokémon in your party are above the cap."
		""
		"- To increase your level cap, you must defeat the &6Key Trainers&r listed on your Trainer Card."
		""
		"- Track your progression using &fAdvancements&r and your Trainer Card."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&e&lFinding Key Trainers:&r"
		""
		"- Key Trainers spawn in specific biomes; check your Trainer Card for hints."
		""
		"- Having a Pokémon at the level cap in your team increases their spawn rate."
		""
		"- Defeating new trainers lowers the chance of previously defeated ones respawning."
		""
		"- At the very start, your Trainer Card’s arrow points to the &fTrainer Association&r NPC. "
		""
		"- Once you select a series, the arrow disappears — you must find Key Trainers using biome info, conditions, or required items."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&e&lUnlocking Gym Leaders:&r"
		""
		"- Some trainers spawn naturally as you explore the world."
		""
		"- Certain Gym Leaders and bosses require a special &e\"Signature Item\"&r (e.g. Hard Stone for Brock)."
		""
		"- To summon them, right-click a &fTrainer Spawner&r with the required item. The trainer will appear after a few seconds!"
		""
		"- Trainer Spawners can be crafted or found near arenas in Pokémon villages."
		""
		"- Advanced content like Leagues and villain teams may require completing multiple series."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&e&lTrainer Association:&r"
		""
		"- Appears near a player with a &fTrainer Card&r but no active series."
		""
		"- When nearby, your Trainer Card will glow and display a guiding arrow."
		""
		"- This NPC lets you start one of many &fTrainer Series&r (Pokémon Adventures, Gym Challenges, Villain Teams, etc.)."
		""
		"- You can only have &cone active series&r at a time. Activating another resets your current progress unless it is finished."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&e&lTips:&r"
		""
		"- Train a rotating team of Pokémon to avoid hitting the cap too quickly."
		""
		"- Prioritize trainer battles early to unlock gyms and progress smoothly."
		""
		"- Always check &fAdvancements&r for hidden goals and guidance."
		""
		"- Use your Trainer Card to find biome and dimension clues for Key Trainers."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&e&lMore Information:&r"
		"For full details, see the official &fRadical Cobblemon Trainers&r documentation:"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"WIKI ! Click Here !\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://srcmc.gitlab.io/rct/docs/0.13/\"}}"
	]
	quest.1CC4F1C3B6F2BC2B.quest_subtitle: "IMPORTANT! (READ ALL PAGES)"
	quest.1CC4F1C3B6F2BC2B.title: "&ePokémon Level Cap and Trainers"
	quest.1D3F797A49A403AD.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Soul Render&r is crafted from &3Cursium&r and Black Steel."
		""
		"It being a massive weapon (as most in &4&lCataclysm&r are) it has big Range and a ton of Damage... but its special effects are even better!"
		""
		"You can use Right Click to be sent charging forward with the &3Soul Render&r. When you do, &3Phantom Halberds&r will drop from the sky where you went! You can also Shift Right Click to spawn &3Phantom Halberds&r all around you."
	]
	quest.1D3F797A49A403AD.title: "&3Soul Render"
	quest.1DB676B8355A8E89.quest_desc: [
		"From the scales of the &2Naga&r, you can craft some armor."
		""
		"The armor isn't very strong."
	]
	quest.1DB676B8355A8E89.title: "&2Naga Scale Armor"
	quest.1DBC580818C000E2.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Dark-type moves."
	quest.1E0802B64B390218.quest_desc: [
		"&f&b&lIcestone&r&f is a rare, chilling material found within the frozen regions of the &b&lAether&r&f."
		""
		"&fIt radiates an icy aura capable of cooling lava and even freezing water nearby, making it a valuable resource for crafting and exploration in the coldest heights of the skylands."
	]
	quest.1E0802B64B390218.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain &b&lIcestone&r&f"
	quest.1E0802B64B390218.title: "&7&lQuest: Frozen Treasure"
	quest.1E52A8B5A243B028.quest_desc: ["The &dTri-Bow&r is dropped from the &3Snow Queen&r, it can shoot 3 Arrows at the same time, while only using 1."]
	quest.1E52A8B5A243B028.quest_subtitle: "Buy One Get Two?"
	quest.1E52A8B5A243B028.title: "&dTri-Bow"
	quest.1E641E88FE5CB549.quest_desc: [
		"&dNetherite&r items are even better overall, and won't burn in lava! You still will though, even wearing the armor. Don't try it out."
		""
		"These items can be used to make some of the best tools and armor in the game."
	]
	quest.1E641E88FE5CB549.title: "&dNetherite Tier"
	quest.1E7098D1A8F982E5.quest_desc: [
		"The &c&lNetherite Monstrosity&r lives up to his name, he's a beast of &cNetherite &fand &cLava&r."
		""
		"He can have up to 48,000 &4Hearts&r but when I first met him he was only at around 9,500 &4Hearts&r. He will regenerate &4Hearts&r when no Player is nearby."
		""
		"He has a few Melee attacks like smacking you with his massive arms and ground pounding on you. He can also throw blocks in the Air causing a Shockwave."
		""
		"If you get farther from him he might charge at you or leap at you."
		""
		"The worst of his attacks are definitely the Ranged ones though... he can shoot &cMagma Balls&r at you and where they drop, &cLava&r will spawn. He can also shoot &cFireballs&r from his hands, these will cause &cFire Spouts&r to come out of the ground."
	]
	quest.1E7098D1A8F982E5.title: "&c&lNetherite Monstrosity&r"
	quest.1E7C47966E77F7BA.quest_desc: [
		"The Warden is a boss added in 1.20."
		""
		"He spawns by having 3 naturally spawning Sculk Shriekers going off in a row, or any Shriekers going off after a first Warden has spawned."
		""
		"He is the most powerful Mob added by Minecraft, with 500 Hearts and over 20 Hearts damage with his attacks."
		""
		"His attacks include hitting you and Sonar Blasts for those farther."
		""
		"His only weakness is being blind, but like daredevil it just made his other senses much stronger! If you are close he can smell you and careful with making noise!"
		""
		"If you somehow kill him he will drop: Sculk Catalysts, Warden Carapace, and Heart of the Deep."
	]
	quest.1E8E5EFE4182F4B2.quest_subtitle: "The Third Upgrade"
	quest.1E8E5EFE4182F4B2.title: "&eGold Chest"
	quest.1E9B2D814F50A265.quest_desc: ["The &6Encased Fan&r is one of the most underrated Machines in &6&lCreate&r. \\n\\nYou can place it down and it'll face you, or Shift Right Click to place it facing away from you. \\n\\nWhen given &dRotational Power&r &e&oClockwise&r, it will blow air away from it. When given &dRotational Power&r &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r it will suck air toward it. \\n\\nThese sucks and blows will also effect &eItems&r and Entities near them, and yes the faster it spins the more it sucks and blows! \\n\\nWe also get extra Recipes we can make by putting a Block in front of the &6Fan&r. This will then effect the &eItems&r being blown on by the &6Fan&r. \\n\\nWe can use &cLava&r to &6Blast&e Items&r like a Furnace. Getting Ingots from Ores, Stone from Cobble, and Nuggets from Tools. \\n\\nIf we put Fire in front of the Fan we can Smoke Items. Like Cooking them! \\n\\nInstead of Lava we can also place Water in front of it. This will wash whatever is in front of it like Concrete Powder into Concrete. \\n\\nAnd last, instead of Fire we can use Soul Fire to haunt Items! This will change Items either into Nether variants or entirely different Items."]
	quest.1E9B2D814F50A265.quest_subtitle: "This blows!"
	quest.1E9B2D814F50A265.title: "&6Encased Fan"
	quest.1EE3EA2D9418700D.quest_desc: ["The &2&lUndergarden&r Dimension is full of diverse and disgusting Biomes full of plenty of Vegetation, Mobs: friendly and unfriendly, and of course Ores and Items. "]
	quest.1EE3EA2D9418700D.title: "Welcome to the &2&lUndergarden&r!"
	quest.1F0CE3C52A63AF28.quest_desc: [
		"&eKoboletons&r are mini Dino Skeletons who serve the &e&lAncient Remnant&r."
		""
		"They only have 12 and a half &4Hearts&r and attack you with their Khopesh."
		""
		"They can drop their weapon, along with their Bones, and Ancient Metal Nuggets."
	]
	quest.1F0CE3C52A63AF28.title: "&eKoboletons"
	quest.1F14F5CFABF975AB.quest_desc: [
		"The &dGauntlet of &bBulwark&r acts different from what you'd assume."
		""
		"Instead of bringing mobs closer it pushes them away, when Holding Right Click, and gives them &bBlazing Brand&r."
		""
		"Then when you release Right Click you'll charge in the direction you are looking."
		""
		"It's made by fusing the &dGauntlet of Guard&r with a &bBulwark of Flame&r in the &4Mechanical Fusion Anvil&r."
	]
	quest.1F14F5CFABF975AB.title: "&dGauntlet of &bBulwark"
	quest.1F2CBDECBC1EC509.quest_desc: [
		"&bIgnitium&r is like Netherite but it takes actual skill to get."
		""
		"The &b&lIgnis&r will only drop 1 so get good use of it! "
		""
		"You can use it to upgrade your Netherite Armor or use it to make the Weapons."
	]
	quest.1F2CBDECBC1EC509.title: "&bIgnitium"
	quest.1F57DB847879BB7F.quest_desc: [
		"Want another pet from &4&lCataclysm&r? Then the Remnant Skull is what you need!"
		""
		"It's a confirmed drop from the &eAncient Remnant&r and when used will spawn a Modern Revenant."
		""
		"This one is much smaller and nicer than the &eAncient&r one. You can tame it by feeding it a Sniffer Egg then it will act like a dog."
		""
		"Attacking what attacks you or what you attack. It also has 3 modes: follow, wander, and stay. Follow it will... well follow you. Wander will have it walking around a certain area. And stay will have it lay down in one spot."
		""
		"They have 2700 &4Hearts&r and you can feed them &eKoboleton Bones&r to heal them!"
	]
	quest.1F57DB847879BB7F.title: "&eModern Remnant&r"
	quest.2078E069979E9FC6.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 21"
	quest.2078E069979E9FC6.title: "Rocket Admin Archer"
	quest.21149CD966FA2261.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 46"
	quest.21149CD966FA2261.title: "Boss Giovanni"
	quest.2122EB9903B72CC4.quest_subtitle: "Raises the holder's Sp. Atk by 1 stage when hit by a damaging Water-type move."
	quest.2171FE872235D2FD.quest_desc: [
		"Is that Smogvent moving? No wait it's just a &3S'Mog&r! The close cousin of the &2Mog&r!"
		""
		"They act exactly like &2Mogs&r just these might drop Blue Mogmoss."
	]
	quest.2171FE872235D2FD.title: "&3S'Mog&r"
	quest.21C6920CCEC5C080.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.21C6920CCEC5C080.title: "&eAdvanced Feeding Upgrade"
	quest.21E45E49D2CFDED3.quest_desc: [
		"&fThe &a&lPale Garden&r&f is a mystical variation of the &a&lDark Forest&r&f. Search for Pale Oak trees&r&f, Pale Moss, and Eyeblossoms that thrive in this eerie grove. &b&lNo animals roam here&r&f, only the soft sounds of the wind and the whispers of the moss."
		""
		"&fStep into the &a&lPale Garden&r&f and uncover its secrets."
	]
	quest.21E45E49D2CFDED3.quest_subtitle: "&f&lFind and explore the &a&lPale Garden&r&f&l biome"
	quest.220D328E9DF6ACEA.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.220D328E9DF6ACEA.title: "&l&9Overworld Bounty:&r&e Zombies"
	quest.2254CA77DB8BD26B.quest_desc: [
		"The &aForgotten Guardian&r is a massive Golem made of &aForgotten Ingots&r."
		""
		"It'll target the Player and will do whatever needed to kill them."
		""
		"They have 80 Hearts and if you can kill them they will drop &aForgotten Nuggets&r."
	]
	quest.2254CA77DB8BD26B.title: "&aForgotten Guardian&r"
	quest.225804AF145DABB8.quest_desc: [
		"After defeating the &cUr-Ghast&r, you'll unlock the Snowy Forest biomes."
		""
		"There are many creatures to fight, but to continue your progression, you'll need to kill the Alpha Yeti."
		""
		"You can find the Alpha Yeti in a massive Yeti cave. Defeat it to move on."
	]
	quest.225804AF145DABB8.quest_subtitle: "You had Snow idea"
	quest.225804AF145DABB8.title: "To the Snow Biomes!"
	quest.226B313AA438ED0B.quest_desc: [
		"&dVoid Cores&r are drops from the &dEnder Golem&r! "
		""
		"They are weapons, when you Right Click with them, &dVoid Runes&r will spawn from the ground."
		""
		"&dVoid Runes&r act like Evoker Fangs, they go in a line for about 10 Blocks in the direction you are using it toward."
		""
		"They do about 3 and a half &4Hearts&r of damage for each time they hit a Mob. They also knockback Mobs which Evoker Fangs do not."
		""
		"This can be used in Crafts for even more &4&lCataclysm&r Weapons!"
	]
	quest.226B313AA438ED0B.title: "&dVoid Core"
	quest.22EA7573BD2658CA.quest_desc: [
		"Catacombs are massive underground structures made of Depthrock Bricks. They might have a part sticking out of the ground you can find."
		""
		"Within the huge maze lies &7Forgottens&r, hidden Chests, and the boss: &aForgotten Guardian&r."
	]
	quest.22EA7573BD2658CA.title: "Catacombs"
	quest.230E55D2B2F1D74F.quest_desc: [
		"&fBefore marriage comes the promise, the &b&lEngagement Ring&r&f allows you to officially get engaged to your loved one in &6&lMinecraft Comes Alive: Reborn&r&f."
		""
		"&fWhen your relationship reaches &d&l50 Hearts&r&f, you can gift this ring to a villager to become engaged. Once engaged, neither other players nor villagers can marry your partner."
		""
		"&fTo craft it, use the same recipe as the &6&lWedding Ring&r&f, but place a &b&lDiamond&r&f in the top-center slot instead of a gold Ingot, and surround it with &6&l8 Gold Ingots&r&f."
		""
		"&fNote: Engagement is a promise, you cannot propose yet until marriage."
		""
		"&fTake the first step toward your happily ever after."
	]
	quest.230E55D2B2F1D74F.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCraft an &b&lEngagement Ring&r&f to propose to your special villager&r"
	quest.230E55D2B2F1D74F.title: "&6&lQuest: Craft the Engagement Ring"
	quest.233F980A2374043B.quest_desc: [
		"&f&bSkyroot Log&r is from the trees within &f&bThe Aether&r."
		""
		"Used to create &f&bSkyroot Planks "
	]
	quest.233F980A2374043B.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain &b&lSkyroot Logs&r&f"
	quest.233F980A2374043B.title: "&7&lQuest: Obtain Skyroot Logs"
	quest.236B4FEFBB10D8AD.quest_subtitle: "Restores any lower stat in battle. Consumed after use."
	quest.2379CC49B04CD686.quest_desc: [
		""
		"&fThe &b&lAether&r&f is a vast world floating high above the clouds, filled with wondrous landscapes and mysterious creatures."
		""
		"&fFrom lush skylands to crystalline peaks and glowing groves, each biome tells part of the Aether’s ancient story."
	]
	quest.2379CC49B04CD686.quest_subtitle: "&f&lDiscover all &b&lAether Biomes&r&f"
	quest.2379CC49B04CD686.title: "&7&lQuest: Explorer of the Skies"
	quest.237AFF59FE52D695.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 55"
	quest.237AFF59FE52D695.title: "Rival Terry"
	quest.239328B41772D481.quest_desc: [
		"&bSludges&r spawn in &bBlooming Caverns&r and act like Slimes!"
		""
		"Their largest form has 8 &4Hearts&r and does a ton of Damage. On death they will spawn 2-4 Medium &bSludges&r."
		""
		"Their medium forms have 2 &4Hearts&r and do much less Damage. On death they'll spawn 2-4 small &bSludges&r."
		""
		"The small form has only a half a &4Heart of Health&r and won't do any Damage."
	]
	quest.239328B41772D481.title: "&bSludge"
	quest.23E55A66BA7D583D.quest_desc: [
		"Sophisticated Storage allows you to upgrade your Chests and Barrels with metals to increase their storage! You can also add upgrades to increase their functionality."
		""
		"These chests are just like a vanilla Chest or Barrel, but they have a slot for a Storage Upgrade!"
	]
	quest.23E55A66BA7D583D.title: "Sophisticated Storage"
	quest.23E924A6CB8BC07F.quest_desc: [
		"You have proven your strength against the &b&lValkyrie Queen&r&f and claimed her treasures. "
		""
		"Among them rests the &c&lRegeneration Stone&r&f, a relic of immense healing power. "
		""
		"Take it and keep it close, for you will need its blessing… the &6&lGold Dungeon&r&f is waiting for you."
	]
	quest.23E924A6CB8BC07F.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain a &c&lRegeneration Stone&r&f&l from the &7&lSilver Dungeon&r&f&l"
	quest.23E924A6CB8BC07F.title: "&7&lQuest: The Final Challenge Awaits"
	quest.23F86679EB68F868.quest_desc: [
		"Near Frostfields you may find Frosty Smogstem Forests. "
		""
		"These are just like Frostfields just with Smogstem Trees!"
	]
	quest.23F86679EB68F868.title: "Frosty Smogstem Forest"
	quest.24A19E8F68F2993B.quest_desc: [
		"The &bBlooming Caverns&r are more like Lush Caves than normal Caves. I say that because of the abundance of PLANTS!"
		""
		"You'll find Plants growing from the ceiling to the floor, Plants growing from the floor to the ceiling, Plants growing from the &9Water&r, and Plants not even Growing at all! "
		""
		"The floor is covered in &bBlooming Sculk Stone&r and even &bBlooming Moss&r."
		""
		"There's even Water Ponds here, the only place you can find &9Water&r in this &3&lDimension&r."
	]
	quest.24A19E8F68F2993B.title: "&bBlooming Caverns"
	quest.24E658BA47367A44.quest_desc: ["&aRope Pulley&r will move any Blocks that are attached to its &aRope&r at the bottom of it. This will also move any Blocks &aGlued&r to that Block! \\n\\nWhen moved &e&oClockwise&r by &dRotational Power&r, it will lower the &aRope&r until it hits another Block, or to where it is set. \\n\\nWhen given &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r &dRotational Power&r it will move the &aRope&r toward the &aPulley&r until it hits the &aPulley&r or it goes where it is set to go. \\n\\nWhy do I keep saying \"set to go\"? Because there is destination settings with Movement Mode! \\n\\nThese will decide where the Blocks end up stopping!"]
	quest.24E658BA47367A44.title: "&aRope Pulley"
	quest.25092191B48B7F14.quest_desc: ["Diamonds are one of the best materials to use for tool crafting, but they also allow you to visit new dimensions like the Twilight Forest!"]
	quest.25092191B48B7F14.title: "We've Struck &bDiamonds&r!"
	quest.2572062789EDE241.quest_desc: [
		"&fLove is in the air! With the &6&lMatchmaker's Ring&r&f, you can help two lonely villagers find their perfect match. This special item allows you to &a&lmarry two unmarried villagers&r&f when used correctly."
		""
		"&fTo craft it, place &c&l8 Iron Ingots&r&f around the edges of the crafting grid, leaving the center empty. Once crafted, make sure you have &a&l2 Matchmaker's Rings&r&f in your inventory, one for each villager."
		""
		"&fStand near two unmarried villagers, open one's interaction menu, choose &a&lInteract → Gift&r&f, and give them the ring. Both rings will disappear, and the two villagers will instantly marry each other!"
		""
		""
		"&fBring happiness to your village, one marriage at a time!"
	]
	quest.2572062789EDE241.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCraft a &6&lMatchmaker's Ring&r&f to arrange a marriage between two unmarried villagers&r"
	quest.2572062789EDE241.title: "&6&lQuest: Craft the Matchmaker's Ring"
	quest.25997612D8B74C83.quest_desc: [
		"&3The Annihilator&r is a weapon made from &3Cursium&r and Black Steel."
		""
		""
		"If you have an &3Annihilator&r in each Hand, then you can Hold Right Click to do a powerful ground pound, damaging all around you!"
	]
	quest.25997612D8B74C83.title: "&3The Annihilator"
	quest.25AB3942F75C3303.quest_desc: ["&cUtherium&r can either be Mined or dropped from &cRot Mobs&r. "]
	quest.25AB3942F75C3303.title: "&cUtherium&r"
	quest.26855F6A07F49A5D.quest_desc: [
		"The Waystone is a powerful tool for quick travel across the world. By activating Waystones, you can teleport between them for faster exploration and travel."
		""
		"To use a Waystone:"
		""
		"1. Find or craft a Waystone (you’ll need a few resources)."
		""
		"2. Right-click on the Waystone to activate it."
		""
		"3. Once activated, you can teleport to it from any other Waystone you’ve unlocked."
		""
		"4. To teleport, simply open the Waystone menu and select your destination."
		""
		"Note: You can only teleport to Waystones that you have previously activated. Enjoy your fast travels!"
	]
	quest.26855F6A07F49A5D.quest_subtitle: "&eWaystone Explanation"
	quest.26855F6A07F49A5D.title: "Waystone"
	quest.26A4A9CBB7C98F75.quest_desc: ["&6Ironwood Armor&r can be crafted using &6Ironwood&r and comes automatically enchanted."]
	quest.26A4A9CBB7C98F75.title: "&6Ironwood Armor"
	quest.26F52E1355D6393A.quest_subtitle: "Protects the holder from additional effects from other Pokémon."
	quest.275C45E1E5220C6F.quest_desc: [
		"To create Netherite tools and armor you'll need to find the &6Netherite Smithing Template&r in chests found inside of Bastions."
		""
		"These can be combined with a &cNetherite&r ingot and a Diamond tool or armor piece in a &aSmithing Table&r to upgrade it to &cNetherite&r."
		""
		"Tip: Don't use all of your templates in one go! You can create duplicates by using the recipe to create another."
	]
	quest.275C45E1E5220C6F.title: "&6Netherite Template&r"
	quest.282E71C993487B5D.quest_desc: [
		"&fSaddles are now &a&lcraftable in the &6&lVanilla Backport&r&f mod. This simple but useful change makes exploration easier and more accessible."
		""
		"&fUnlock the recipe by picking up Leather for the first time. &d&lCraft your own Saddle&r&f and get ready to ride."
	]
	quest.282E71C993487B5D.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCraft a &a&lSaddle&r&f&l using 3 &6&lLeather&r&f&l and 1 &7&lIron Ingot"
	quest.282E71C993487B5D.title: "&6&lQuest: Craft a Saddle"
	quest.2840B370946C57EB.quest_desc: [
		"&eBone Reptile Armor&r is made from &eKoboleton Bones&r, &eAncient Metal&r, and for the Helmet a &eKobolediator Skull&r."
		""
		"These don't appear to do anything special, just give very good stats for cheap Armor!"
	]
	quest.2840B370946C57EB.title: "&eBone Reptile Armor"
	quest.28A0E43B48FE8AEB.quest_desc: [
		"&7Cloggrum&r is the Iron of the &2&lUndergarden&r."
		""
		"It is found everywhere and is used in a dozen different recipes."
	]
	quest.28A0E43B48FE8AEB.title: "&7Cloggrum&r"
	quest.28EBBEEFC60021EB.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Water-type moves."
	quest.2930CBC841FBE168.quest_desc: [
		"The &5Echoing Forest&r is a little plain but it also houses the &5Echoing Trees&r!"
		""
		"The &5Echoing Trees&r act like normal Trees, you can Mine their &aLogs&r for Crafting and their &5Leaves&r will drop Saplings. You can also find Sculk Gleam within the Leaves."
		""
		"Around it you will find &5Echoing Soil&r all over the surface. These unfortunately can not be made into Farmland or Dirt, they're just Blocks."
	]
	quest.2930CBC841FBE168.title: "&5Echoing Forest"
	quest.296D4C2F8CA1623D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Scepter of Fortification&r summons shields around you for protection."
		""
		"To recharge, combine with &6Golden Apples&r in a crafting grid."
	]
	quest.296D4C2F8CA1623D.quest_subtitle: "Summons Shields"
	quest.296D4C2F8CA1623D.title: "&6Scepter of Fortification"
	quest.29917E6196649F5D.quest_desc: ["Speed is distance over time, AKA how long it takes to get from point A to point B... well... we are working with &dRevolutions&r, it is more how long it takes to get from point A to point A in this big of a Circle. \\n\\nAnyways it is how quick our &6Machines&r move, including &dCogs&r and &8Shafts&r! \\n\\nThis is important because Speed will effect how other &6Machines&r work. Some will need a certain Speed and others will work more efficiently at higher Speeds. \\n\\nWe can place a Speedometer (yes, like in a car) into our Kinetic System to see how fast everything is moving."]
	quest.29917E6196649F5D.title: "Speed"
	quest.29B10D2544CB4EB9.quest_desc: ["Auto-feeds you with food in the Backpack."]
	quest.29E6BB90428046CF.quest_subtitle: "Grants the holder immunity to powder and spore moves and damage from weather."
	quest.2A3FBC572B962939.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the holder's Accuracy."
	quest.2A6E77112864A472.quest_desc: [
		"&2Dwellers&r are the Cows of &2&lUndergarden&r."
		""
		"They are Passive and will drop Leather and Dweller Meat on death."
	]
	quest.2A6E77112864A472.title: "&2Dweller&r"
	quest.2A99F37C23B4E163.quest_desc: [
		"Do you want to be able to shoot Ender blasts like the &eLich&r? If so, the &9Scepter of Twilight&r is the scepter for you!."
		""
		"To recharge, combine it with an &5Ender Pearl&r in a crafting grid."
	]
	quest.2A99F37C23B4E163.quest_subtitle: "Shoots Ender Blasts"
	quest.2A99F37C23B4E163.title: "&9Scepter of Twilight"
	quest.2AC8CA7B08893C03.quest_desc: [
		"&2Achaeology&r allows players to find items inside of &aSuspicious&r blocks like Sand and Gravel."
		""
		"These blocks can be found in various structures like Warm Ocean Ruins, Desert Pyramids, Desert Wells, and &eTrail Ruins&r."
		""
		"To uncover an item from a Suspicious block, you need to create a &aBrush&r to brush away the block to unveil an item."
	]
	quest.2AC8CA7B08893C03.title: "&2Archaeology&r!"
	quest.2AEA51044AD44BE8.quest_desc: ["&eDepots&r will hold &eItems&r. They can hold them to process the &eItems&r, or deposit to a &eChute&r, or even just for decoration! \\n\\nYou can place a &eChute&r near the end of a &eBelt&r to bring &eItems&f from the &eBelt &fonto the &eDepot&r. \\n\\nThe &eDepot&r can also be placed beneath a &6Machine&r to process &eItems&r within it. "]
	quest.2AEA51044AD44BE8.title: "&eDepot"
	quest.2B6161D8F3839FF4.quest_desc: [
		"The tutorial is now finished!"
		""
		"View new quests in the menu on the left, they are sorted by category."
	]
	quest.2B6161D8F3839FF4.quest_subtitle: "Read my description!"
	quest.2B7ECB12E07BB430.quest_desc: ["Magnets items into the Backpack."]
	quest.2BA3E1FA48783AEB.quest_desc: ["Chests have 27 slots and can be made into a double chest to store twice that amount."]
	quest.2BA3E1FA48783AEB.quest_subtitle: "The Chest"
	quest.2BA3E1FA48783AEB.title: "Vanilla Storage"
	quest.2BB3DB19D5EFC7E2.quest_desc: ["The &dClutch&r can be connected to our Kinetic Systems where it will act like a Fence Gate. \\n\\nBy giving it a &4Redstone Signal&r it will stop the flow of &dRotational Power&r through it. \\n\\nSo all &dRotating&r will stop at the &dClutch&r if it is powered with &4Redstone&r. The ones &dRotating&r into it will continue &dRotating&r as normal though!"]
	quest.2BB3DB19D5EFC7E2.title: "&dClutch"
	quest.2BB9998AF9016386.quest_desc: [
		"&fYou’ve caught strong Pokémon, but did you know some can be ridden? You can mount your Pokémon and travel the world faster than ever! Learn how to ride, dismount, and control your Pokémon like a pro!"
		""
		"&6🏇 How to Ride Pokémon:&r"
		""
		"&7- Crouch and Right-click a &arideable Pokémon &7 and click on the ride option to mount it. &7Use &eWASD &7to move and &eSpace &7to jump (if your Pokémon can)."
		""
		"&9Flying Pokémon: &7Hold &eSpace &7to ascend and &eShift &7to descend. You fly in the direction you are looking."
		""
		"&3Water Pokémon: &7Glide smoothly over water like a true aquatic master!"
		""
		"&c❗ How to Dismount:&r"
		"&7- Press &eR &7to safely get off your Pokémon."
		""
		"&4⚠ Warning! &7Make sure you’re not in mid-air when dismounting!"
	]
	quest.2BB9998AF9016386.quest_subtitle: "Master the art of Pokémon riding!"
	quest.2BB9998AF9016386.title: "Ride Like a Champion!"
	quest.2BE310CF4172BDA2.quest_desc: [
		"&3Sculk Grime&r is &3&lDeeper and Darker's&r version of Clay!"
		""
		"You can find it within a few Biomes and when you mine it you'll get &3Grime Balls&r."
		""
		"These can then be made back into &3Sculk Grime&r or made into &3Grime Bricks&r."
	]
	quest.2BE310CF4172BDA2.title: "&3Sculk Grime"
	quest.2BE9059BD306DB54.quest_desc: ["Coal is your first real source of power. If you are running low and can't find any Coal, an alternative would be to use Charcoal."]
	quest.2BE9059BD306DB54.quest_subtitle: "Smelt your logs"
	quest.2C2958E38293717E.quest_desc: ["To start with the new &6&lCreate&r &eItems&r we'll need &eCardboard&r! \\n\\nWhich is made from &6Pressing&r Pulp. \\n\\nPulp is made from &6Mixing&r 4 Saplings and &9Water&f in a &6Mechanical Mixer&r and &8Basin&r. \\n\\nYou can combine &eCardboards&r to make &eBlocks of Cardboard&r which can make the new &eItems&r in &6&lCreate&r... or &eCardboard Armor&r!"]
	quest.2C2958E38293717E.title: "&6&lCreate&r 1.21"
	quest.2C5ADE0BF901B747.quest_desc: ["Functioning similar to a Furnace &fThe &b&lFreezer&r&f is a powerful utility block capable of infusing items with the chilling essence of the &b&lAether&r&f."]
	quest.2C5ADE0BF901B747.title: "&7&lQuest: Craft a Freezer"
	quest.2CA78763EBCB3EE7.quest_desc: [
		"&dNargoyles&r are nasty and hostile Mobs that spawn underground."
		""
		"They have 7 and a half Hearts and will relentlessly try to kill you."
		""
		"They drop nothing and just serve as an obstacle for those trying to peacefully mine. "
	]
	quest.2CA78763EBCB3EE7.title: "&dNargoyle&r"
	quest.2CDC4FF2EC3EEC51.quest_desc: [
		"This quest only requires you to make one Diamond tool or armor piece, but it's probably good to get a full set!"
		""
		"Diamond tools boast high durability, and the armor offers great protection overall."
		""
		"To make the better tools and armor in the game, you'll need Diamond stuff as a base!"
	]
	quest.2CDC4FF2EC3EEC51.title: "&9Gearing Up"
	quest.2D2471CDCEACD8CF.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.2D2471CDCEACD8CF.quest_subtitle: "&6Held items&f are &bItems&f that can be &e[held by a Pokémon]&f. When held, these items will give Pokémon certain buffs or effects in battle."
	quest.2D2471CDCEACD8CF.title: "Held Items"
	quest.2D41B04C75FA02BC.quest_desc: ["The &6Mechanical Press&r is very helpful for making even more &6Machines&r! \\n\\nWhen powered with &dRotational Power&r (and a lot of Stress Units) it will send the &6Metal Press&r down to Blocks below it. Like a Hydraulic Press! \\n\\nAny Items below it: either on a &eBelt&r, &eDepot&r, or even just dropped, will be &6Pressed&r. \\n\\nThis is mainly for turning &7Ingots &finto &7Plates&r with no charge. You can also use it to get Paper from Sugarcane and Paths from Dirt! \\n\\nIf you place a &8Basin&r beneath it you can then use the &6Press&r to combine &bLiquids&r, &eItems&r, and Blocks to create new &eItems&r. \\n\\nAnother option with the &8Basin&r below our Press is Compacting Crafting. This is automated Crafting for Recipes that contain only one type of &eItem&r, like 9 &7Iron Ingots&f into an &7Iron Block&r."]
	quest.2D41B04C75FA02BC.title: "&6Mechanical Press"
	quest.2D96965317D3CFEC.quest_desc: ["Yay, complicated subjects! This time it is &5Conductors&r and &5Train Schedules&r. \\n\\nFirst is getting our &5Conductor&r, these are any Lead-able Mobs or &cBlaze Burners&r. If we have a Seat next to the Train Controls we can Lead a Mob into the Seat where it will wait to become a &5Conductor&r. \\n\\n&cBlaze Burners&r work similar, just without the need for a seat, they bring their own. \\n\\nThen, we can hand our Mob or &cBlaze Burner&r, a filled out &5Schedule&r to give them that task plus a &5Conductor's Hat&r. \\n\\n&5Schedules&r are Items that can be \"Coded\" to order our &5Conductors&r to preform certain tasks. The tasks are either: go to &5Station&r, pickup or drop off Packages, change title, or change max speed. \\n\\nOnce we add a task, we can edit its configs to change when it will start the next task! These can be either a certain Time waited, Time of Day, amount of stuff in &5Train&r, or even &4Redstone&r!"]
	quest.2D96965317D3CFEC.title: "&5Conductors"
	quest.2DB9797B82032203.quest_desc: ["When &6&lPhoenix Armor&r&f meets the cool depths of water, it hardens into &8&lObsidian Armor&r&f. This resilient set represents balance between fire and flow, strength and calm. Take the plunge, quench the flames, and claim armor forged from both extremes."]
	quest.2DB9797B82032203.quest_subtitle: "&f&lHave a full set of &8&lObsidian Armor&r&f&l in your inventory"
	quest.2DB9797B82032203.title: "&7&lQuest: Forged in Fire, Tempered by Water"
	quest.2DC096FA124A761D.quest_desc: ["Auto-smelt items in the Backpack."]
	quest.2DC096FA124A761D.title: "&eAuto-Smelting Upgrade"
	quest.2DCD89D4499FCA74.quest_desc: [
		"&bBlazing Grips&r are another Item we can make with &bIgnitium&r!"
		""
		"It is a Curios Item that goes on your Hands."
		""
		"When worn, all attacks have a chance of giving the recipient &bBlazing Brand&r."
	]
	quest.2DCD89D4499FCA74.title: "&bBlazing Grips"
	quest.2DE271C5C036E77D.quest_desc: [
		"Overhauled Endermen is a similar Mod to Overhauled Creepers! Just with Endermen."
		""
		"You'll find all these Endermen in all different Biomes and each are unique in their own ways! Some have different attacks, some drop different Pearls, and they all look different!"
	]
	quest.2DE271C5C036E77D.title: "Enderman Variants"
	quest.2E029230177ECD86.quest_subtitle: "Reduces the holder's Speed by 50% and grounds the holder."
	quest.2E1212BD718A3D17.quest_desc: [
		"&fLeashes have been reworked in &6&lVanilla Backport&r&f, featuring improved physics and new mechanics. &a&lYou can now leash two entities together&r&f and even snip leashes with Shears or use dispensers to manage them automatically."
		""
		"&fExperiment with the new leash system to master your mob management skills. &b&lConnect two creatures&r&f and discover how the new leash mechanics work."
	]
	quest.2E1212BD718A3D17.quest_subtitle: "&f&lUse a &c&lleash&r&f&l to connect two mobs together"
	quest.2E1212BD718A3D17.title: "&6&lQuest: Master of Leashes"
	quest.2E2C7143DE2671A7.quest_desc: [
		"The &cNetherite Ministrosity&r is a Pet given to us by &4&lCataclysm&r!"
		""
		"First, you'll need to Craft a &cNetherite Effigy&r."
		""
		"Then, we can kill the &c&lNetherite Monstrosity&r for the &cLava Power Cells&r."
		""
		"Finally, place down the &cEffigy&r and feed it a &cPower Cell&r to tame him! "
		""
		"Once tamed he can be Shift Right Clicked to edit whether he is following, staying, or wandering."
		""
		"You can also Right Click him to open his Inventory. He has an Inventory of 15 Slots. "
		""
		"He also has 3000 &4Hearts&r"
	]
	quest.2E2C7143DE2671A7.title: "&cNetherite Ministrosity"
	quest.2E41CBF264C105C3.quest_desc: [
		"&aForgotten Minions&r aren't spawned like normal Mobs, they need to be created. They are created by placing a Carved Gloomgourd over a &aBlock of Forgotten Ingots&r. "
		""
		"They act similar to Snow Golems, they won't ever attack you and instead shoot at Hostile Mobs."
		""
		"They have 10 Hearts and don't drop anything on death"
	]
	quest.2E41CBF264C105C3.title: "&aForgotten Minions&r"
	quest.2E4324C29D8F0492.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Deeplands&r are most similar to the &3Deep Dark&r."
		""
		"They are full of &3Sculk &falong with &3Shriekers &fand &3Sensors&r, which yes can still spawn the &9&lWarden&r. "
		""
		"Here you'll also find more &3Sculk Creatures&r and Plants, and even the one Structure the &3&lOtherside&r has!"
	]
	quest.2E4324C29D8F0492.title: "&9Deeplands"
	quest.2E6B3F188C6B448F.quest_desc: [
		"Once you've unlocked the &2Highland&r biome, head over and find some Trolls to kill."
		""
		"They can drop some &9Magic Beans&r. You'll also find chests that give you Uberus Soil, which is needed to grow the Magi Beans."
	]
	quest.2E6B3F188C6B448F.title: "Visiting the Giants"
	quest.2EF97E4712CD9BE9.quest_subtitle: "Allows the holder to switch out in any situation."
	quest.2F75A5F9610F0AA3.quest_desc: [
		"&5Gloompers&r are technically Passive but they have a defense mechanism against you so I consider them Neutral! "
		"When hit they will drop an Effect similar to a Lingering Potion."
		""
		"On death they will drop their Legs and possibly Leather."
		""
		"They can also be bred with Gloomgourds!"
	]
	quest.2F75A5F9610F0AA3.title: "&5Gloomper&r"
	quest.2F787F702A5C7983.quest_desc: [
		"In order to fight &5&lThe Leviathan&r you'll need a sacrifice. The &5Abyssal Sacrifice&r to be specific."
		""
		"The Items needed is Blocks of Iron, Gold, Diamond, Emerald, and Amethyst."
		""
		"Then, you'll need a Nautilus Shell and a Heart of the Sea. Which are rare to get... unless you kill &5Deeplings&r which can drop them!"
		""
		"You'll also need an Athame which is a weapon used by &5Deepling Warlocks &fand &5Priests&r and dropped by them on death."
		""
		"The last part gives us a choice, either Crystallized Coral or Coral Chunk. Both are drops from &5Coral Golem&r and &5Coralssus&r."
	]
	quest.2F787F702A5C7983.quest_subtitle: "Waking up The Leviathan"
	quest.2F787F702A5C7983.title: "&5Abyssal Sacrifice"
	quest.2FDF483933F83043.quest_desc: ["Increases stack size in the Backpack by 8."]
	quest.2FDF483933F83043.title: "&bStack Upgrade Tier 3"
	quest.2FE44C69B34D550F.quest_subtitle: "Infatuates the opponent when the holder becomes infatuated."
	quest.301D7B3C746D9A30.quest_desc: ["Adds a Jukebox GUI to the Backpack."]
	quest.3029E1E133B91ED8.quest_desc: ["The &6Mechanical Drill&r can be used within a &aContraption&r or without. The without will need &dRotational Power&r but still does the same task. \\n\\nThe &6Mechanical Drill&r will Mine any Block in front of it (that it can). \\n\\nIt will Mine as fast as the &dRotational Power&r will give. And if there is an Inventory connected to the &aContraption&r, the Mined Block will be put into it, instead of on the floor."]
	quest.3029E1E133B91ED8.title: "&6Mechanical Drill"
	quest.30AC43222FF9B18A.quest_desc: ["&5Train Signals&r are used with &5Conductors&r who aren't Players. \\n\\nThey place just like &5Train Stations&f and &5Observers&r, but the way they are placed determines the Arrow placement. \\n\\nThe Arrows will restrict where &5Conductors&r can pass their &5Trains&r, if the Arrow is facing the opposite way, the &5Train&r won't pass. \\n\\nYou can add two Signals facing opposite directions to let &5Conductors&r pass wherever you want. \\n\\nWith a bunch of &5Signals&r we can make Stop Lights for &7Track&r intersections. Place the &5Signals&r to where there are Arrows on both sides of the intersection. \\n\\nThis will make it so &5Trains&r will stop if another &5Train&r is in the intersection. That prevents collisions which Derail &5Trains&r. Derailed &5Trains&r will need a Wrench to put them back on &7Track&r!"]
	quest.30AC43222FF9B18A.title: "&5Train Signals"
	quest.31435D6CAE06409F.quest_subtitle: "When the holder successfully inflicts damage, the target may also flinch."
	quest.315E34179BC33CF8.quest_subtitle: "Bring back an ancient warrior!"
	quest.315E34179BC33CF8.title: "The Mysterious Dome"
	quest.3171CFB0E5AEC01C.quest_desc: [
		"&9Sploogies&r can rarely spawn but when they do they are destined to annoy you."
		""
		"They will shoot spit at you but if you hit them they will run away; similar to a baby Piglin."
		""
		"They only drop Depthrock Pebbles on death."
	]
	quest.3171CFB0E5AEC01C.title: "&9Sploogie&r"
	quest.31AD25384D6D9BEF.quest_desc: [
		"&3Sculk Stone&r spawns pretty much everywhere but &cOvercast Columns&r."
		""
		"It works like normal &7Stone&r, like in every single way. You can smelt Cobbled versions to get &3Sculk Stone&r which can then be made into many other Building Blocks."
		""
		"Unfortunately it can't be used to make Stone Tools though..."
	]
	quest.31AD25384D6D9BEF.title: "&3Sculk Stone"
	quest.31BA212AB592395C.quest_desc: [
		"The tippy top of the massive &9Acropolis&r is where the &9&lScylla&r will spawn. Like the &d&lEnder Guardian&r you just need to be near to Spawn here."
		""
		"She is one of the smallest Bosses in &4&lCataclsym&r only being around 3 Blocks Tall. She has 390 &4Hearts&r and 12 Armor Points."
		""
		"Don't let her Size or lack of Buffs let you underestimate her."
		""
		"She can use her &9Anchor&r, &9Ceranus&r, to pull you closer to her from far away, or simply swing it at you to deal a ton of Damage!"
		""
		"She can toss &9Lightning Spears&r at you from her Back or from Clouds. Even leaping into the Air and Jumping back down to bring &9Lightning Strikes&r all around where she Hit."
		""
		"That's not even it! She also has control over &9Water&r allowing her to send &9Waves&r at you or even summon &9Water Snakes&r to Bite you! \\n\\nWhen slayed, she will Drop the usual Boss Gear, as well as &9Lacrima&r and &9Ess"
	]
	quest.31BA212AB592395C.title: "&9&lScylla"
	quest.320350E9961B9FB7.quest_desc: ["Keeps the player's inventory stacked up from items inside the Backpack."]
	quest.32736107FF96FDD5.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.32736107FF96FDD5.title: "&eAdvanced Void Upgrade"
	quest.3278754A04323A8F.quest_desc: [
		"&5Echo Soil&r covers the floor of the &5Echoing Forests&r."
		""
		"They do not act like normal &2Grass&r or Dirt besides allowing &5Echoing Saplings&r to grow on them."
		""
		"No normal Saplings."
	]
	quest.3278754A04323A8F.title: "&5Echo Soil"
	quest.330101F659558C7C.quest_desc: ["The Blood Mushroom Bog is home to the giant Blood Mushrooms. "]
	quest.330101F659558C7C.title: "Blood Mushroom Bog"
	quest.330370E0E9936286.quest_desc: [
		"&cGloomy Geysers&r are Blocks you can find within &cOvercast Columns&r."
		""
		"When you Walk over them they will shoot you high up into the Air! Be careful though, you'll still take Fall Damage."
		""
		"You can pick them up with Silk Touch."
	]
	quest.330370E0E9936286.title: "&cGloomy Geyser"
	quest.3314FBC4FEAE1D08.quest_desc: ["&6Deployer&r is a very fun &6Machine&r for poking! \\n\\nBy poking, I mostly mean &eItem Interactions&r that we can preform. Place an &eItem&r into the &6Deployer Hand&r, and then give it &dRotational Power&r. It will then place the &eItem&r into the Block on a &eDepot&f or &eBelt&r below. \\n\\nThis will mimick many actions that we can do, like adding &6Wax&r to &cCopper&r. \\n\\nYou'll most likely use it for &8Andesite&r/&cCopper&r/&eBrass&r Casings and &4Polished Rose Quartz&r."]
	quest.3314FBC4FEAE1D08.quest_subtitle: "Poke"
	quest.3314FBC4FEAE1D08.title: "&6Deployer"
	quest.3391FC0E046EBE66.quest_subtitle: "Halves the holder's weight."
	quest.3406D9E70BDAF11B.quest_desc: [
		"&cUtherium Armor&r has same stats as Netherite Armor! "
		""
		"Without needing a Smithing Template!"
	]
	quest.3406D9E70BDAF11B.title: "&cUtherium&r Armor"
	quest.3406E2940AF009E8.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the holder's Attack but only allows the use of one move."
	quest.3424729BC6EB3782.quest_desc: ["Just like almost every modpack, punch some trees to get wood."]
	quest.3424729BC6EB3782.title: "Got Wood?"
	quest.3453301601B6A45E.quest_subtitle: "Capture one Pokémon of each classic type: Grass, Fire, and Water"
	quest.3453301601B6A45E.title: "The Elemental Triad"
	quest.345EE595E4F66B00.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Fighting-type moves."
	quest.347F8A7896A1F487.quest_desc: [
		"I'm going to assume you've been crafting, right? It is MineCRAFT after all."
		""
		"We need to upgrade by making a Crafting Table!"
	]
	quest.347F8A7896A1F487.title: "Whats Minecraft without Crafting?"
	quest.34D055968CAB04EF.quest_subtitle: "Protective moves like Light Screen and Reflect will be effective longer."
	quest.354EE41AE7E37750.quest_subtitle: "Raises the holder's Sp. Def but prevents the use of status moves."
	quest.3557C5A899DA0D19.quest_desc: [
		"&5Tidal Claws&r are a confirmed drop from &5&lThe Leviathan&r."
		""
		"It has two modes, attack and grapple. Attack is with Left Click, Grapple is with Right Click."
		""
		"When you use its attack it will launch the claw and go through max of 5 mobs. Dealing damage and giving &5Abyssal Curse&r which will continue to damage them. "
		""
		"The grapple instead will latch on to whatever is in range and pull you toward it."
		""
		"There's no durability."
	]
	quest.3557C5A899DA0D19.title: "&5Tidal Claws"
	quest.356514DE7EE8E474.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Moonworm Queen&r is like a torch launcher. It launches &eMoonworms&r at the targeted block, which light up the block similar to a torch."
		""
		"These can be found in some &2Hollow Hill&r and &eLich Tower&r loot chests."
	]
	quest.356514DE7EE8E474.title: "&6Moonworm Queen"
	quest.3573E849E0C32F06.quest_desc: [
		"Shriek Worms spawn from stepping on &3Infested Sculk&r in &9Deeplands&r."
		""
		"They are Mini bosses with 100 &4Hearts&r."
		""
		"If you get too close they'll bite you, causing a ton of Damage! But if you go too far they'll retreat back down into the ground."
		""
		"They don't drop anything but a bit of &aXP&r."
	]
	quest.3573E849E0C32F06.title: "&bShriek Worm"
	quest.35B9A54FB1D4F99A.quest_desc: ["For just a few &eAncient Metal&r you get a Weapon that does more Damage than a Netherite Sword, has insane Range, and throws &eSandstorms&r!?"]
	quest.35B9A54FB1D4F99A.title: "&eAncient Spear"
	quest.35C2DFB38AC2EAFE.quest_desc: [
		"&aEcho Logs&r are made from &aEcho Trees&r which spawn in the... &5Echoing Forest&r"
		""
		"&aEcho Trees&r have &5Purple Leaves&r and Sculk Gleam within them. While their Logs have a &7Light Grey Bark&r and a very &aLight Green Log color&r."
		""
		"All the Planks and Wood Items made from it are all the &aLight Green Color&r, almost Mint like."
	]
	quest.35C2DFB38AC2EAFE.title: "&aEcho Trees"
	quest.360A949BEAED4DCF.quest_desc: [
		"Is that rock moving? Oh wait that isn't a rock, it's a &2Mog&r!"
		""
		"&2Mogs&r can be bred together with Depthrock Pebbles and on death might drop more Pebbles or Mogmoss!"
		""
		"Mogmoss can be used in many different recipes!"
	]
	quest.36968E551E602EEF.quest_desc: [
		"Functioning similar to a Furnace, &fThe &a&lAltar&r&f is a sacred block used to &d&lenchant items&r&f and &b&lrepair armor&r&f"
		""
		"&fIt draws its mystical power from &e&lAmbrosium Shards&r&f, so make sure to keep a steady supply nearby."
		""
		"&fWith this block, you can strengthen your gear and harness the magic of the skies."
	]
	quest.36968E551E602EEF.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCraft an &a&lAltar&r&f"
	quest.36968E551E602EEF.title: "&7&lQuest: Crafting the Altar"
	quest.3697AAF8F281B247.quest_desc: ["This one's a doozy! So listen carefully! \\n1st is constructing the actual &bSteam Engine&r. The &bFluid Tanks&r will judge how much &9Water&r can be held within it and decide the Level the &bSteam Engine&r will be at. \\n\\nThen, simply attach the &bSteam Engine&r to the side of the &bFluid Tanks&r and it'll become a &bSteam Boiler&r. After, place a &8Shaft&r on the &bSteam Engine&r to get our Mechanical Arm that will give us &dRotational Power&r from it. \\n\\n2nd is a &cHeat Source&r. We'll need a &cHeat Source&r beneath the &bFluid Tanks&r to heat up the &9Water&r. There's quite a few &cHeat Sources&r: Fire, Campfire, Lava, Magma Blocks but &cBlaze Burners&r are the best! \\n\\nThe better the &cHeat Source&r, the more Stress Units! So feed those &cBlaze Burners&r some &cBlaze Cakes&r and you'll be rocking! \\n\\n3rd is &9Water&r. This is the fuel of our &bSteam Engine&r, there wouldn't be Steam without &9Water&r."]
	quest.3697AAF8F281B247.title: "&bSteam Engine"
	quest.36D77BD95FE5CA71.quest_desc: [
		"From the ashes of the &6&lSun Spirit&r&f’s defeat, the &6&lPhoenix Armor&r&f rises, glowing with eternal flame. "
		""
		"Each piece radiates warmth and power, a reward worthy of those who have conquered the skies. Wear it proudly, hero, you have earned the fire of the heavens."
	]
	quest.36D77BD95FE5CA71.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain a piece of &6&lPhoenix Armor&r&f&l from the &6&lGold Dungeon&r&f&l"
	quest.36D77BD95FE5CA71.title: "&7&lQuest: Wings of the Phoenix"
	quest.36F6B0C9B15621CA.quest_desc: [
		"Not all Cataclysm Dungeons are as easy to find as the &eCursed Pyramids&r are."
		""
		"So, a specific Eye might help you find them!"
		""
		"Each of the different Eyes will lead you to its set structure; and don't worry, the Eyes rarely break."
	]
	quest.36F6B0C9B15621CA.title: "&2Eye of Ender"
	quest.36FF3C7B1EC40C5B.quest_desc: [
		"Froststeel spawns in the Frozen Biomes: Frostfields, Frosty Smogstem Forests, and probably Icey Seas."
		""
		"It spawns in Shiverstone which replaces Depthrock in these Biomes. The Shiverstone will act similar to Ice as in it is slippery and slows you down a little."
		""
		"You might also find some Nuggets in Munchers bellies!"
	]
	quest.36FF3C7B1EC40C5B.title: "&bFroststeel&r"
	quest.3701ABFC5F75A6A1.quest_desc: [
		"The &eWadjet&r is similar to the &eKobolediator&r as it lies within the &eCursed Pyramid&r waiting for a Player to come near."
		""
		"The &eWadjet&r has 1050 &4Hearts&r and thankfully won't give you Mining Fatigue!"
		""
		"She has many attacks, the most basic is when you are close she will swing her weapon at you. If you get farther she might throw a Sandstorm at you or drop Sand Blocks from the roof on top of you."
		""
		"On death they will only drop Ancient Metal Ingots."
	]
	quest.3701ABFC5F75A6A1.title: "&eWadjet"
	quest.372559BC727F14DC.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the Basic Storage Chapter!"
		""
		"You'll find all of the basic ways to store items without needing power, as well as useful items for your storage needs!"
	]
	quest.372559BC727F14DC.title: "Basic Storage"
	quest.373B6394A9715E63.quest_subtitle: "Praise be to the Helix!"
	quest.373B6394A9715E63.title: "The Spiral’s Secret"
	quest.374A953E77AB0D34.quest_desc: [
		"&3Cursium Armor&r is an upgrade to Netherite Armor. Combine Netherite Gear, with a &3Cursium Ingot&r, and a &3Cursium Upgrade Template&r. You can Craft those don't worry!"
		""
		"The &3Cursium Helmet&r can be used to see Mobs through Blocks! Like the Spectral Eye."
		""
		"The &3Cursium Chestplate&r works as a built in Totem of Undying. After you die you will be saved. It has a 6 minute Cooldown though..."
		""
		"The &3Cursium Leggings&r grants a chance to avoid all damage, especially from projectiles."
		""
		"The &3Cursium Boots&r allow you to get sent backwards in a leap. They also reduce Fall Damage."
	]
	quest.374A953E77AB0D34.title: "&3Cursed Armor"
	quest.37D6388CB5488F57.quest_desc: [
		"&4Munchers&r are similar to any other Hostile Mobs in the &2&lUndergarden&r, but this ones drops makes it much more useful!"
		""
		"The Muncher can drop &7Cloggrum&r and &bFroststeel Nuggets&r on death."
	]
	quest.37D6388CB5488F57.title: "&4Muncher&r"
	quest.37D883165C6C535C.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Bug-type moves."
	quest.37DE94F939A302AB.quest_desc: [
		"The &cOre Magnet&r that can pull up anything with Ore in name, except Coal."
		""
		"This can be found in &2Hollow Hill&r chests."
	]
	quest.37DE94F939A302AB.title: "&cOre Magnet"
	quest.37EA63AE64139CDA.quest_desc: ["Combining a &8Raven Feather&r with &eTorchberries&r and &6Glowstone&r will give you a &eMagic Map Focus&r."]
	quest.37EA63AE64139CDA.title: "&eMagic Map Focus"
	quest.38898FF006057D5B.quest_desc: [
		"With a &8Giant's Pickaxe&r, you'll want to head back to Troll Caves to find &5Giant Obsidian&r."
		""
		"Use the &8Giant's Pickaxe&r to break it, and you'll find some loot. Acquire the &6Lamp of Cinders&r to continue."
	]
	quest.38898FF006057D5B.title: "&6Lamp of Cinders"
	quest.38AFA6DD6258FB34.quest_desc: ["&fBy combining it with &b&lIcestone&r&f, you can create frozen accessories like the &b&lIce Pendant&r&f or &b&lIce Ring&r&f, items that grant protection and power drawn from the cold skies themselves."]
	quest.38AFA6DD6258FB34.quest_subtitle: "&f&lUse a &b&lFreezer&r&f &land &b&lIcestone&r&f &lto freeze an accessory, obtain an &b&lIce Pendant&r&f &lor &b&lIce Ring&r&f"
	quest.38AFA6DD6258FB34.title: "&7&lQuest: Frozen Finesse"
	quest.38CB5044AB3F859B.quest_desc: ["&aSuper Glue&r is used to attach Blocks together! In order to move them with &aContraptions&r. \\n\\nTo &aGlue&r Blocks together, Right Click two different Blocks and all between them will be &aGlued&r. If you want to &aUnglue&r them, just Left Click them with the &aSuper-Glue&r. \\n\\nThere is some requirements though, each Block must be connected to the other ones and not diagonally. \\n\\nYou can also combine other &aGlued&r Blocks to different &aGlued&r Blocks. Everyone gets &aGlue&r! \\n\\nPlus this will effect other Blocks near the originally &aGlued&r one. Blocks adjacent to &aGlued&r Blocks will be moved with them. Same with Blocks that are attached to &aGlued&r Blocks, like Torches or Signs."]
	quest.38CB5044AB3F859B.title: "&aSuper-Glue"
	quest.38DA514ACD9F30F0.quest_desc: ["Hate exploring many different Biomes to get all the different Tree Saplings? Well most of them are in the Dense Forest!"]
	quest.38DA514ACD9F30F0.title: "Dense Forest"
	quest.3936090B6A2E10AB.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bloom Berries&r grow from &bGlowing Vines&r on the roof of the &bBlooming Caverns&r."
		""
		"Within the &bGlowing Vines&r, &6Bloom Berries&r might spawn and will wait for you to pick them off the &bVine&r with Right Click!"
		""
		"This is the only Food Source in the &3&lOtherside&r"
	]
	quest.3936090B6A2E10AB.title: "&6Bloom Berries"
	quest.39623952B782F878.quest_desc: [
		"&fThe &c&lCreaking&r&f is a haunting creature bound to the Creaking Heart. It awakens when you look at it at night within the Pale Garden."
		""
		"&fIt freezes when observed, but attack it and its heart will respond with resin and rage. Face the Creaking but don't look away."
	]
	quest.39623952B782F878.quest_subtitle: "&f&lFind or spawn a &c&lCreaking&r&f&l mob at night"
	quest.39623952B782F878.title: "&6&lQuest: Encounter the Creaking"
	quest.397568448DE5DAD5.quest_desc: [
		"Once you've gathered enough Ender Pearls and Blaze Powder, you can make your way to the End Portal in the Overworld."
		""
		"To do this, craft some &dEyes of Ender&r and right click to throw them in the sky. These will point in the direction of the closest End Portal."
		""
		"Make your way to the Stronghold, find the End Portal, and complete the frame using the Eyes of Ender to create the portal to &dThe End&r."
	]
	quest.397568448DE5DAD5.title: "&aFinding &dThe End"
	quest.39A7619B4C5592BE.quest_desc: ["&bItem Drains&r are what we can use to mass extract &bFluid&r from &eItems&r! \\n\\nIf a Bottle or Bucket is thrown on top of the &bDrain&r: either by Belts, Chutes, or Hands, the &bFluid&r will be emptied into the &bDrain&r. \\n\\nThe now empty &eItem&r will then be pushed off the &bDrain&r in the opposite direction, and the &bFluid&r will be sitting in the &bDrain&r waiting to be &bPiped&r out."]
	quest.39A7619B4C5592BE.title: "&bItem Drain"
	quest.39AC7D505ACC858F.quest_subtitle: "The holder's type immunities are removed."
	quest.3A4C62865C7CC862.quest_desc: ["&bFluid Tanks&r can hold &bFluids&r. Like Chests, but for &9Water&r and such! \\n\\nYou can only Input &bFluids&r with Buckets but with &bPipes&r you can Input and Output &bFluids&r from them. \\n\\nEach &bFluid Tank&r can hold 8 Buckets or 8000mB of &bFluid&r. But that number will rise when we combine them! \\n\\nYes, you heard me right! We can place multiple &bFluid Tanks&r next to each other to connect their Inventories. They will stack when placed on top of each other up to 32, or by 2x2 or 3x3."]
	quest.3A4C62865C7CC862.title: "&bFluid Tanks"
	quest.3A4E09928A966978.quest_desc: [
		"&l&2Poison&r&f is not just a hazard in the Aether, it is also a mysterious tool for transformation."
		""
		"&fBy tossing certain items into poison, they will slowly mutate into new, enchanted forms."
		""
		"&fExperiment with what you throw in and you may uncover the Aether’s alchemical secrets."
		""
		"&f&lExamples of Transformations"
		""
		"- &6&lGolden Dart&r&f ➜ &d&lEnchanted Dart&r&f"
		""
		"- &a&lSkyroot Poison Bucket&r&f ➜ &a&lSkyroot Remedy Bucket&r&f"
		""
		"- &7&lHolystone&r&f ➜ &a&lHealing Stone&r&f"
		""
		"- &7&lQuicksoil&r&f ➜ &7&lQuicksoil Glass&r&f"
		""
		"- &9&lBlue Berry&r&f ➜ &d&lEnchanted Berry&r&f"
		""
		"- &d&lGravitite Ore&r&f ➜ &d&lEnchanted Gravitite&r&f"
		""
		"- &5&lPurple&r&f or &a&lGreen Squash&r&f ➜ &9&lBlue Squash&r&f"
		""
		"&f&lTip"
		""
		"&fTry tossing enchantable or Aether-infused items, you might discover something magical."
	]
	quest.3A4E09928A966978.quest_subtitle: "&f&lTransform an item by throwing it into &2&lPoison&r&f"
	quest.3A4E09928A966978.title: "&7&lQuest: Alchemical Corruption"
	quest.3A6E12CEF3A0EB7C.quest_subtitle: "Gradually restores the holder's HP throughout a battle."
	quest.3A8E27514EFE2B20.quest_desc: [
		"Within the &2Dark Forest&r, you'll find the &8Dark Tower&r."
		""
		"To enter, look for the reappearing blocks at the base. Find your way through the maze all the way to the final floor to fight the &cUr-Ghast&r."
		""
		"The &cUr-Ghast&r is recommended to kill with a ranged weapon. There are 4 Ghast traps found on the boss floor, which can be used to damage the &cUr-Ghast&r."
		""
		"These are charged with &cGhastling&r kills, then activating with Redstone. You don't have to use them, but they can prove useful."
	]
	quest.3A8E27514EFE2B20.quest_subtitle: "Dark Carmonite Tower"
	quest.3A8E27514EFE2B20.title: "&cTears of Fire"
	quest.3AF2BC9A0E298882.quest_desc: ["With our &8Andesite Alloys&r we can now make &8Andesite Casing&r. \\n\\nGet some Wood, Strip it with an Axe, and then Right Click the Stripped Wood with the &8Andesite Alloy&r. \\n\\nThat will give us our &8Andesite Casing&r! \\n\\n&8Andesite Casing&r will be needed for many, many, many &6Machines&r! And looks good for decoration."]
	quest.3AF2BC9A0E298882.title: "&6&lMachines"
	quest.3B320591EDF16C35.quest_subtitle: "Doubles an untransformed Ditto's speed."
	quest.3B33173D91869019.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Ground-type moves."
	quest.3B3B38B17CF5D81C.quest_desc: ["&ePackage Frogports&r are adorable and helpful &6Machines&r used for mixing &ePackages&f and &8Chain Conveyors&r! \\n\\nFirst, Right Click a part of the &8Chain &fon a &8Chain Conveyor&r with the &eFrogport&r in Hand, this will set it as the &eFrogports&r destination. \\n\\nThen, when placed we can mess with its GUI. Here we can change the name of its Address, determine whether it takes and gives &ePackages&r or just gives &ePackages&r. \\n\\nThey have 18 Slots to Hold &ePackages&r for moving. \\n\\nIf the Address of the &ePackage&r doesn't match the Address you gave the &eFrogport&f, the &eFrogport&r will send the &ePackage&r onto the &8Chain Conveyor&r. \\n\\nIf it matches the Address, the &ePackage&r will be taken into the &eFrogport&r. If there is no matching Address the &ePackage&r will just go in circles! \\n\\n&ePackages&r can also be automatically sent and taken from &eFrogports&r with &eFunnels &fand &eBelts&r."]
	quest.3B3B38B17CF5D81C.title: "&ePackage Frogport"
	quest.3B6595DA92AA9C56.quest_desc: ["Auto-swaps to the tool that is most effective for the block you are looking at."]
	quest.3B8E3479C31FE2CE.quest_desc: [
		"Wigglewood Forests are forests like all others."
		""
		"Just these Trees like to go as they please."
	]
	quest.3B8E3479C31FE2CE.title: "Wigglewood Forest"
	quest.3C156F322DA83424.quest_desc: ["The &aSeeker Bow&r is dropped from the &3Snow Queen&r, it can shoot Arrows that home in on your targets. No more missing!"]
	quest.3C156F322DA83424.quest_subtitle: "Skill Issue?"
	quest.3C156F322DA83424.title: "&aSeeker Bow"
	quest.3C28D3DBE7866927.quest_desc: [
		"The &cCarminite Builders&r, when powered with a Redstone signal, will generate temporary blocks in the direction the signal came from."
		""
		"The &cCarminite Reactor&r will convert nearby Obsidian and Netherack into &eFalse Gold&r and &3False Diamond&r. After a short period of time, this will suck up nearby blocks and explode, creating &cCarminite Ghastlings&r around it."
	]
	quest.3C28D3DBE7866927.title: "&cCarmanite Builders \\& Reactors"
	quest.3C7B8A3B411F9E9E.quest_desc: [
		"The next step of progression is to make an Iron Pickaxe."
		""
		"This pickaxe can mine some of the rarer ores in the game, like Diamond!"
	]
	quest.3C7B8A3B411F9E9E.title: "An &aIron&r Pick"
	quest.3C892B33758B7BA6.quest_desc: ["&dCogs &fand &dLarge Cogs&r can interact with each other to change Speed and Stress! \\n\\nIf you connect a &dCog&r, diagonally from a &dLarge Cog&r, the &dCog&r will double in Speed! This is because the &dLarge Cog&r has more Teeth than the &dCog&r, it takes longer to take a full &dRotation&r. \\n\\nThis also works in the reverse, if you put a &dLarge Cog&r diagonal to a &dCog&r, the &dLarge Cog&r will spin at half Speed. \\n\\nThese will also change the Stress Units from the &dCogs&r. More Speed, more Stress. Less Speed, less Stress."]
	quest.3C892B33758B7BA6.title: "&dCog&r Teamwork!"
	quest.3C8E8B4390AC5067.quest_desc: [
		"The medium sized &cRot Mob&r, the &cRotwalker&r."
		""
		"They have 20 Hearts."
		""
		"Like all &cRot Mobs&r they will target &2Stoneborns&r and &7Forgottens&r and will drop &cUtheric Shards&r."
	]
	quest.3C8E8B4390AC5067.title: "&cRotwalker&r"
	quest.3C9120CC0D9FA31B.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the holder's Special Attack but only allows the use of one move."
	quest.3C99017FD32B6DE2.quest_desc: [
		"&eBrass Casings&r are made the same way as &8Andesite&r and &cCopper Casings&r. Just apply the &eItem&r to Stripped Wood. \\n\\nBut with &eBrass Casings&r giving us some of the most powerful &6Machines&r, it won't be as easy to get as &8Andesite&r or &cCopper&r. "
		""
		"The &6&lCreate&r way would be to throw a &cCopper Ingot&r and &7Zinc Ingot&r into a &8Basin&r below a &6Mechanical Mixer&r, while the &8Basin&r is heated."
	]
	quest.3C99017FD32B6DE2.title: "&eBrass Casing"
	quest.3CA4F8C991EE32CE.quest_subtitle: "Allows the holder to immediately use a move that normally requires a change of turn to charge. Consumed after use."
	quest.3CB88AC2AE85C01A.quest_desc: [
		"You'll have to fight the &bIgnited Revenant&r first to get &bBurning Ashes&r."
		""
		"Once you have them, use them on the Altar of Fire to summon the &b&lIgnis&r."
	]
	quest.3CB88AC2AE85C01A.title: "&bBurning Ashes"
	quest.3D08570C4079F00E.quest_subtitle: "Bring back a prehistoric powerhouse!"
	quest.3D08570C4079F00E.title: "The Skull of Power"
	quest.3D2A03EB2B91E9C1.quest_desc: ["These are literally just fancy Hoppers. \\n\\nThey connect two Inventories, bringing &eItems&r from the Top one to the Bottom one. \\n\\n&eChutes&r can connect to each other, even diagonally. \\n\\nYou can also use them with &6Fans&r to shoot &eItems&r up the &eChutes&r!"]
	quest.3D2A03EB2B91E9C1.title: "&eChute"
	quest.3D502928A932BCD3.quest_desc: ["The Dimension known for housing the piglins and blazes and wither skeletons, now houses 2 more bosses to fight!"]
	quest.3D502928A932BCD3.title: "&4Nether&r"
	quest.3D8812A674B33831.quest_desc: [
		"&9Cindaria&r are Jellyfish/Human Mobs that protect &9Acropolis&r. They are Greenish/Purple-ish and transparent."
		""
		"They have 60 &4Hearts&r with no Armor."
		""
		"They also wield what looks like an Umbrella but is actually a deadly Weaon!"
		""
		"If you are too close, they'll swing their Weapon to Hit you with it. If you are farther, they will Shoot a &9Lightning Spear&r at you."
		""
		"&9Lightning Spears&r bounce off Walls, thankfully the &9Acropolis&r doesn't have many of those!"
		""
		"On Death, the &9Cindaria&r will Drop &9Lacrima&r."
	]
	quest.3D8812A674B33831.title: "&9Cindaria"
	quest.3E9013E96D1FDCE4.quest_desc: [
		"Overhauled Creepers gives us many different varients of Creepers for different Biomes. "
		""
		"Each have different drops and even some are friendly! "
		""
		"All are afraid of cats though..."
	]
	quest.3E9013E96D1FDCE4.title: "Creeper Variants"
	quest.3E914002223CD090.quest_desc: [
		"This is a Backpack upgrade so you can put your Backpack in your Backpack."
		""
		"So you can have your Backpack in your Backpack for when you need your Backpack in your Backpack."
	]
	quest.3EE11737783B3C36.quest_desc: [
		"&2Stoneborns&r are the perfect mix of Villagers and Iron Golems."
		""
		"You can trade with them by Right Clicking them. "
		""
		"And they will fight off Hostile Mobs (or Players who hit them)."
	]
	quest.3EE11737783B3C36.title: "&2Stoneborn&r"
	quest.3EF07A656BFDCDA9.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the damage of the holder's super effective moves by 20%."
	quest.3F02EF19112D23BE.quest_desc: ["You'll need &6Mechanical Crafters&r to make the &6Crushing Wheels&r, they are too big for a 3x3 Crafting Table. You'll also need a ton of &8Andesite Alloys&r. \\n\\nBTW, you'll need 2 to actually use them. \\nOnce you have 2, place them next to each other. Then, feed them both &dRotational Power&r and a lot of Stress Units. \\n\\nMake sure that the &6Crushing Wheels&r are spinning in opposite directions or else it won't &6Crush&r! The left one must be spinning &e&oClockwise&r, and the right one must spin &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r. \\n\\nOnce they are spinning (fast and in the right directions) you can have &eItems&r Dropped in between them and they will be &6Crushed&r. \\n\\nWhat &eItems&r? &6Crushed&r Ores from Ores, &eItems&r from Stones and Netherrack, Sand and Flint from Gravel, and even Netherwart from Netherwart Blocks!"]
	quest.3F02EF19112D23BE.title: "&6Crushing Wheels"
	quest.3F2C1A81C17D2D67.quest_desc: ["&6Mechanical Arms&r must be configured before Placing them, like the &eWeighted Ejector&r. \\n\\nIt has a 4 Block Range and can pick up from &eBelts &fand &eDepots&r. It can also deposit into &eBelts&f, &eDepots&f, and &eFunnels&r. \\nWhile Holding the &6Mechanical Arm&r, Right Click Blocks to set as Input, then Click again to change it to Output. You can Left Click to deselect the Blocks. You can select as many are in range! \\n\\nOnce it has &dRotational Power&r, an &eItem&r in any Input Block, and space in any Output Block, it will start moving &eItems&r. It will go faster the more Speed is given to it. \\n\\nLike the &eBrass Tunnel&r, the &6Mechanical Arm&r has Distribution Modes. Thankfully a lot less! Round Robin: will go in order for Inputs and Outputs. Forced Round Robin: will wait until every Output has space or every Input has &eItems&r available. Prefer First Target: will go for the closest Block to it."]
	quest.3F2C1A81C17D2D67.quest_subtitle: "Why do it yourself when Robot can do it better?"
	quest.3F2C1A81C17D2D67.title: "&6Mechanical Arm"
	quest.3F663416E824720C.quest_desc: ["&cCopper Casings&r will be needed for most Machines involved in &bFluid Logistics&r. \\n\\nYou wanna place &9Water&r? You'll need &cCopper Casings&r. You wanna pick up &9Water&r? You'll need &cCopper Casings&r. \\n\\nThey are made just like &8Andesite Casings&r, apply a &cCopper Ingot&r to a Stripped Log."]
	quest.3F663416E824720C.title: "&cCopper Casings"
	quest.3F6711A2E5D569AD.quest_desc: [
		"...is not implemented."
		""
		"There is a Kobold that spawns in as a \"placeholder\" but you will get nothing from killing it."
	]
	quest.3F6711A2E5D569AD.quest_subtitle: "Final Castle"
	quest.3F6711A2E5D569AD.title: "&cThe Final Boss"
	quest.3F924F02594FF3CE.quest_desc: [
		"&fThe &c&lGrim Reaper&r&f is the ultimate challenge in &6&lMinecraft Comes Alive: Reborn&r&f. It can be summoned by lighting the &d&lGrim Altar&r&f, but only under the right conditions."
		""
		"&fTo begin the ritual, all three &a&lObsidian Pillars&r&f must be lit before igniting the &b&lEmerald Block&r&f at the center. Make sure it is nighttime, otherwise you'll receive the message \"The Reaper fears the sunlight.\""
		""
		"&fWhen defeated, the Grim Reaper drops his legendary weapon, the &c&lScythe&r&f, capable of &a&lKilling fallen villagers&r&f at the cost of life drain."
		""
		"&fYour legend can also be upgraded into the &a&lStaff of Life&r&f."
		""
		"&fFace this legendary foe and reclaim the power of death itself!"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lBoss Fight Details:"
		""
		"&fThe Grim Reaper has &c&l200 HP&r&f and &a&lregenerate 4 HP every 5 seconds&r&f. He can fly, cast spells, and wield &5&lDark Magic&r&f. Because he is skilled as an &5&lInfernal Smite&r&f enchantment, this is particularly effective against him."
		""
		"&f&lAttacks:"
		""
		"&f&l■ &c&lBlock&r&f: Raises his scythe to nullify all incoming damage, then &a&lteleports a short distance away&r&f."
		"→ &e&lTip&r&f: Wait for this phase to end before attacking again."
		""
		"&f&l■ &c&lSlash&r&f: &a&lCharges forward&r&f with his scythe, dealing &c&lunblockable damage&r&f and applying the Wither effect."
		"→ &e&lTip&r&f: Strafe sideways and counterattack quickly."
		""
		"&f&l■ &c&lLightning Strike&r&f: &a&lHovers and calls down lightning&r&f every 5-10 seconds. Lightning may summon armored &c&lzombies or skeletons&r&f."
		"→ &e&lTip&r&f: Keep moving, spawned mobs have low health from lightning fire."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lVictory:"
		""
		"&fUpon defeating the &c&lGrim Reaper&r&f, you'll obtain the &c&lScythe&r&f, a weapon of immense dark power. With it, you can choose to balance life and death itself, or pursue the light by forging the &a&lStaff of Life&r&f."
		""
		"&fYour actions will define the fate of your village and its people."
	]
	quest.3F924F02594FF3CE.quest_subtitle: "&f&lFace and defeat the &c&lGrim Reaper&r&f - a powerful undead boss that guards the line between life and death&r"
	quest.3F924F02594FF3CE.title: "&6&lQuest: Defeat the Grim Reaper"
	quest.3F982CC960236117.quest_desc: [
		"&f&6&lVanilla Backport&r&f brings modern Minecraft features to older versions, adding new biomes, mobs, blocks, and mechanics for a richer world."
		""
		"&fExplore &a&lChase the Skies&r&f with new heights, discover &a&lThe Garden Awakens&r&f with fresh flora, watch nature &a&lSpring to Life&r&f with vibrant growth, and embark on adventures with &a&lBundles of Bravery&r&f to carry your journey."
		""
		"&fYour classic Minecraft world just got a massive upgrade."
	]
	quest.3F982CC960236117.quest_subtitle: "&f&lBegin your adventure and explore the new features brought by &6&lVanilla Backport&r&f&l"
	quest.3F9D6124093AA4A5.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Clawdian&r is the miniboss of &9Acropolis&r."
		""
		"They are huge lobsters who hold an even bigger Axe! "
		""
		"They have 225 &4Hearts&r and 12 Armor Points."
		""
		"They like to use their Axe and Feet to Attack you. From swinging their Axe at you to do moderate Damage. To smashing the ground with an Axe to unleash a Shockwave. To stomping on the ground to unleash an even bigger Shockwave and &9Waves&r at you!"
		""
		"If you get too far they'll charge after you, Breaking Blocks in their way! "
		""
		"If you can Kill one, they'll Drop their &9Claw&r! Kinda graphic but thankfully it's just fantasy violence!"
	]
	quest.3F9D6124093AA4A5.title: "&9Clawdian"
	quest.3FBCBBEBB78B83FC.quest_desc: ["Finally make a &5Train&r! \\n\\nWe should have our &5Boogeys&r from the &5Train Station&r Quest, no the design of &5Boogey&r doesn't matter. \\n\\nThen, we can place Blocks onto the &5Boogey&r with &aSuper-Glue&r. It doesn't matter what Blocks, pretty much any Block that can be moved can be &aGlued&r! \\n\\nThis is when you try and make it look pretty! Check out Artwork-Builds Showoff in Discord to see a few of them. \\n\\nThe most important Block for our &5Train&r is the &5Train Controls&r. You'll need one in order to actually move the &5Train&r. \\n\\nYou can also add a &5Seat&r for &5Conductors&r (more on that later) or even yourself! \\n\\nOnce it is all ready, just hit \"Assemble Train\" and either your &5Train&r will be made, or it will tell you what you did wrong!"]
	quest.3FBCBBEBB78B83FC.title: "Constructing &5Trains"
	quest.404234754B44487A.quest_subtitle: "Grounds the holder, and halves their speed."
	quest.404D7C001E6B24A4.quest_desc: [
		"Defeating the Alpha Yeti unlocks the &9Glacier&r biome. Here, you'll find cute little Penguins and the &3Snow Queen&r."
		""
		"At the top of the &bAurora Palace&r, the &3Snow Queen&r will summon Ice crystals to protect herself."
		""
		"She'll also slam &3Ice&r down that can destroy the floor and deal massive damage."
		""
		"You'll only be able to hit her top half, as she's protected by &3Ice&r."
		""
		"After defeating the &3Snow Queen&r, you'll unlock access to the &2Highlands&r."
	]
	quest.404D7C001E6B24A4.title: "&bClear Skies"
	quest.4050B36FBA989FE7.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Electric-type moves."
	quest.4057EC9E1B4E3AF3.quest_desc: [
		"&3The &bImmolator&r is an &3Annihilator&r upgraded with an &bIgnitium Ingot&r within the &4Mechanical Fusion Anvil&r."
		""
		"These do more Damage to Mobs with &bBlazing Brand&r afflicted on them, so &bBlazing Grips&r work pretty well with it!"
		""
		"If you have &3The &bImmolator&r in each Hand, you can Hold right Click to summon a &bFlame Strike&r beneath you. This will Damage all Mobs in it and explode when done as a final farewell!"
	]
	quest.4057EC9E1B4E3AF3.title: "&3The &bImmolator"
	quest.406F193B99BC418B.quest_desc: [
		"You can try your luck at trying to catch a Pokémon by simply throwing a Pokéball at them, but odd are that isn't going to work. (Just right click while holding a Pokéball)."
		""
		"You need to battle and weaken them to have a higher chance at catching them. "
		""
		"Press &6R&r when given the prompt to start a battle."
		""
		"FUN FACT: You can not catch a Pokémon whose health has hit zero so be careful."
	]
	quest.406F193B99BC418B.quest_subtitle: "Time to put those Poké Balls to use! Catch your first Pokémon and expand your team."
	quest.406F193B99BC418B.title: "Catch Your First Pokémon"
	quest.4071F0E8A666EDBA.quest_desc: ["The &dEye of Void&r will take you to the &dRuined Citadel&r to fight the &d&lEnder Guardian&r."]
	quest.4071F0E8A666EDBA.title: "&dEye of Void&r"
	quest.408692315A333A38.quest_desc: ["Adds a Smithing Table GUI to the Backpack."]
	quest.40A8CEC25BBA4737.quest_desc: [
		"&eBrutes&r spawn in a few Biomes and are Neutral."
		""
		"If hit, all in the area will attack you. Similar to Wolves or Zombified Piglins."
		""
		"On death they might drop their Tusks, which can act as a replacement for Bones!"
	]
	quest.40A8CEC25BBA4737.title: "&eBrutes&r"
	quest.40B86B9167AA213D.quest_desc: [
		"Sculk Gleam has properties of Shroomlights. They don't need a Tool to collect, but break fastest with a Hoe."
		""
		"They spawn within &5Echoing Trees&r and rarely underground."
	]
	quest.40D01496C185337C.quest_desc: [
		"The &cOvercast Columns&r are much more Hot and &6Orange&r than any other Biome here."
		""
		"Here &3Sculk&r is replaced with &cGloomy Sculk&r and &3Sculk Stone&r is replaced with &cGloomslate&r."
		""
		"You'll also find Soul Sand/Soil plus &cMagma &fwith &cLava&r beneath them."
		""
		"With the temperatures being so Hot, Mobs won't normally spawn here, but there is a few Plant life! "
	]
	quest.40D01496C185337C.title: "&cOvercast Columns"
	quest.413736C5BC03A506.quest_subtitle: "Boosts Clamperl's Sp. Def stat."
	quest.414CB75FA5B3C348.quest_desc: [
		"&3Sculk Tendrils&r are like &bTwisting Vines&r... just &3Sculky&r."
		""
		"They spawn rarely in &9Deeplands&r."
	]
	quest.414CB75FA5B3C348.title: "&3Sculk Tendrils"
	quest.4193D20E7A36E5B4.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.4193D20E7A36E5B4.title: "&eAdvanced Pickup Upgrade"
	quest.4194397DFD0199C2.quest_desc: ["&6Mechanical Crafters&r can be used for &6Auto-Crafting&r and Recipes that are bigger than 3x3 Crafting Grid like the &6Crushing Wheel&r. \\n\\nPlace the &6Mechanical Crafters&r in the order that is needed, then you'll need to set which direction the &eItems&r in the recipe go. \\n\\nThe direction is known by the arrows on the edge of the &6Crafters&r. These can be changed by Right Clicking them with a &6Wrench&r! \\n\\nThen, just place &eItems&r into the &6Mechanical Crafters&r either with your Hands or automated with &eFunnels&r. \\n\\nAfter that, you can supply &dRotational Power&r to any of the &6Mechanical Crafters&r (they share &dCogs&r) to start up the Recipes. \\n\\nIf it isn't working, check to make sure every &eItem&r is in, every arrow is facing the right way, and it has enough &dRotational Power&r."]
	quest.4194397DFD0199C2.title: "&6Mechanical Crafter"
	quest.41C9DD56E8D75C45.quest_subtitle: "Allows the holder to receive a share of experience from battles without participating."
	quest.41D262A6435A1999.quest_subtitle: "The Final Upgrade"
	quest.41D262A6435A1999.title: "&dNetherite Backpack"
	quest.41DDC75C554F8997.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Ghost-type moves."
	quest.41FCA68CFAE18676.quest_desc: [
		"The &eLich Tower&r is home to the &eLich&r! "
		""
		"The fight has 3 phases:"
		""
		"Phase 1: The &eLich&r surrounds himself in shields, and attacks you with &5Ender Pearls&r that shoot out like Ghast fireballs. Reflect them back to the &eLich&r to break his shields! As his shields break, he'll send out duplicates to distract you."
		""
		"Phase 2: The &eLich&r switches scepters to summon Zombies to help him in the fight. With his defenses down, you will be able to melee him!"
		""
		"Phase 3: Once all of the charges are spent on his Scepter, he will switch to a &eGolden Sword&r and go berserk. Kill him fast!"
	]
	quest.41FCA68CFAE18676.title: "&eBring out your Dead"
	quest.4261F296518AEC06.quest_desc: [
		"&bIgnitium&r is an upgrade for Netherite. You'll need an &bIgnitium Upgrade&r which is Crafted, and an &bIgnitium Ingot&r which is dropped from the &b&lIgnis&r."
		""
		"The &bIgnitium Helmet&r allows you to see clearly under Lava."
		""
		"The &bIgnitium Chestplate&r can combined with an Elytra."
		""
		"The &bIgnitium Leggings&r don't make us flame-proof, rather the Fires that are covering our bodies will go out quicker!"
		""
		"The &bIgnitium Boots&r allow us to walk over Lava. Like Leather Boots over Powdered Snow, you can Hold Shift to lower into the Lava."
	]
	quest.4261F296518AEC06.title: "&bIgnitium Armor"
	quest.4285510271B5223D.quest_desc: ["The &dGearbox&r is helpful for sending &dRotational Power&r in a whole bunch of different directions! \\n\\nThe normal &dGearbox&r will have 4 internal &8Shafts&r, on each of the Cardinal Directions: North, East, South, and West. \\n\\nThe other &8Shafts&r will match the Speed and Stress Units but they will also spin in different directions from the original &8Shaft&r."]
	quest.4285510271B5223D.title: "&dGearbox"
	quest.42DA53B9CE3A642B.quest_desc: ["&3Cursium&r is a rare and powerful crafting material. It can only be obtained by defeating Maledictus"]
	quest.42DA53B9CE3A642B.title: "&3 Cursium Ingot"
	quest.43062245C125CFF2.quest_desc: [
		"&aForgotten Ingots&r need to be obtained through the Catacombs; whether it be looting the Chests or killing the &aForgotten Guardian&r."
		""
		"You'll also need a Smithing Template which is found in Catacomb Chests."
	]
	quest.43062245C125CFF2.title: "&aForgotten&r"
	quest.430FF58A005E5F60.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 79"
	quest.430FF58A005E5F60.title: "Rocket Admin Archer"
	quest.431203B67CD4DF70.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Psychic-type moves."
	quest.4314BAEB72A6ADB4.quest_desc: ["The &bDiamond Minotaur Axe&r is dropped by the &cMinoshroom&r. It deals more damage when the user is sprinting."]
	quest.4314BAEB72A6ADB4.title: "&bMinotaur Axe"
	quest.431E229F5492B60B.quest_desc: [
		"Deep in the heart of the &6&lGold Dungeon&r&f waits the &6&lSun Spirit&r&f, final guardian of the &b&lAether&r&f."
		""
		"He has &c&l500 health&r&f and can shoot Fire Crystals and Ice Crystals."
		""
		"Each time he takes damage, a Fire Minion spawns."
		"  "
		"Prove your worth by defeating him and claim your &6&lGold Key&r&f, &a&l4 levels of experience&r&f, and &6&l1 Sun Altar&r&f as proof of your victory.  "
	]
	quest.431E229F5492B60B.quest_subtitle: "&f&lDefeat the mighty &6&lSun Spirit&r&f&l within the &6&lGold Dungeon&r&f&l"
	quest.431E229F5492B60B.title: "&7&lQuest: Defeat the Gold Boss"
	quest.4395428BD0F7DC74.quest_desc: ["Compacts items in the Backpack to their 2x2 recipe."]
	quest.43E7CE2AC8D7193F.quest_desc: [
		"&bBlooming Stems&r aren't like Trees, they're more like if Chorus and Bamboo had a baby."
		""
		"They spawn within the &bBlooming Caverns&r and need other &bBlooming Stems&r to keep up! This is the only way to find them. "
		""
		"You can still Strip them or make Planks out of them. The Planks have a &bLight Blue color&r to them, and so will whatever you make out of them!"
	]
	quest.43E7CE2AC8D7193F.title: "&bBlooming Wood"
	quest.4409F73A5CD4C76D.quest_desc: [
		"&fThe &b&lBlueprint&r&f is an essential tool for every village leader in &6&lMinecraft Comes Alive: Reborn&r&f. It allows you to view, organize, and control various aspects of your village, from buildings and villagers to &a&ltaxes and rules&r&f."
		""
		"&fTo craft it, place &f&l8 Paper&r&f around the edges of the crafting grid and &b&l1 Blue Dye&r&f in the center."
		""
		"&fOnce crafted, right-click to open its management interface and begin shaping your settlement."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lBlueprint Interface Overview:"
		""
		"&fLeft Menu Options:"
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lMap&r&f: Displays a visual map of all village buildings."
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lRank&r&f: Shows your current player rank."
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lCatalog&r&f: Lists all building types recognized by villagers."
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lVillagers&r&f: Displays all village inhabitants."
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lRules&r&f: Manage tax rates, birth limits, and age restrictions."
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lRefresh&r&f: Updates all displayed village data."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&fRight Menu Options:"
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lAdd Room:&r&f Register a new room as a building."
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lRemove Building:&r&f Delete a registered building."
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lAdvanced:&r&f Access additional configuration tools."
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lAuto Scan:&r&f Automatically register buildings entered by villagers."
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lRestrict Access:&r&f Prevent certain villagers from entering specific buildings."
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&lRename Village:&r&f Rename your village once you own at least four buildings."
		""
		"&fUse the Blueprint to grow your community, manage its rules, and ensure a thriving and organized village."
	]
	quest.4409F73A5CD4C76D.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCraft a &b&lBlueprint&r&f to manage and monitor your village's growth and structure&r"
	quest.4409F73A5CD4C76D.title: "&6&lQuest: Craft the Blueprint"
	quest.440D187BF3731165.quest_desc: ["The &bEye of Flame&r will take you to the &bBurning Arena&r to fight the &b&lIgnis&r."]
	quest.440D187BF3731165.title: "&bEye of Flame&r"
	quest.442C288B7870FC00.quest_subtitle: "The First Upgrade"
	quest.442C288B7870FC00.title: "&6Copper Backpack"
	quest.442D915CFB378BB4.quest_desc: ["Auto-smelt items in the Backpack."]
	quest.442D915CFB378BB4.title: "&eAuto-Smoking Upgrade"
	quest.443EE62FF3CA772A.quest_desc: ["Do I really need to explain the &2Overworld&r to you?"]
	quest.443EE62FF3CA772A.title: "&2Overworld&r"
	quest.4456AF3DAA9CC4DB.quest_desc: ["&cUtherium&r Tools are similar to Diamond Tools but the weapons are more effective to &cRot Mobs&r!"]
	quest.4456AF3DAA9CC4DB.title: "&cUtheric&r Tools"
	quest.446275591A376A2F.quest_desc: ["Yeti Armor can be crafted with Alpha Yeti Fur."]
	quest.446275591A376A2F.title: "Yeti Armor"
	quest.44CAA56576C89AA6.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of moves used consecutively."
	quest.455242BED131E26D.quest_desc: [
		"&fTo begin your adventure among the clouds, you will first need to open the gateway to the &b&lAether&r&f, a realm high above the Overworld."
		""
		"&fUnlike a Nether Portal, this one glows with heavenly energy and hums with the sound of wind through clouds."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lHow to Build the Portal"
		""
		"&fYou will need:"
		""
		"&f&e&lGlowstone Blocks&r&f - at least 10, to form a rectangular frame (just like a Nether Portal)."
		""
		"&f&b&lWater Bucket&r&f - this will serve as your “flint and steel” for activation."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lA New Beginning"
		""
		"&fAs you emerge in the &b&lAether&r&f, you will find yourself surrounded by floating islands of &b&lSkyroot&r&f and &7&lHolystone&r&f."
		""
		"&fFrom this point forward, your survival depends on your courage and curiosity, the &d&lHostile Paradise&r&f awaits."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lPro Tip"
		""
		"&fBring plenty of building blocks and food before entering, resources are different in the &b&lAether&r&f, and falling means an express trip back to the Overworld"
	]
	quest.455242BED131E26D.quest_subtitle: "&f&lConstruct and activate a &e&lGlowstone Portal&r&f&l to enter the &b&lAether&r&f&l dimension"
	quest.455242BED131E26D.title: "&7&lQuest: Entering the Aether"
	quest.456A96E84EC0780A.quest_desc: ["Now that you have a fossil, it's time to analyze it! The Monitor will help identify the species hidden within the ancient remains."]
	quest.456A96E84EC0780A.quest_subtitle: "What secrets does this fossil hold?"
	quest.456A96E84EC0780A.title: "Analyzing the Fossil"
	quest.459BA85E48B343AE.quest_desc: ["&aRadial Chasis&r work similar to &aLinear Chasis&r in connecting to other &aRadial Chasis&r but everything else changes. \\n\\nYou can connect other &aRadial Chasis&r on the top or bottom of other ones and they will automatically connect. \\n\\nThen, &aGlue&r the sides of the &aRadial Chasis&r to &aGlue&r every Block within a set Radius of the &aChasis&r. BTW Radius means circle! \\n\\nYou can change how far the circle goes with a &6Wrench&r to the &aRadial Chasis&r."]
	quest.459BA85E48B343AE.title: "&aRadial Chasis"
	quest.45C067280949FAA8.quest_desc: ["Adds a Crafting Table GUI to the Backpack."]
	quest.45DA208946E7C327.title: "&l&9Overworld Bounty:&r&e Creepers"
	quest.45EC31812FB9934D.quest_desc: ["&aMechanical Pistons&r act like normal Pistons with Moving Blocks, but after that the similarities end! \\n\\nThey don't work off &4Redstone&r, instead they use &dRotational Power&r. The &dRotational Power&r will determine how fast and the direction the Piston moves. \\n\\nThey also can have &aSlime Balls&r added to &aStick&r to Blocks. And those Blocks can be &aGlued&r to have everything moving with the Piston. \\n\\nBest part is that we can add &aPiston Extension Poles&r to the back of the &aPiston&r to change how far the &aPiston&r can move! \\n\\nEach new &aPole&r adds a new Block of distance. I'm not sure of the max you can add, maybe that is something you can find out yourself!"]
	quest.45EC31812FB9934D.title: "&aMechanical Pistons"
	quest.460A746F466A2B34.quest_desc: [
		"The Barren Abyss is as the name suggests, barren... "
		""
		"It holds nothing but Hostile Mobs."
	]
	quest.460A746F466A2B34.title: "Barren Abyss"
	quest.461088EDD581CCF2.quest_desc: [
		"By Right Clicking with them, 2 &eSandstorms&r will spawn. The &eSandstorms&r will circle you and move with you."
		""
		"Whatever is hit by them will be Damaged and Knockbacked."
	]
	quest.461088EDD581CCF2.title: "&eSandstorm in a Bottle"
	quest.463215D773996C8D.quest_desc: ["You will need these to make Backpack Upgrades."]
	quest.463215D773996C8D.quest_subtitle: "The Base for Upgrades"
	quest.46333D54F1795D37.title: "Acquire 10 Ultra Balls"
	quest.467009C3E53F6C72.quest_desc: ["Smogstem Forest is a neighboring Biome to Indigo Mushroom Bogs."]
	quest.467009C3E53F6C72.title: "Smogstem Forest"
	quest.468DA18A7D5FA894.quest_desc: ["This upgrade makes it so the Backpack can't die."]
	quest.469DD48C0286A4C8.quest_subtitle: "Increases the holder's Speed by 2 stages if the holder's move misses."
	quest.46AF5CFC47760C3A.quest_desc: [
		"The &cCharm of Life I&r is a single-use item that will prevent death. Instead of dying, the charm will be consumed and you'll be given health regen for a short period of time."
		""
		"These can be found in loot chests."
	]
	quest.46AF5CFC47760C3A.title: "&cCharm of Life I"
	quest.46C525F59DBEC06B.quest_desc: [
		"&dEndermaptera&r live around the &dRuined Citadel&r. "
		""
		"They have 8 &4Hearts&r and only a basic attack of gnawing at you."
		""
		"If they gnaw at you too much they might break their jaws, to which they won't drop on death anymore."
		""
		"So make sure to kill them quickly if you want those &dVoid Jaws&r!"
	]
	quest.46C525F59DBEC06B.title: "&dEndermaptera"
	quest.473FA799A98A5205.quest_subtitle: "Raises and untransformed Ditto's Defense and Special Defense by 50%."
	quest.47482DA061C9FA88.quest_subtitle: "Mega Evolution is a temporary &ctransformation&r that greatly enhances a Pokémon's &eStats&r and, in some cases, changes its &bType or Ability&r."
	quest.47482DA061C9FA88.title: "Mega Stones"
	quest.476C7317510198D9.quest_desc: ["Okay this ones fun! You like throwing &eItems&r? Like, I mean to really throw them! \\n\\nThen, the &eWeighted Ejector&r is for you! \\n\\nFirst, you need to Shift Right Click a Block with the &eWeighted Ejector&r to set it as the target. The target has to be in line with where the &eEjector&r is aimed in order to hit it. \\n\\nOnce it has a target and is placed down, it can be fed &dRotational Power&r to charge it! Then, when an &eItem&r is placed on the &eWeighted Ejector&r, it will throw it! \\nYou can hold on some of the Sides to change the Stack Size needed to throw &eItems&r."]
	quest.476C7317510198D9.title: "&eWeighted Ejector"
	quest.47897D827C50629D.quest_desc: ["&aPiston Extension Poles&r are how we can make and expand &aMechanical Pistons&r. \\n\\nNot normal Pistons, sorry!"]
	quest.47897D827C50629D.quest_subtitle: "Why only move so far?"
	quest.47897D827C50629D.title: "&aPiston Extension"
	quest.47903FC7E285D897.quest_desc: ["Adds a Anvil GUI to the Backpack."]
	quest.47A6769B6BF1A46D.quest_desc: ["&eFunnels&r are like if a Hopper and Dispenser had a baby. \\n\\nWhen placed onto a Block with an Inventory, like Chests, it will automatically take &eItems&r out 1 at a time. \\nIf you Shift Right Click it will automatically take &eItems&r into the Inventory. \\n\\nBoth can be turned off with a &4Redstone Signal&r!"]
	quest.47A6769B6BF1A46D.title: "&eAndesite Funnel"
	quest.47C34B7874084B5F.quest_subtitle: "Has no effect."
	quest.47D7E28C0B189425.quest_desc: [
		"Inside the &2Dark Forest&r, you'll find a structure that leads underground."
		""
		"To enter, you'll need to place one of the boss trophies you've acquired on the nearby pedestal, don't worry about which one you place, you can pick it back up."
		""
		"On the 3rd layer, you'll find the Knight Phantoms. Defeat these to unlock the next boss."
	]
	quest.47D7E28C0B189425.quest_subtitle: "The Darkest of Forests"
	quest.47D7E28C0B189425.title: "&2The Dark Forest"
	quest.481B96683F6BB23A.quest_desc: [
		"Witherite is a drop from &4The Harbinger&r, it will always drop 1 block which can be made into 9 ingots."
		""
		"Witherite is used to craft 3 Weapons and the &4Mechanical Fusion Anvil&r which can be used to combine &4&lCataclysm&r Items!"
	]
	quest.481B96683F6BB23A.title: "&4Wither plus Netherite = ...?"
	quest.483892F0A0F75B97.quest_desc: ["&bFluid Pipes&r are what we'll use to actually move &bFluids&r automatically from one Inventory to another! \\n\\nYou can place them down and they will automatically connect to Inventories and other &bPipes&r. \\n\\nWith a Wrench you can add Windows to a &bPipe&r. These won't connect to parallel &bPipes&r without Windows. \\n\\nThe &bPipes&r themselves won't move &bFluids&r though, we'll need a &bMechanical Pump&r for that! \\n\\nWhen we do get &bPipes&r to start flowing though, we can use them to take &bFluids&r out from a Source Block or the opposite with placing down Source Blocks. \\n\\nThe &bPipe&r will need to have an Open End to do so though, so there can't be Blocks in the way."]
	quest.483892F0A0F75B97.title: "&bFluid Pipe"
	quest.48662C44C5F42F34.quest_desc: ["Welcome to the &cNether&r. Make sure to wear at least one piece of golden armor to keep the piglins from attacking."]
	quest.48662C44C5F42F34.title: "Welcome To The Nether"
	quest.48BE7DAC5082044D.quest_desc: ["Stress, like &dRotational Power&r, is important and confusing. \\n\\nStress Units (Su) are power loads for our &6Machines&r. Some &6Machines&r will have a minimum Stress, that means you'll need that much Stress in your System to work the &6Machine&r. \\n\\n&6Deployers&f, &6Mechanical Saws&f, and &6Encased Fans&r are examples of those! \\n\\nSome &6Machines&r also have a maximum Stress Units. That means if it goes over the amount, it will most likely stop working. Or blow up, either or! \\n\\nStress Units are developed from &dCogs&r and from our &6Machines&r that make &dRotational Power&r. &9Water Wheels&r give little Stress while &dSteam Engines&r can give a ton!"]
	quest.48BE7DAC5082044D.title: "Stress"
	quest.490C2406470636BF.quest_subtitle: "Extends the duration of rain from 5 to 8 turns."
	quest.495B0CC178B4CFA9.quest_desc: ["The &eBrass Funnel&r is placed and used similar to the &eAndesite Tunnel&r. \\n\\nBut each side comes with new configs! \\n\\nThe Input Side will now come with a Filter option. Just place the &eItem&r in, and it will only take in that &eItem&r. \\n\\nThe Output Side will now come with a limit. You can Scroll to set a number from 1 to 64. You can also choose whether it will Output exactly that amount, or up to that amount. \\n\\nIf it is exactly that amout, it will wait until that amount is within the Inventory to Output it. If it is up to, it will keep Outputting &eItems&r until that number is reached."]
	quest.495B0CC178B4CFA9.title: "&eBrass Funnel"
	quest.4987EDA5728FA6EF.quest_desc: ["The &3Eye of Curse&r will lead you to the &3Frosted Prison&r to fight the &3&lMaledictus&r."]
	quest.4987EDA5728FA6EF.title: "&3Eye of Curse"
	quest.49D6144F33442E90.quest_desc: [
		"I'm going to assume you've been out mining, right? It is MINEcraft after all."
		""
		"Iron is probably one of the most important ores you'll want to get every time you run into it. The world of modded MC pretty much runs on Iron."
	]
	quest.49D6144F33442E90.title: "The &9Metal&r Age"
	quest.4A178567A38E8896.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.4A178567A38E8896.title: "&eAdvanced Deposit Upgrade"
	quest.4A183D84E9CC7FF9.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Soul Elytra&r works just like a normal &8Elytra&r, just now with more Durability and Armor Points!"
		""
		"They can't be repaired with &7Phantom Membranes&r like normal &8Elytras&r... but Enchantments can still repair them!"
		""
		"To Craft one you'll need an &8Elytra&r, 4 &3Sculk Bones&r which drop from &3Shattered&r, 2 &3Soul Dust&r which drop from &3Sculk Snappers &for &3Sculk Leeches&r, and a &3Soul Crystal&r which drops from the &3&lStalker&r."
	]
	quest.4A183D84E9CC7FF9.title: "&3Soul Elytra"
	quest.4A3B8A6A5B39DEBE.quest_desc: [
		"The &5Abyssal Egg&r is also a drop from &5&lThe Leviathan&r."
		""
		"Place the &5Egg&r down, then wait awhile and you'll have your own baby &5Leviathan&r."
		""
		"Once its hatched you can feed it a ton of Tropical Fish to tame it."
		""
		"The &5baby&r has 2400 &4Hearts&r and can heal by feeding it Tropical Fish."
		""
		"Once tamed, like the &eModern Remnant&r it can be set with Shift Right Click to follow or stay or wander."
	]
	quest.4A3B8A6A5B39DEBE.title: "&5Abyssal Egg&r"
	quest.4A731367A7C16455.quest_desc: [
		"&3Sculk Jaws&r are Blocks we can find within the &9Deeplands&r."
		""
		"When you accidentally walk over them they'll bite you, this drags you down and deals Damage when you are stuck in them."
		""
		"You can take them by using Silk Touch."
	]
	quest.4A731367A7C16455.title: "&3Sculk Jaw"
	quest.4A78FC07C3633743.quest_desc: [
		"The Ender Dragon is the Boss that guards The End. "
		""
		"When you enter an End Portal you'll arrive at the End Island where she spawns."
		""
		"She has 200 Hearts and can attack with Fireballs or ramming into you."
		""
		"You'll have to break the End Crystals on the pillars as they heal her, in order to kill her!"
		""
		"Once you do kill her, she'll drop: Arcane Essence, Epic Shaderbags, Dragonskin, Dragon Scales from two different mods, and a bunch of experience!"
		""
		"Then the Portal will open up so you can return to the Overworld, or you can find an End Gateway to explore the outer islands. You'll also find a Dragon Egg on the Portal."
	]
	quest.4AEEB8FDE1187952.quest_subtitle: "The Final Upgrade"
	quest.4AEEB8FDE1187952.title: "&dNetherite Chest"
	quest.4B59FCEAA94745AD.quest_desc: ["&6Gloomy Cacti&r are just like normal &2Cacti&r, just these spawn within &cOvercast Columns&r."]
	quest.4B59FCEAA94745AD.title: "&6Gloomy Cacti"
	quest.4B6E68B13594B5C2.quest_desc: ["Increases stack size in the Backpack by 2."]
	quest.4B9B9F3E09AE9EDD.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Fire-type moves."
	quest.4BAEF21DB6E9F2A2.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.4BAEF21DB6E9F2A2.title: "&eAdvanced Pump Upgrade"
	quest.4BE35433B40D20A3.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Dragon-type moves."
	quest.4C0860E314BF4830.quest_subtitle: "Poisons the holder."
	quest.4C31649D721F76B5.quest_desc: ["The &6Mechanical Harvester&r will automatically Farm Mature Crops, and Replant them. \\n\\nObviously it has to be moved by a &aContraption&r to work. \\n\\nIt will also automatically place the collected Crops into Inventories connected to the &aContraption&r. If not, it will drop the Crops on the ground."]
	quest.4C31649D721F76B5.title: "&6Mechanical Harvester"
	quest.4C77ABCD41383F32.quest_desc: ["&cBlaze Cakes&r can be used to &bSuper-Heat&r &cBlaze Burners&r! A Heat that has never been seen before! \\n\\nBut how do we Bake them? \\n\\nFirst, we'll need to make the &4Blaze Cake Base&r. To get it, process an Egg, Sugar, and &4Cinder Flour&r in a Mechanical Press and Basin. \\n\\n&4Cinder Flour&r is created by Crushing &4Netherrack&r through two Crushing Wheels. \\n\\nThen, once we have our &4Blaze Cake Base&r, we can fill it with &cLava&r from a &bSpout&r to make our &cBlaze Cake&r!"]
	quest.4C77ABCD41383F32.title: "&cBlaze Cakes"
	quest.4C97646F7174979B.quest_desc: [
		"&f&lPage 1 - Overview"
		""
		"&fWith &6&lMCA Reborn&r&f installed, villagers become far more human-like than in vanilla Minecraft. They now have &e&lGenders, Personalities, Traits, Genetics,&r&f and &e&lFamily Trees&r&f."
		""
		"&fOver time, you can &a&lbuild relationships, form families, and truly live among them&r&f."
		""
		"&fVillagers still retain their core behaviors, professions, jobs, and sleeping routines, but now they also &a&lfeel alive, react to your actions, and form emotional connections with you&r&f."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lPage 2 - Interactions and UI"
		""
		"&fRight-click a villager to open the &a&linteraction menu&r&f. They'll greet you with a \"Hello!\" and you can choose how to interact, talk, trade, or &a&lflirt&r&f. Each villager's &a&lpersonality and mood&r&f will affect how they respond."
		""
		"&fThe interface shows:"
		""
		"&f&l■ &fName and Profession"
		""
		"&f&l■ &fMood and Personality"
		""
		"&f&l■ &fRelationship Hearts"
		""
		"&f&l■ &fTraits and Family Tree"
		""
		"&f&l■ &fMarital Status and Genetics"
		""
		"&fSome menus like &a&lWork&r&f or &a&lInventory&r&f only appear if the villager is married to you or part of your family."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lPage 3 - Talking and Building Relationships"
		""
		"&fThe main way to bond with villagers is by &a&ltalking to them!&r&f You can:"
		""
		"&f&l■ &a&lChat&r&f - simple conversation (+1 or +3 heart)"
		""
		"&f&l■ &a&lTell Jokes&r&f - success depends on mood or personality"
		""
		"&f&l■ &a&lTell Stories&r&f - from simple tales to epic adventures"
		""
		"&f&l■ &a&lHug, Flirt, or Kiss&r&f - bold actions that depend on your current relationship"
		""
		"&fEach success builds &a&ltrust&r&f, each failure may &c&lhurt it&r&f. Choose wisely, your words shape your bond!"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lPage 4 - Interacting Beyond Words"
		""
		"&fYou can &a&lgive gifts&r&f to villagers, homes or work areas, and even tell them to follow you during adventures!"
		""
		"&fMarried villagers (or children you raise) can &a&lwork for you&r&f, farming, fishing, or chopping wood."
		""
		"&fThey'll also &a&lreact to the world&r&f around them, sleep, relax, and even ride horses if allowed. Your interactions define their &a&lloyalty and happiness&r&f."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lPage 5 - Family and Growth"
		""
		"&fWhen you marry a villager, you can eventually have &a&lchildren&r&f. After procreation, a &a&lBaby Item&r&f appears in your inventory. After 20 minutes, it grows into a &a&lChild&r&f."
		""
		"&fChildren pass through stages: &a&lBaby → Toddler → Child → Teen → Adult&r&f, each with unique dialogues, interactions, and personalities."
		""
		"&fFamily trees will &a&lrecord your generations&r&f, showing parents and grandparents over time."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lPage 6 - Relationships and Villager Bonds"
		""
		"&fVillagers can also &a&lmarry each other!&r&f Give one a &6&lMatchmaker's Ring&r&f, and they'll instantly pair with the nearest villager."
		""
		"&fAfter marriage, gifting one of them a &a&lCake&r&f will cause them to have a child."
		""
		"&fLove, friendship, and family, &6&lMCA Reborn&r&f turns your world into a thriving village. Form bonds, raise generations, and create stories that last for lifetimes."
	]
	quest.4C97646F7174979B.quest_subtitle: "&f&lLearn how the villagers in &6&lMinecraft Comes Alive: Reborn &fwork&r"
	quest.4D336C8470709226.quest_desc: [
		"&f&d&lAechor Petals&r&f are dropped by the dangerous &d&lAechor Plants&r&f that dwell across the &b&lAether&r&f."
		""
		"&fThese petals are soft, fragrant, and incredibly useful, they serve as the main food source for &a&lMoas&r&f, helping you raise and tame your flying companions.."
	]
	quest.4D336C8470709226.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain an &d&lAechor Petal&r&f"
	quest.4D336C8470709226.title: "&7&lQuest: Aechor Petal Discovery"
	quest.4D80D0820B6ACDE4.quest_subtitle: "Lowers the holder's Speed when Trick Room is in effect. Consumed after use."
	quest.4D825257C5B82870.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.4D825257C5B82870.title: "&eAdvanced Restock Upgrade"
	quest.4D9FA2B3AE5C9992.quest_subtitle: "The Fourth Upgrade"
	quest.4D9FA2B3AE5C9992.title: "&bDiamond Chest"
	quest.4DAA740D9C882458.quest_desc: [
		"Slingshot is a very fun weapon added by &2&lUndergarden&r. "
		""
		"It has 4 Ammo that can be shot: "
		""
		"Scintling Goo can be fired and when it hits a Mob it'll give them the Gooey Effect."
		""
		"Depthrocks are just normal projectiles."
		""
		"Rotten Blisterberries will blow up on impact."
		""
		"And &eGronglets&r don't do any damage they just make noise."
	]
	quest.4DBE26FB8250E199.quest_desc: [
		"In the depths of the Labyrinth Swamp is a giant &cMinoshroom&r."
		""
		"Once defeated, it'll drop &eMeef Stroganoff&r. To unlock the next area, you must eat it."
	]
	quest.4DBE26FB8250E199.title: "&cMighty Meef Stroganoff"
	quest.4DD1F09FBF8E7C21.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Grass-type moves."
	quest.4DED2CC6D8292774.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the holder's Speed but only allows the use of one move."
	quest.4E29ABD79AFF295E.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 63"
	quest.4E29ABD79AFF295E.title: "Trainer Brendan"
	quest.4E6F296F88380EDD.title: "&l&9Overworld Bounty:&r&e Skeletons"
	quest.4E8880E527FF386F.quest_desc: [
		"&7Cloggrum&r has stats a little worse than Iron Armor."
		""
		"The Boots also help with going through Scintling Goo!"
	]
	quest.4E8880E527FF386F.title: "&7Cloggrum&r Armor"
	quest.4EE10B8E194F5CA9.quest_desc: ["&6&lCreate&r 1.21 also now comes with Trains included with the base Mod. \\n\\nFirst, you'll need &5Sturdy Metal&r! \\n\\nCrush &5Obsidian&r to get &5Obsidian Dust&r. Then, use a &bSpout&r to place &cLava&r into the &5Crushed Obsidian&r. \\n\\nAfter that, Press it twice with &6Mechanical Presses&r and you'll get &5Sturdy Metal&r. \\n\\n&5Sturdy Metal&r can then be applied to a &eBrass Casing&r to make &5Train Casings&r."]
	quest.4EE10B8E194F5CA9.title: "&5&lTrains"
	quest.4EEE052CDBB19A7B.quest_desc: [
		"&bGwibs&r are larger and angrier versions of &bGwiblings&r."
		""
		"They don't have any Drops nor can they be placed in Buckets. All they offer is pain!"
	]
	quest.4EEE052CDBB19A7B.title: "&bGwib&r"
	quest.4EFC028C26AF2AF9.quest_desc: [
		"&3Sculk Centipedes&r are long neutral Mobs that spawn in the &3&lOtherside&r."
		""
		"They have 10 &4Hearts&r and will attack in a group if Hit, like Wolves."
		""
		"They only drop &aXP&r and maybe String, so best to leave them be!"
	]
	quest.4EFC028C26AF2AF9.title: "&3Sculk Centipede"
	quest.4EFD2008E08CD3C3.quest_desc: ["I assume you know how to make planks, but if you don't just place the logs you just aquired into a single square of the 2x2 crafting grid in your inventory."]
	quest.4EFD2008E08CD3C3.title: "Planks"
	quest.4F7FFDA039C02B4C.quest_desc: [
		"To upgrade from &cNetherite&r to &9Warden Gear&r, you'll need a &9Smithing Template&r!"
		""
		"These are found in Chests in &6Ancient Cities&r."
		""
		"They can then be duplicated with 7 Diamonds and a &3Sculk Block&r!"
	]
	quest.4F7FFDA039C02B4C.title: "&9Warden Upgrade Template"
	quest.4F878F9B648D44B7.quest_desc: [
		"This is slightly stronger than &2Naga&r armor, and comes fully enchanted."
		""
		"You can make these by finding &2Steeleaf&r within the &9Twilight Forest&r."
	]
	quest.4F878F9B648D44B7.title: "&2Steeleaf Armor"
	quest.4FAB391F97D8C0CC.quest_subtitle: "The holder's multi-strike moves will hit at least 4 times."
	quest.4FD8F9D69F7BAA54.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 29"
	quest.4FD8F9D69F7BAA54.title: "Trainer Brendan"
	quest.50485D5022AFF255.quest_desc: [
		"&6Gems&f are &bHeld Items&f that can be &e[held by a Pokémon]&f, that increase the power&f of the first respective move type. "
		""
		"Consumed after use"
	]
	quest.50560C45C81CBE74.quest_desc: [
		"&fThe &d&lTears&r&f music disc is a rare drop from defeating a Ghost with its own Fireball. &a&lOnce obtained&r&f, play it in a &e&lJukebox&r&f to fill your base with a haunting melody."
		""
		"&fThis disc has a comparator output of 10 and represents the sorrow of the Nether. &d&lClaim the Tears&r&f disc and enjoy its melancholic beauty."
	]
	quest.50560C45C81CBE74.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain the &d&lTears&r&f&l music disc and play it in a &e&lJukebox"
	quest.50560C45C81CBE74.title: "&6&lQuest: Play \"Tears\" by Anos Roddy"
	quest.50A59F72CE07BABB.quest_desc: [
		"Getting to the &2&lUndergarden&r is similar to getting to &c&lThe Nether&r. You'll need to craft a Portal."
		""
		"It is the same shape and size as Nether Portals but instead of Obsidian you'll need a varient of Stone Bricks. Stone Bricks, Mossy Stone Bricks, or Deepslate Bricks."
		""
		"Once formed, you can activate it by using the Catalyst on it. "
	]
	quest.50A59F72CE07BABB.quest_subtitle: "Making the Portal"
	quest.50A59F72CE07BABB.title: "The Undergarden"
	quest.50DBB87E53017E60.quest_desc: ["&bFluid Valves&r can be used to stop &bPipes&r from moving &bFluid&r. \\n\\nGive them a Rotation, most likely from a &cValve Handle&r, to stop moving &bFluids&r. \\n\\nJust Rotate it again to get the &bFluids&r back!"]
	quest.50DBB87E53017E60.title: "&bFluid Valve"
	quest.5134C81D96C55375.quest_desc: ["&5Train Observers&r work like a fancy Detection Rail. \\n\\nWhen a &5Train&r rolls over it the &7Track&r it is set to (which is chosen like the &5Train Station&r) it will give a &4Redstone Signal&r. \\n\\nYou can also place Filters into the &5Observer&r to only get &4Redstone Signals&r when the &5Train&r has that &eItem &for &bFluid&r within."]
	quest.5134C81D96C55375.title: "&5Train Observer"
	quest.516E4C41F210E887.quest_desc: ["Automatically use potions, food with effects, or milk buckets."]
	quest.51A5DED59F19D76E.quest_desc: [
		"The &dGauntlet of the Guard&r is the drop from the &d&lEnder Guardian&r."
		""
		"When you hold it in either Hand, you can Hold Right Click to bring all Mobs near you, even closer!"
		""
		"You can also smack Mobs with it in your Main Hand to deal Damage."
		""
		"Try using the pull mechanic with flying Mobs!"
	]
	quest.51A5DED59F19D76E.title: "&dGauntlet of Guard"
	quest.51EA6B1452883AB2.quest_desc: ["Linear Chasis work like Puddy in real life, only connecting to each other. \\n\\nLinear Chasis, which are facing the same way, will automatically connect as if they were Glued. Other Linear Chasis or ones facing different ways, will not stick together. \\n\\nYou can then use Glue on the Top and Bottom of the Linear Chasis to connect a line of Blocks from it. So all Blocks on top of those will be Glued to the Linear Chasis. Very helpful for saving Glue! \\n\\nWith the Wrench you can set how many Blocks get Glued on the Top or Bottom of the Linear Chasis."]
	quest.51EA6B1452883AB2.title: "&aLinear Chasis"
	quest.51F7BFB269807464.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Sculk Transmitter&r is a very rare Item we can find within Chests of the &6Ancient Temple&r."
		""
		"Once you do find one, it'll be your Bestfriend!"
		""
		"To use it, simply Shift Right Click a Block that has a GUI, think of: Chests, Crafting Tables, and Furnaces. Then, the &3Transmitter&r will be bound to that Item."
		""
		"After that, we can use the &3Transmitter&r to remotely access that Block from wherever!"
		""
		"To unbind the Block, Shift Right Click the Air with the &3Transmitter&r."
	]
	quest.51F7BFB269807464.title: "&3Sculk Transmitter"
	quest.524F08904E535375.quest_desc: ["The &fCharm of Keeping II&r works the same as the &6Charm of Keeping I&r but stops you from losing the stuff in your hotbar when you die too."]
	quest.524F08904E535375.title: "&fCharm of Keeping II"
	quest.5283FFD52697080B.quest_desc: ["Once a Gym Leader and later promoted to Elite Four, Koga blends ancient ninja techniques with deadly Poison-types. His traps are as dangerous as his toxins."]
	quest.5283FFD52697080B.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 68"
	quest.5283FFD52697080B.title: "Koga"
	quest.52EF6F5C7FEFCBB1.quest_desc: [
		"The &7Glass Sword&r deals 40 hearts of damage, but only has 1 durability."
		""
		""
		"These are rarely found in loot chests in the &bAurora Palace&r."
	]
	quest.52EF6F5C7FEFCBB1.title: "&7Glass Sword"
	quest.53024F3F025B1E92.quest_desc: ["Now that you have a fossil, it’s time to identify it! Each fossil corresponds to a specific ancient Pokémon."]
	quest.53024F3F025B1E92.quest_subtitle: "What kind of fossil have you found?"
	quest.5379FFF9786BF9A1.quest_desc: ["Adds a battery to the Backpack."]
	quest.53806ED3AFD892CD.quest_desc: [
		"There's 3 Pets from &4&lCataclysm&r the &eModern Remnant&r, &5Baby Leviathan&r, and &4Netherite Ministrosity&r!"
		""
		"Both the &eModern Remnant&r and &4Netherite Ministrosity&r can be placed in Buckets."
		""
		"The &5Baby Leviathan&r will need a Water Bucket."
	]
	quest.53B99295DCBCE71E.quest_desc: [
		"Zombies have different varients that spawn in other Biomes."
		""
		"Husks- spawn in Deserts. "
		"Drowned- spawn Underwater."
		"Gelid- spawn in Cold Biomes."
		"Thickets- spawn in Jungles."
	]
	quest.53B99295DCBCE71E.title: "Zombie Variants"
	quest.53EF84A1AE34B8E0.quest_desc: [
		"Ancient Seas are wide open Seas in the &2&lUndergarden&r."
		""
		"The Water also holds &bGwibs&r and &bGwiblings&r. And can't forget Glitterkelp!"
	]
	quest.53EF84A1AE34B8E0.title: "Ancient Sea"
	quest.540BEA8BF5E05AA2.quest_desc: ["Another Sea, just this one is much colder."]
	quest.540BEA8BF5E05AA2.title: "Icy Sea"
	quest.54D7260C919FF99D.quest_desc: [
		"Sophisticated Backpacks offers upgradable Backpacks that can use filters to add nifty features!"
		""
		"Backpacks can be put in your Curios Back slot and they can be dyed."
	]
	quest.54D7260C919FF99D.quest_subtitle: "Inventories are too Small"
	quest.54D7260C919FF99D.title: "Sophisticated Backpacks"
	quest.54EC1C7FC1DA9107.quest_desc: ["&dAdjustable Chain Drives&r work like &dEncased Chain Drives&r, just with more configs. \\n\\nIf we send a &4Redstone Signal&r to the &dAdjustable Chain Drive&r that the original &8Shaft&r is connected to, the other &dChain Drive &8Shafts&r will double in Speed! \\n\\nIf we send one to a different &dChain Drive&r though, the Speed of that &dChain Drive&r will be cut in half!"]
	quest.54EC1C7FC1DA9107.title: "&dAdjustable Chain Drive"
	quest.553654847018F89E.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.553654847018F89E.title: "&eAdvanced Magnet Upgrade"
	quest.5553603525266E7D.quest_desc: [
		"&5The Coralssus&r works as a Guard and Steed for the &5Sunken City&r."
		""
		"They can be ridden by &5Deeplings&r to move quicker and attack together!"
		""
		"They have 160 &4Hearts&r and basic attacks . Its attacks are just smacking and throwing you."
		""
		"When killed it'll drop Coral Chunks which can be used to make the &5Abyssal Sacrifice&r."
	]
	quest.5553603525266E7D.title: "&5Coralssus&r"
	quest.555B818AF4B8BF0C.quest_desc: [
		"&fThe &d&lEyeblossom&r&f is a flower that sees the world differently. &a&lIt opens its eye at night&r&f and closes during the day, whispering to its neighbors as it changes."
		""
		"&fUse &b&lBone Meal&r&f on grass in the Pale Garden to grow them, or trade with &b&lWandering Traders&r&f. &d&lCollect both variants&r&f and watch them blink open and closed beneath the moonlight."
	]
	quest.555B818AF4B8BF0C.quest_subtitle: "&f&lLocate and collect both &d&lClosed&r&f&l and &d&lOpen Eyeblossoms"
	quest.555B818AF4B8BF0C.title: "&6&lQuest: Locate and Collect Eyeblossoms"
	quest.558EAB9482651B45.quest_subtitle: "Lengthens the duration of moves and Abilities that alter the terrain of the battlefield"
	quest.55DD1E77690276DF.quest_desc: ["Adds a filter for items you want to auto-delete in the Backpack."]
	quest.561321F02181327D.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.561321F02181327D.title: "&eAdvanced Refill Upgrade"
	quest.561C6FEC0472C832.quest_desc: [
		"The healing machine will start with zero charge when placed."
		""
		"The healing machine will charge up over time and continue charging indefinitely, even after being fully charged."
		""
		"Pokécenters can generate within villages, which contain a naturally generated Healing Machine. These healing machines are unique in that they have a different texture and if mined drops 1 Iron Ingot instead of the block itself."
	]
	quest.561C6FEC0472C832.quest_subtitle: "Your Pokémon deserve the best care. Craft a Healing Machine to make sure you're always prepared!"
	quest.56449EFA24C5E6B7.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Rock-type moves."
	quest.567A5473958FD14B.quest_subtitle: "The Second Upgrade"
	quest.567A5473958FD14B.title: "&fIron Backpack"
	quest.568651A3AC56EEAA.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's punching moves and prevents them from triggering contact with the target."
	quest.569D88C83F6A7589.quest_subtitle: "Grants the holder a chance of going first."
	quest.56C1E869DAE716ED.quest_subtitle: "Revive the ancient predator of the skies!"
	quest.56C1E869DAE716ED.title: "The Winged Legend"
	quest.57306560BD3CB140.quest_desc: ["To power up &4&lThe Harbinger&r you'll need a Nether Star, which you get from killing the Wither."]
	quest.57306560BD3CB140.quest_subtitle: "Powering The Harbinger"
	quest.57306560BD3CB140.title: "Nether Star"
	quest.576BD9A8286DF0C6.quest_desc: [
		"Once feared for knocking you out of the sky, the &b&lZephyrs&r&f now face their reckoning."
		""
		"Take up the &6&lHammer of Kingbdogz&r&f and send them crashing down from the clouds they love so much. "
		""
		"Let justice, and gravity, do the rest."
	]
	quest.576BD9A8286DF0C6.quest_subtitle: "&f&lKill a &b&lZephyr&r&f&l using the &6&lHammer of Kingbdogz&r&f&l"
	quest.576BD9A8286DF0C6.title: "&7&lQuest: Sweet Revenge!"
	quest.578D2DFE56977EC0.quest_desc: ["Increases stack size in the Backpack by 4."]
	quest.578D2DFE56977EC0.title: "&eStack Upgrade Tier 2"
	quest.5794C65245733370.quest_desc: [
		"The &3&lStalker&r is a Boss that can be spawned by breaking Ancient Vases."
		""
		"He has 200 &4Hearts&r and a Boss Bar to keep track. We'll need to kill him to get &3Soul Crystals&r."
		""
		"He is very fast and does a ton of Damage if he Hits you. Thankfully he is Blind, like the &9&lWarden&r. But he also has an amazing sense of hearing which allows him to hear everything nearby. "
		""
		"He has a few attacks, normally he will just Hit you. Sometimes he might cause an AOE attack and can summon &3Sculk Leeches&r to attack you!"
		""
		"He'll also attack every non-&3Sculk&r Mob."
	]
	quest.5794C65245733370.title: "&3&lStalker"
	quest.579FD2A64B56C5B9.quest_desc: ["Minecarts with Chests are Minecarts with Chests in them. You can't ride in these but they can be useful for transporting items across Rail systems."]
	quest.57A18F2E51952EB8.quest_desc: ["&5Postboxes&r will use Addresses and &5Trains&r to deliver &ePackages&r! \\n\\nFirst, &ePackages&r can be held on &5Trains&r with &eDepots&r! Obviously the &eDepot&r needs to be connected to the &5Train &fvia &aGlue&r. \\n\\nNext, we can assign the &5Postbox&r to a &5Train Station&r by Right Clicking the &5Train Station&r wtih the &5Postbox&r in Hand. \\n\\nWe can then place the &5Postbox&r nearby and when a &5Train &farrives at the &5Station&r they will interact with the &5Postbox&r. \\n\\nIn the &5Postbox's&r GUI we can change its Address, which will effect whether &ePackages&r are delivered or sent from it. If the Address of the &ePackage&r matches the Address of the &5Postbox&r, it will be sent to the &5Postbox&r. If it doesn't match, it will go from the &5Postbox&r to your &5Train&r!"]
	quest.57A18F2E51952EB8.title: "&5Postboxes"
	quest.57A564CD668C7378.quest_desc: [
		"&cReappearing Blocks&r are like really cool doors. Once right-clicked, they'll disappear for a short time."
		""
		"&cVanishing Blocks&r will disappear when right-clicked, but they don't come back."
	]
	quest.57A564CD668C7378.title: "&cReappearing \\& Vanishing Blocks"
	quest.57A7A5C79389A96A.quest_desc: ["Most Players will already know of &6&lCreate&r especially its billions of Addons! Not that many Mods have whole Modpacks based around them! \\n\\nIf you aren't used to &6&lCreate&r, these Quests should help you to learn the Mod. And with many &eItems &fand &6Machines&r there is a Ponder Option! Hold W while viewing the &eItem&r to watch a schematic that will teach you to understand the &eItem &for &6Machine&r. \\n\\nAnd trust me, you'll want to learn &6&lCreate&r, it is super useful! \\n\\nTo start you'll need &8Andesite&r and lots of it."]
	quest.57A7A5C79389A96A.title: "&6&lCreate&r"
	quest.57B9E8B1429F561D.quest_desc: [
		"The &4Wither Assault Shoulder Weapon (W.A.S.W.)&r is the last weapon you can make from &4Witherite&r."
		""
		"It has 2 different projectiles it can shoot: &4Wither Missiles&r and &4Wither Howitzers&r."
		""
		"The &4Wither Missiles&r shoot from just Holding Right Click, and will Damage whatever gets hit by them, with low cooldown."
		""
		"The &4Wither Howitzers&r are fired when you Shift Hold Right Click, they damage a bigger area and leave an area of Wither Effect, that damages whatever walks in it. They have much longer cooldown though."
	]
	quest.57B9E8B1429F561D.title: "&4Wither Assault Shoulder Weapon"
	quest.5801331BD9BB32FB.quest_desc: [
		"The &2Amethyst Crab&r lives in the Lush Caves with the Axolotls."
		""
		"It has 2800 &4Hearts&r and is initially neutral. That means it won't attack first but it will hit you back."
		""
		"It has a few attacks one being just smacking you with its claws. It can also throw Amethysts at you and burrow under the ground."
		""
		"On death it'll drop its meat and shells. Its meat can be blessed in an Altar of Amethyst to be better. The Shells can be crafted together to make Bloom Stone Pauldrons which have similar stats to Netherite Chestplate but can do similar abilities as the &2Crab&r itself."
	]
	quest.5801331BD9BB32FB.title: "&2Amethyst Crab&r"
	quest.588D723E18110C25.quest_desc: [
		"The icon in the top left of the inventory screen is the FTB Teams &rmenu. This allows you to add other players to your team."
		""
		"On the right of the FTB Teams &ricon is the Quest Book icon, which allows you to access the Quest Book at any time."
	]
	quest.588D723E18110C25.quest_subtitle: "Read my description!"
	quest.58ACBDC3CE0D1C7B.quest_desc: [
		"&eThe Cursed Pyramid&r spawns in deserts and it's very hard to miss. A massive pyramid with huge pillars by the entrance."
		""
		"Enter within and you will find traps all around, &eKoboletons&r, and mini-bosses!"
		""
		"Don't worry there's also Chests, Pots, and even Suspicious Sand which you will need for the..."
	]
	quest.58ACBDC3CE0D1C7B.title: "&eCursed Pyramid&r: Home of &e&lAncient Remnant&r"
	quest.58CF700B0CB07AB6.quest_desc: [
		"&7Cloggrum&r Tools act just like Iron Tools, these just look more like Mud than Iron does!"
		""
		"The Sword does more damage than an Iron Sword though."
	]
	quest.58CF700B0CB07AB6.title: "&7Cloggrum&r Tools"
	quest.58D8C0D1770A118E.quest_desc: ["Adds a Blast Furnace GUI to the Backpack."]
	quest.5911A1810A7FF49E.quest_desc: [
		"This guide is here to introduce you to the fundamentals of Cobblemon."
		""
		"&e&lTrainer Tips:&r&r"
		""
		"- Hit \"&eJ&r\" to open your party summary and select a starter!"
		""
		"- Certain Pokémon appear only in specific biomes or during specific times."
		""
		"- Utilize the new &cpokedex&r to discover more about Pokémon spawns."
		""
		"- The Poképedia is your go to for everything Cobblemon."
		""
		"[\"\",{\"text\":\"Click Here For The Official Cobblemon Wiki\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"bold\":true,\"underlined\":false,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://wiki.cobblemon.com\"}}]"
	]
	quest.5911A1810A7FF49E.title: "Welcome To Cobblemon"
	quest.591E90EBA5771712.quest_subtitle: "Extends the duration of hail or snow from 5 to 8 turns."
	quest.596631E328B29A68.quest_desc: [
		"&fPhygs are the Aether’s adorable flying pigs, gentle yet brave enough to soar among the clouds."
		""
		"&fSaddle one up and experience the freedom of gliding across the endless skies."
	]
	quest.596631E328B29A68.quest_subtitle: "&f&lMount a &6&lPhyg&r&f"
	quest.596631E328B29A68.title: "&7&lQuest: Ride the Clouds"
	quest.5979DE0E2BA3DAE5.quest_desc: ["&7Train Tracks&r are... well what you'll use to move &5Trains&r! \\n\\nYou'll need to &6Deploy&r 2 &7Iron Nuggets&r onto a &8Stone Slab&r, then &6Press&r it with a &6Metal Press&r to get 1. \\n\\nThese will be the first Block you place in order to get &5Trains&r as it will be needed to place &5Train Stations&r. \\n\\nThey have some limitations though, they can't go at steep angles to turn, or elevate. You'll need 4 Blocks of space to get up a Block with &7Train Tracks&r. To turn it is even worse! Let's just say, if you want a perfect circle with &7Train Tracks&r, it'll need a diameter of 18 Blocks."]
	quest.5979DE0E2BA3DAE5.title: "&7Train Tracks"
	quest.59AAD96EB0E2DE9B.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's special moves."
	quest.59C6C34DB4C86DED.quest_desc: [
		"The &0&lBlack Moa&f&r is one of the rarest and most majestic mounts in the &b&lAether&f&r. Thanks to its &a&ltriple jump&f&r, skilled riders can soar much higher and farther than with most other mounts. "
		""
		"Tame it, put on a &6&lsaddle&f&r, and take to the skies on this legendary creature to truly master the floating islands."
	]
	quest.59C6C34DB4C86DED.quest_subtitle: "&f&lMount and ride a &0&lBlack Moa&f"
	quest.59C6C34DB4C86DED.title: "&7&lQuest: Ride a Black Moa"
	quest.59EE48E24A87C98C.quest_desc: [
		"The &cInfernal Forge&r is a drop from the &c&lNetherite Monstrosity&r and is technically not a weapon, it's a pickaxe!"
		""
		"It can be used to mine up to Netherite Tier."
		""
		"When right clicked it will attack in an AOE mode. Pounding the ground hitting everything close by. "
		""
		"(It can be enchanted with Sword and Pickaxe enchantments!)"
	]
	quest.59EE48E24A87C98C.title: "&cInfernal Forge"
	quest.5A6403184F99C48B.quest_desc: [
		"1. &lFind Mega Crystals:&r Mega Crystals can be found in designated areas known as Megasites"
		""
		"2. &lBreak Mega Crystals:&r When you break a Mega Crystal, it will drop a Blank Mega Stone."
	]
	quest.5A6403184F99C48B.quest_subtitle: "Steps to Obtain Mega Stones"
	quest.5A6403184F99C48B.title: "Obtain A Raw Mega Stone"
	quest.5B36DE3826F26963.quest_desc: ["&dRotational Power&r is the most important and confusing part of &6&lCreate&r. \\n\\nAll Machines will need some sort of &dRotational Power&r to work, but what is it and how do we use it? \\n\\n&dRotational Power&r is simply our Machines moving. Blocks like Shafts and Cogs will move that &dRotational Power&r to our Machines. \\n\\nTalking about Shafts, that is our start to &dRotational Power&r. They can be placed in a straight line, next to each other. \\n\\nWhen one &8Shaft&r is moved, all &8Shafts&r connected to it (on the same axis) will move with it. \\n\\nCraft 2 &8Andesite Alloys&r to create 8 &8Shafts&r."]
	quest.5B36DE3826F26963.title: "&d&lRotational Power"
	quest.5BC288E8F65E1D5B.quest_desc: ["Trapped Chests are the same as regular Chests only the emit a Redstone signal when opened and they can't be combined together into 1."]
	quest.5BC288E8F65E1D5B.quest_subtitle: "\"I wonder what's in here?\""
	quest.5BCFA49E9EF2FBD6.quest_desc: [
		"The Elder Guardian was considered a third Boss for Minecraft before the Warden."
		""
		"The Elder Guardians spawn in Ocean Monuments. Three of them spawn there and will inflict Mining Fatigue on anyone nearby."
		""
		"If you want the treasures of the Ocean Monument, you'll need to find and kill them! (Tip: I've always found 1 in the top Room, 1 on the far left, and 1 on the far right!) "
		""
		"They have 80 Hearts and attack like normal Guardians, Lasers and Thorns!"
		""
		"On death they will drop: Sponges, Prismarine, and their lunch..."
	]
	quest.5BD12B2120F6CD77.quest_desc: [
		"7 basic Poké Balls needed:"
		""
		"-&4Poké Ball&r"
		"-&eCitrine Ball&r"
		"-&2Verdant Ball&r"
		"-&9Azure Ball&r"
		"-&dRoseate Ball&r"
		"-&0Slate Ball&r"
		"-&fPremier Ball&r"
	]
	quest.5BD12B2120F6CD77.quest_subtitle: "Create one of each type of basic PokéBall available in the crafting table."
	quest.5BD12B2120F6CD77.title: "Do I Get A Wish?"
	quest.5C4A8893BAFE81BA.quest_desc: [
		"To save you from having this &oentire quest section&r covered with upgrades, take a look at the Sophisticated Backpack upgrades."
		""
		"You'll need to make the Sophisticated Storage equivalent, but they function about the same."
	]
	quest.5C4A8893BAFE81BA.quest_subtitle: "The Base for Upgrades"
	quest.5C6D655085BD2142.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Acropolis&r is a giant city in the Clouds above the vast &9Oceans&r."
		""
		"It is made of &9Azure Seastone&r, &3Prismarine&r, and &9Water&r! Yes, lots and lots and lots of &9Water&r!"
		""
		"It is based off Greek Architecture, with lots of different floors and gardens and even arenas."
		""
		"All around it will spawn &9Octohosts&r, &9Urchinkin&r, &9Cindaria&r, &9Hippotamus&r, and &9Clawdian&r! As well as a few very unfortunate &9Ocean&r Mobs."
		""
		"Hidden throughout the Architecture you'll find Chests and rare Blocks like Diamond Blocks and Sponges!"
	]
	quest.5C6D655085BD2142.title: "&9Acropolis&f: Home of &9&lScylla"
	quest.5D4D74C3D8D10864.quest_subtitle: "Prevents the holder from evolving."
	quest.5D4E32DC547DD524.quest_subtitle: "The holder is unaffected by Rain or Harsh Sunlight"
	quest.5D6FC12B3C45FBE9.quest_desc: [
		"&4&lThe Harbinger&r takes a lot of inspiration from what powers him, the Nether Star."
		""
		"He has 15,600 &4Hearts&r and will attack every Mob and Player he sees that doesn't spawn in the &4Ancient Factory&r."
		""
		"He will fly around and even charge at you. Like &0The Wither&r, &l&4The Harbringer&r will break almost every Block in its path."
		""
		"To attack he can shoot &4Wither Missiles&r at you which can give you &0Wither Effect&r or shoot &4Wither Howitzers&r from his back which will shoot off in every direction."
		""
		"He also has &4Lasers&r he can shoot you with, &4Laser Gatlings&r, and a &4big mouth beam&r."
		""
		"He has a big weakness, like the other living machines, he is weak to the &4EMPs&r! If you use them on him, he will be stun locked, unable to move or fight for a few seconds."
	]
	quest.5D6FC12B3C45FBE9.title: "&4&lThe Harbinger&r"
	quest.5DC892BA79EB52EC.quest_desc: ["The &6Mixer&r can do quite a few different Recipes but all will need a &8Basin&r below it! \\n\\nWe can &6Mix&r, this combines &bLiquids&f and &eItems&f into new &eItems&r. Like Baking! \\n\\n&6Brewing&r can combine the right &bLiquids &fand &eItems&r to make Liquid Potions. These can then be scooped out into Empty Bottles to get Potions. You'll need Heat from a &cBlaze Burner&r to &6Brew&r though. \\n\\nLast is &6Automated Shapeless Crafting&r. To the normal Player this might be a confusing statement but trust me it ain't that bad. &6Shapeless Crafting&r is a Recipe that can be made with the ingrediants in any pattern. \\n\\nLike Dying Wool, the Dye and Wool can be anywhere in the Crafting Table. Or even Silent Gear parts and patterns!"]
	quest.5DC892BA79EB52EC.title: "&6Mechanical Mixer"
	quest.5DC8E3AC76FAE959.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Steel-type moves."
	quest.5DD6631F5996BA71.quest_desc: ["&9Water Wheels&r are simple automatic &dRotational Power&r generators. \\n\\nSimply place them down, and have &9Water&r run over them in a certain direction. If it flows over both sides, it won't move, and the direction the &9Water&r flows determines where the &9Water Wheel&r &dRotates&r to. \\n\\nThe normal &9Water Wheel&r is just 1 Block big and provides a bit of Speed but with minimal Stress Units. \\n\\nThe &9Large Water Wheel&r takes up 3x3 area and grants more Stress Units, just at a lower Speed. \\n\\nYou can use both together to get the same Stress Units and Speed!"]
	quest.5DD6631F5996BA71.title: "&9Water Wheels"
	quest.5E13C19CA466A540.quest_desc: ["After so many battles, dungeons, and skybound adventures, even heroes need a break. Rest your head among the clouds and drift into dreams under the endless sky. At this point, you have truly made the &b&lAether&r&f your home."]
	quest.5E13C19CA466A540.quest_subtitle: "&f&lSleep in a &f&lBed&r&f&l within the &b&lAether Dimension&r&f&l"
	quest.5E13C19CA466A540.title: "&7&lQuest: Finally, Rest Among the Clouds"
	quest.5E2E0786092E86CA.quest_desc: [
		"The Copper Chest can be made but is not needed to make an Iron Chest."
		""
		"It can be used if you want to save some Iron though."
	]
	quest.5E2E0786092E86CA.quest_subtitle: "The First Upgrade"
	quest.5E2E0786092E86CA.title: "&6Copper Chest"
	quest.5EC72E4E924120B2.quest_subtitle: "The Fourth Upgrade"
	quest.5EC72E4E924120B2.title: "&bDiamond Backpack"
	quest.5ED1F2B2E167C2B5.quest_desc: [
		"&5Coral Golems&r spawn within the &5Sunken City&r."
		""
		"They are similar to their bigger counterparts: &5Coralssus&r but have less &4Hearts&r at 110 and can't be ridden by &5Deeplings&r."
		""
		"They have more attacks than their counterparts though! Like jumping at you and smashing the ground next to you. And it can smack you."
		""
		"On death they will drop Crystallized Coral Fragments, which can be crafted into Crystallized Coral. Those can be made into the &5Abyssal Sacrifice&r."
	]
	quest.5ED1F2B2E167C2B5.title: "&5Coral Golem"
	quest.5EFC1CBEAB22783D.quest_subtitle: "Protects the holder from contact effects from the target."
	quest.5F0802901696A8F1.quest_desc: [
		""
		"&fOne of the most iconic features of the Aether’s floating islands is the &b&lAercloud&r&f, mystical clouds that react when stepped on."
		""
		"&fAmong them, the &b&lBlue Aercloud&r&f is a favorite: soft, bouncy, and full of kinetic sky energy."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lFinding Aerclouds"
		""
		"&fBlue Aerclouds naturally spawn around the edges and undersides of Aether islands."
		""
		"&fThey appear as &b&llight-blue, semi-transparent blocks&r&f that gently shimmer in the sunlight."
		""
		"&fBe cautious when exploring for them, one wrong move could send you falling into the void (and back to the Overworld)."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lThe Bounce"
		""
		"&fWhen you land on a &b&lBlue Aercloud&r&f, you will be launched &a&linto the air&r&f with a satisfying bounce."
		""
		"&fUse this to reach higher places, cross gaps, or just enjoy the thrill of sky acrobatics."
		""
		"&fOther Aerclouds have different effects, experiment with them all to see how they can help you navigate this aerial paradise."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lPro Tip"
		""
		"&fCombine &b&lBlue Aerclouds&r&f with &d&lGravitite Tools&r&f or &a&lMoa mounts&r&f for maximum mobility."
		""
		"&fMastering their use can make traversing the &b&lAether&r&f faster, safer, and a lot more fun."
	]
	quest.5F0802901696A8F1.quest_subtitle: "&fFind and bounce on a &b&lBlue Aercloud&r&f in the &b&lAether&r&f"
	quest.5F0802901696A8F1.title: "&7&lQuest: Bounce on a Blue Aercloud"
	quest.5F4CCAB99A61BD5D.quest_desc: ["Allows you to pump experience between you and the Backpack."]
	quest.5F4CCAB99A61BD5D.title: "&aExperience Pump Upgrade"
	quest.5F941E8B4B23D44D.quest_desc: [
		"The &2Zombie Scepter&r exists because who doesn't want to summon their own &2Zombies&r?"
		""
		"To recharge, combine with &cRotten Flesh&r in a crafting grid."
	]
	quest.5F941E8B4B23D44D.quest_subtitle: "Summons Zombies"
	quest.5F941E8B4B23D44D.title: "&2Zombie Scepter"
	quest.5FF9909A9EDA147A.title: "Acquire 10 Great Balls"
	quest.602AEB647FD9359D.quest_desc: ["Welcome to Modpack"]
	quest.602AEB647FD9359D.title: "Getting Started"
	quest.60720A390340E343.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the amount of HP the holder recovers from HP-stealing moves."
	quest.607B3D66A804554A.quest_desc: [
		"Using the &6Lamp of Cinders&r, you are able to break the Thorns in the Thornland Biome."
		""
		"Gather some &cThorn Roses&r to continue on to the &2Final Plateau&r."
	]
	quest.607B3D66A804554A.title: "Every Thorn has its Rose"
	quest.608CD278A088265A.quest_subtitle: "When holder is struck by a damaging move, forces the attacker that used the move to switch out."
	quest.60B23990691359FD.quest_desc: [
		"No, the &9&lWarden&r doesn't use Swords and Axes. But we can!"
		""
		"Both the &9Warden Sword &fand &9Axe&r are upgrades of their &cNetherite versions&r with a &9Reinforced Echo Shard &fand &9Warden Upgrade Template&r."
		""
		"They each have 1 &4Heart&r of Damage more and even more Durability!"
	]
	quest.60B23990691359FD.title: "&9Warden&r Weapons"
	quest.611C662B0F5C553D.quest_desc: [
		"After conquering the mighty &7&lSilver Dungeon&r&f and defeating the &b&lValkyrie Queen&r&f, you probably expected some legendary power… not farming gear. "
		""
		"Still, even heroes have to grow crops sometimes, so give that &b&lValkyrie Hoe&r&f a swing and make the fields proud."
	]
	quest.611C662B0F5C553D.quest_subtitle: "&f&lUse a &b&lValkyrie Hoe&r&f&l"
	quest.611C662B0F5C553D.title: "I defeated the Silver Dungeon and all I got was this stupid Hoe"
	quest.6130F2E6CE78574F.title: "&l&9End Bounty:&r&e Endermen"
	quest.6146643E85C33F32.quest_desc: [
		"Craft the &bCobblemon Smartphone&r and unlock its powerful features! "
		""
		"With this essential device, you can:  "
		""
		"- Use &aPokeHeal&r every 15 minutes to keep your team in top condition.  "
		""
		"- Access your &bPC&r every 5 seconds for rapid management of your Pokémon."
	]
	quest.6146643E85C33F32.quest_subtitle: "Craft your smartphone to enhance your Pokémon management!"
	quest.6146643E85C33F32.title: "Get Your Cobblemon Smartphone!"
	quest.619B886D9F37EDBC.quest_subtitle: "The Second Upgrade"
	quest.619B886D9F37EDBC.title: "&fIron Chest"
	quest.61B0A8FD090876F7.quest_desc: [
		"Looks like someone flipped the ON switch this time! "
		""
		"&4The Prowler&r is a miniboss guarding the &4Ancient Factory&r. He has 640 &4Hearts&r."
		""
		"He has 3 attacks. The Saw for close up Enemies. And for farther Enemies he has Shoulder Missiles, similar to the WASW, and a Laser from his eye."
		""
		"On death he'll drop Redstone and Iron."
		""
		"(Tip he's also weak to the EMP attacks)"
	]
	quest.61B0A8FD090876F7.title: "&4The Prowler&r"
	quest.61FACFDDF439CCF5.quest_desc: [
		"The Mazebreaker is a special pickaxe that is rarely found in Labyrinths."
		""
		"This pickaxe will take 1 damage when breaking Maze Walls, instead of the 16 damage for all other pickaxes!"
	]
	quest.61FBBCE88A7A85A7.quest_subtitle: "Has no effect."
	quest.62431D06A11D1335.quest_desc: [
		"The largest and most dangerous &cRot Mob&r."
		""
		"They have 80 Hearts. "
		""
		"Like all &cRot Mobs&r they will target &2Stoneborns&r and &7Forgottens&r and will drop &cUtheric Shards&r."
	]
	quest.62431D06A11D1335.title: "&cRotbeast&r"
	quest.62673762667192DD.quest_desc: [
		"It's time to go to the &2Swamps&r! In the &2Swamps&r, you'll find an odd-looking hill with an entrance on top. This is the &cMinoshroom Labyrinth&r!"
		""
		"Inside, you'll fight several new enemies that can drop &eMaze Map Focus&r. This is needed to make a &eMaze Map&r."
		""
		"This is a special map that will map your way around the &cMinoshroom Labyrinth&r. Minimaps have no power here."
		""
		"You can also find several loot rooms with special loot for the Maze!"
	]
	quest.62673762667192DD.title: "&2To the Swamps!"
	quest.6281B9027770BC0F.quest_desc: ["More Filtering Options"]
	quest.6281B9027770BC0F.title: "&eAdvanced Alchemy Upgrade"
	quest.6337E186C8692D5E.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Twilight Forest&r is a mod that adds the Twilight Forest dimension to the game. This dimension is filled with brand new items, biomes, mobs and bosses!"
		""
		"To create the portal to get to the &9Twilight Forest&r, make a 2x2 hole in the ground and fill it with water. Surround the edges of the hole with flowers, and throw a Diamond into the water."
		""
		"Assuming you did it correctly, Thor will give you a sign and the portal will activate."
	]
	quest.6337E186C8692D5E.quest_subtitle: "Enter the Twilight Forest"
	quest.6337E186C8692D5E.title: "Welcome to the &9Twilight Forest&r!"
	quest.6353A39CBEE599A0.quest_desc: ["You like combining Inventories and making a way of viewing and interacting with all those Inventories with a few simple &6Machines&r similar to &b&lAE2&r and &7&lSophisticated Storage&r? \\n\\nThen, you'll need some &eStock Links&r! \\n\\n&eStock Links&r can be placed on &ePackagers&r to connect to the Inventory the &ePackager&r is connected to. When first placed, a new &eStock Network&r will be created. \\n\\nThese can connect to Chests, Barrels, and even &eVaults&r! \\n\\nYou can also Right Click another &eStock Link&r with a &eStock Link&r in hand to tune them to the same &eNetwork&r. When the new &eStock Link&r is placed onto another &ePackager&r, its Inventory Block will be added to the same &eNetwork&r. \\n\\nIf you'd like to Interact with these &eNetworks&r you'll need other Blocks!"]
	quest.6353A39CBEE599A0.title: "&eStock Link"
	quest.635FC246BCAE7D3E.quest_desc: [
		"This map is a must have for the &9Twilight Forest&r."
		""
		"Using a &eBlank Magic Map&r will give you a map that shows icons for nearby bosses and structures."
	]
	quest.635FC246BCAE7D3E.title: "&eMagic Map"
	quest.63B78BAEF8EAE9B2.quest_desc: [
		"&aArmor Trims&r are items used to add trims to your armor! This can be done in Smithing Tables."
		""
		"While they do have a recipe, most of the trims are rare finds in from loot chests or archaeology digs. Once you find one, you can dupe the Template by using the recipe to create more!"
	]
	quest.63B78BAEF8EAE9B2.title: "&dArmor Trims"
	quest.63DEEB7D63A0F6C8.quest_desc: ["Barrels work the same as Chests only they can't be combined together into 1. They look cool though."]
	quest.63DEEB7D63A0F6C8.title: "Barrel"
	quest.64490FC548C8487F.quest_desc: ["The &cEye of Monstrous&r will take you to the &cSoul BlackSmith&r to fight the &c&lNetherite Monstrousity&r."]
	quest.64490FC548C8487F.title: "&cEye of Monstrous&r"
	quest.646EEDA7125B3AD0.quest_desc: [
		""
		"&fThe &8&lDried Ghast Block&r&f is a mysterious relic found in Nether Fossils. &a&lWaterlog it&r&f and wait about 30 minutes to witness a Ghastling come to life."
		""
		"&fEach hydration stage emits sounds and particles, signaling your progress. &d&lBring the block to life&r&f and witness the first step in the Ghast's rebirth."
	]
	quest.646EEDA7125B3AD0.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCraft a &e&lDried Ghast Block&r&f&l using 1 &e&lSoul Sand&r&f&l and 2 &e&lGhast Tears"
	quest.646EEDA7125B3AD0.title: "&6&lQuest: Create a Dried Ghost Block"
	quest.647E69232DF4957E.quest_desc: [
		"To get back to the &2&lOverworld&r, we can leave the same way we came!"
		""
		"Use the &9Heart of the Deep&r on a Frame of &8Reinforced Deepslate&r."
		""
		"Luckily we get one of those within the bottom of the &6Ancient Temple&r."
	]
	quest.647E69232DF4957E.title: "Home, Sweet Home!"
	quest.64860340A5BEBAB9.quest_desc: ["&eTable Cloths&r can either be used to show off &eItems&r, or to sell off &eItems&r! \\n\\nTo set up a Shop, do all the steps from the previous Quest: placing &eStock Links&f, &eStock Tickers&r, and a Mob on a Seat or &cBlaze Burner&r. \\n\\nNow use a &eTable Cloth&r to Interact with the Mob or &cBlaze Burner&r, this will bind the &eTable Cloth&r to that &eStock Ticker&r. \\n\\nPlace down the &eTable Cloth&r and you'll be able to place the &eItems&r you want to sell on top, and the price below. \\n\\nWhen someone buys an &eItem&r, it will send a message to the &eStock Link&r, which will &ePackage&f the &eItems&r bought and take the price."]
	quest.64860340A5BEBAB9.quest_subtitle: "With Table Cloths"
	quest.64860340A5BEBAB9.title: "Shops"
	quest.64B4C6850FD57103.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 55"
	quest.64B4C6850FD57103.title: "Rocket Admin Ariana"
	quest.64ECE673D2CEDBE1.quest_desc: [
		"You can craft the &7Cloggrum Shield&r which acts like a normal Shield."
		""
		"But the &7Battleaxe&r is a rare drop from &7Forgottens&r."
	]
	quest.64ECE673D2CEDBE1.title: "&7Cloggrum&r Weapons"
	quest.64FF7118E29931C0.quest_desc: ["Before we get into the many &eItems&r we can get from the &6Millstone&r, let's talk about how to use it! \\n\\nFirst, it will need some &dRotational Power&r, don't worry it only needs a little. \\n\\nThen, you'll need to Drop the &eItem&r you want &6Milled&r, into the top of the &6Millstone&r. After it gets &6Milled&r, just Right Click the &6Millstone&r to take out your &eItems&r. \\n\\nNow, what &eItems&r can we get from the &6Millstone&r? We can get Dyes from pretty much every Flower, we can crush &7Stone&r into Gravel or other &7Stone&r like Blocks into similar Gravel Items. You can even get Wheat Flour from Wheat!"]
	quest.64FF7118E29931C0.title: "&6Millstone"
	quest.651854F26339C479.quest_desc: [
		"&3Soundproof Glass&r is made by combining &3Soul Dust&r and Glass."
		""
		"These work at dampening Sound just like Wool! If a &3Sculk Sensor &for &3Shrieker&r has one covering them, they won't hear Sounds."
		""
		"Just these you can see through!"
	]
	quest.651854F26339C479.title: "&3Soundproof Glass"
	quest.656731AF4AA24087.quest_desc: [
		"To share your quests with your friends, you need to create a team."
		""
		"To do this, type the command: \"/ftbteams party create\" or use the menu at top left."
		""
		"From here, you can click on Settings to configure your team (name, color, description, etc.)."
		""
		"Now you can add your friends from the same interface and start your shared adventure together."
	]
	quest.656731AF4AA24087.quest_subtitle: "Read my description!"
	quest.65D54FFA5634393F.quest_desc: ["Allows the Backpack to pick up items."]
	quest.65EDD3D3CF0FD9C9.quest_subtitle: "Reduces the accuracy of enemy pokemon's moves by 10%."
	quest.66433FD189A824CD.quest_desc: ["A war veteran and electric-type specialist, Lt. Surge once powered up entire bases with his Raichu. He believes in shock-and-awe strategies."]
	quest.66433FD189A824CD.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 34"
	quest.66433FD189A824CD.title: "Lt. Surge"
	quest.666694CA697DE16A.quest_desc: [
		"To find this egg, you'll need to brush away &aSuspicious Sand&r in Warm Ocean Ruins."
		""
		"You can place the Egg into the world and it will slowly hatch into a &dSnifflet&r. This takes around 20 minutes to hatch normally, but can be placed on a Moss block to double the hatch speed, taking only 10 minutes to hatch."
		""
		"The Snifflet will eventually grow into an adult &dSniffer&r that can sniff up items like &2Torchflower Seeds&r or &2Pitcher Pods&r when they wander over blocks they can dig in."
		""
		"You can breed 2 adult Sniffers by using Torchflowers."
	]
	quest.666694CA697DE16A.title: "&aThe &5Sniffer"
	quest.66BD07A623B86118.quest_desc: [
		"It's easy to get lost in the &9Twilight Forest&r. In your travels, you'll run into &5Obsidian Pillars&r."
		""
		"These pillars will have &8Ravens&r around them. Kill them and they'll drop their feathers, which you can use to create a map for the &9Twilight Forest&r!"
	]
	quest.66C394E051EE5744.quest_desc: [
		"You can view your Pokédex by right clicking whilst holding the item"
		""
		"Pokémon can be added to the Pokédex by holding right click whilst holding the item and scanning the Pokémon, by fighting a Pokémon, or by capturing the Pokémon."
		""
		"Scanning a Pokémon instead of capturing them will only display minimal information."
	]
	quest.66C394E051EE5744.quest_subtitle: "Professor Oak entrusted you with a Pokédex. Use it to keep track of the Pokémon you encounter!"
	quest.66C394E051EE5744.title: "Obtain The Pokédex"
	quest.66DDD4FB344DF409.quest_desc: [
		"The &d&lEnder Guardian&r is a hulking beast of Endstone, &dPurpur&r, and &5Obsidian&r that waits within the &dVoid Altar&r."
		""
		"It has 13,320 &4Hearts&r and careful not to get too close or you might be sucked closer to him!"
		"He has a ton of attacks and abilities, one being a very simple punch for those who are too close to his personal space, or a slam which will knock you back."
		""
		"If you are farther from him, he might close the gap by charging and knocking into you. Or he might stomp and produce &dVoid Runes&r to hit you! He can also send &dShulker Balls&r in a row."
		""
		"Also remember when I said he can suck you closer to him? Yeah he does that with a thing called a &dVoid Typhon&r, which he can also summon at your Feet to get you stuck. After you are there for too long, it will explode, most likely damaging you in the process."
		""
		"When you get him to half &4Health&r, his Mask will break revealing his true Head! In anger he will destroy the floor of the arena taking you both to the lower level. "
		""
		"Now he will suck you in more, send more &dVoid Runes&r after you, and attack faster and stronger!"
	]
	quest.66DDD4FB344DF409.title: "&d&lEnder Guardian&r"
	quest.66EEE47B1B3CF954.quest_desc: [
		"&fThe &a&lStaff of Life&r&f is a divine tool that channels pure energy from the &d&lNether Star&r&f, infused through the &b&lEnd Rod&r&f, and purified by the &c&lGrim Reaper's&r&f scythe."
		""
		"&fWith it, you can bring back villagers who have died, but at a cost."
		""
		"&fTo use the staff, simply &6&lright-click the tombstone&r&f of a fallen villager while holding it in your hand. Each use consumes part of its power, and it can only be used &c&l10 times&r&f before breaking."
		""
		"&fA tool of redemption and hope, the Staff of Life is the light that counters darkness."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lCrafting Recipe:"
		""
		"Combine the following items in a crafting table:"
		""
		"&f&l■ &d&l1 Nether Star&r"
		""
		"&f&l■ &b&l1 End Rod&r"
		""
		"&f&l■ &c&l1 Grim Reaper's Scythe&r"
		""
		"Once forged, the &a&lStaff of Life&r&f becomes the ultimate symbol of mercy, a weapon once used for death, now reborn to grant life."
	]
	quest.66EEE47B1B3CF954.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCraft the &a&lStaff of Life&r&f - a sacred artifact capable of reviving fallen villagers and restoring balance to your village&r"
	quest.66EEE47B1B3CF954.title: "&6&lQuest: Forge the Staff of Life"
	quest.672F9CF5B0E626F1.quest_desc: ["&ePackagers&r are the new and very important &6Machine&r for &6&lCreate&r. In order to use pretty much everything from the Update we'll need a &ePackager&r. \\nCombine some of our new-found &eCardboard&r to make a Block of Cardboard. No, these aren't &eBoxes&r yet and they certainly don't do anything. \\n\\nWell besides Crafting our &ePackager&r! The &ePackager&r will then be placed onto a Block with an Inventory, like Chest or Barrel. You'll know it is connected when one of the sides changes to appear like a wall. \\n\\nThen, when given a &4Redstone Signal&r it will pull all &eItems&r within the Inventory into a &ePackage&r! More on that later! \\n\\nThe &ePackages&r can then be pulled out by Hand or &eBelt&r. You can also send &ePackages&r back into the &ePackager&r to put the &eItems&r back into an Inventory. \\n\\nIf you place and name a Sign on the &ePackager&r it will give all &ePackages&r that it makes an Address."]
	quest.672F9CF5B0E626F1.title: "&ePackagers"
	quest.67477FFF039BCD4A.quest_desc: ["Adds a Stonecutter GUI to the Backpack."]
	quest.67716E3E3CF152FC.quest_desc: [
		"The &b&lValkyries&r&f are fierce warriors, each guarding treasures of divine craftsmanship. "
		""
		"Defeat them in honorable combat to claim a piece of their sacred armor or weaponry. "
		""
		"Wearing their gear is both a mark of triumph and a &e&lpromise of greater battles ahead&r&f."
	]
	quest.67716E3E3CF152FC.quest_subtitle: "&f&lObtain a piece of &b&lValkyrie Equipment&r&f&l from the &7&lSilver Dungeon&r&f&l"
	quest.67716E3E3CF152FC.title: "&7&lQuest: Valkyrie’s Legacy"
	quest.67A46ED73E488CEE.quest_desc: ["&dGearshifts&r work similar to a &dClutch&r by connecting to our Systems and being powered by &4Redstone&r. \\n\\nInstead of stopping &dRotational Power&r though, the &dGearshift&r will change its Direction! \\n\\nIf it is going &e&oClockwise&r into the powered &dGearshift&r, it will come out &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r, and vice versa."]
	quest.67A46ED73E488CEE.title: "&dGearshift"
	quest.67AE1D3227C1ACBC.quest_desc: [
		"&eAncient Metal&r is a Drop from pretty much everything within the &eCursed Pyramid&r!"
		""
		"Like other Ingots it can be Crafted from Nuggets or Blocks and vice versa."
		""
		"You can use it to make &eBone Reptile Armor&r or the &eAncient Spear&r."
	]
	quest.67AE1D3227C1ACBC.title: "&eAncient Metal"
	quest.681E5AFEFF98A15E.quest_desc: [
		"The first boss you'll have to kill on your adventure in the &9Twilight Forest&r can be found within the Courtyard."
		""
		"The &2Naga&r is a green serpent made up of multiple segments, as you deal damage to it, it's segments will disappear."
		""
		"Killing the &2Naga&r will drop some nice items and grant you entry to the home of the next boss, the Lich."
	]
	quest.681E5AFEFF98A15E.title: "&2Evening The Scales"
	quest.6820971BCE28A131.quest_desc: ["Ender Chests all share the same inventory and that inventory is different for every player. They can't be combined together into 1."]
	quest.687AC3778C902020.quest_desc: ["The &eCharm of Keeping III&r works the same as the other Charms of Keeping, but stops you from losing all of the stuff in your inventory"]
	quest.687AC3778C902020.title: "&eCharm of Keeping III"
	quest.6893D537716AA748.quest_desc: ["&dCogwheels&r (&dCogs&r) are the next Block needed to use &dRotational Power&r! They can connect to &8Shafts&r or other &dCogs&r to move the &dRotational Power&r. \\n\\nThere is two versions of &dCogs&r: regular &dCogs &fand &dLarge Cogs&r. They will both act the same in the sense of &dRotational Power&r but there is also a few changes! \\nRegular &dCogs&r can connect to other &dCogs&r adjacent to them. This will move the &dRotational Power&r into a whole different direction. When this happens the direction of the second &dCog&r will be reversed. If the first &dCog&r is rotating &e&oClockwise&r, the second one will rotate &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r. \\n\\n&dLarge Cogs&r are a little more difficult to use than &dCogs&r. They can't connect to other &dLarge Cogs&r adjacent, rather they can only connect to &dCogs&r that are diagonal to them! \\n\\nMost &6Machines&r will need &dRotational Power&r from connecting &dCogs&r. You'll recognize if the &6Machine&r has an internal &dCog&r, that is what must be moved in order to use the &6Machine&r. "]
	quest.6893D537716AA748.quest_subtitle: "I just call them Cogs"
	quest.6893D537716AA748.title: "&dCogwheels&r!"
	quest.68A4E69B125DE2BE.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Ancient Temple&r is the important and necessary Structure found within the &9Deeplands&r."
		""
		"It looks like a Mayan Pyramid made of &8Deepslate &fand &3Sculk&r. There's tons of &3Sculk Sensors &fand &3Shriekers&r as well as Chests and Ancient Vases. "
		""
		"Within the higher floors you'll find mostly just Chests and Ancient Vases but within the &6Pyramid&r we'll find even &eBlocks of Gold&r and other Materials."
	]
	quest.68A4E69B125DE2BE.title: "&6Ancient Temples"
	quest.68A88E55766E114B.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 73"
	quest.68A88E55766E114B.title: "Trainer May"
	quest.68D7D893EB074476.quest_desc: ["The &9Eye of Storm&r will take you to the &9Acropolis&r to fight &9&lScylla&r."]
	quest.68D7D893EB074476.title: "&9Eye of Storm"
	quest.6903306E84DEFAC8.quest_desc: ["Engage in and win 50 Pokémon battles! Whether you’re facing wild Pokémon or challenging trainers, every victory brings you closer to becoming a master trainer. Test your strategy, fine-tune your team, and let your skills shine on the battlefield."]
	quest.6903306E84DEFAC8.quest_subtitle: "Prove Your Battling Prowess"
	quest.6903306E84DEFAC8.title: "50 Pokémon Battles"
	quest.6979CE9037A4556B.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Ice-type moves."
	quest.69BE77718F7E7D14.quest_desc: [
		"The &4Meat Shredder&r is a Melee weapon you can make from &4Witherite&r."
		""
		"It has two attacks, either using Left Click or Right Click. "
		""
		"When you Left Click it'll use the &4Meat Shredder&r like an Axe, hitting them once from a decent range."
		""
		"When you hit Right Click it will repeatedly shred them with it's Saw, doing much quicker Damage from closer."
	]
	quest.69BE77718F7E7D14.title: "&4Meat Shredder"
	quest.69DD2FFBBB121866.quest_desc: [
		"Ancient Armor is what's worn by &7Forgottens&r, and is where you can get it from."
		""
		"There isn't any Ancient Boots"
	]
	quest.69DD2FFBBB121866.title: "Ancient Armor"
	quest.69EE22CB4FF1E591.quest_desc: ["&aContraptions&r are very difficult to understand but pretty much it is the art of combining different Blocks and &6Machines&r into one moving systems. \\n\\nYou'll need &6Machines&r to actually move the &aContraption&r like &aLinear Chasis&r, you'll need the &6Machines&r you want to work like &6Drills&r, and you'll need &aGlue&r to hold it all together! \\n\\nOnce it is all &aGlued&r it should move when &dRotational Power&r is given to the moving &6Machine&r of the &aContraption&r."]
	quest.69EE22CB4FF1E591.title: "&a&lContraptions"
	quest.6A3C2EB3BB34CBF9.quest_desc: [
		"The &9&lWarden&r. The most difficult boss in &2&lMinecraft&r, of course being within the most difficult Structure."
		""
		"He's spawned from a &3Sculk Shrieker&r being activated 3 times, or any amount after the first &9&lWarden&r."
		""
		"He has 500 &4Hearts&r and does a ton of Damage from either hitting you with his fists or his &bSonic Blast&r!"
		""
		"He does have a weakness though, that being that he is Blind. He can only find you with Sound, or Smell if you are close enough! Keep your distance, like 23 Blocks up."
	]
	quest.6A3C2EB3BB34CBF9.title: "Kill the &9&lWarden&r"
	quest.6A4443F781B53376.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the holder's critical hit ratio."
	quest.6A4B75D117C733CE.quest_desc: [
		"The Smog Spires are where all the Smog comes from! Well not all, we can't discredit the &2Mogs&r and &3S'mogs&r."
		""
		"Here you will find Blisterberries, Coarse Deepsoil, and Smog Vents."
	]
	quest.6A4B75D117C733CE.title: "Smog Spires"
	quest.6AD9A1A2513B7C59.quest_desc: ["With your fossil identified, it's time to take a closer look! The Fossil Analyzer will provide more details about its origins and potential restoration."]
	quest.6AD9A1A2513B7C59.quest_subtitle: "A deeper look into ancient remains!"
	quest.6B17BEF57BEBCD71.quest_desc: ["Adds a tank to the Backpack."]
	quest.6B8B3DA140355D5E.quest_desc: [
		"The Barren Wasteland of the &5End&r now has 1 more resident."
		""
		"The other being the &dEnder Dragon&r of course!"
	]
	quest.6B8B3DA140355D5E.title: "&5End&r"
	quest.6BB636CC57EA5163.quest_desc: ["The &bIce bow&r can be found randomly in loot chests, it will inflict Slowness III for 10 seconds on hit."]
	quest.6BB636CC57EA5163.title: "&bIce Bow"
	quest.6BF70C2C439F99CA.quest_desc: [
		"&eKobolediators&r are one of the two mini-bosses within the &eCursed Pyramid&r."
		""
		"They will remain dormant until a Player walks near them and they will wake up."
		""
		"They have 1080 &4Hearts&r and will inflict Mining Fatigue on you."
		""
		"They will swing their Sword at you if you get too close! If you gain some distance from them, they will charge at you as if you were holding a Football and running for the endzone! "
		""
		"On death they will drop Koboleton Bones, Ancient Metal Ingots, and their Skull!"
	]
	quest.6BF70C2C439F99CA.title: "&eKobolediator"
	quest.6C1002EE8CB7193E.quest_desc: ["Compacts items in the backpack to their 3x3 recipe."]
	quest.6C1002EE8CB7193E.title: "&eAdvanced Compacting Upgrade"
	quest.6C1EA08DCA40B73F.quest_desc: [
		"&5&n&lAffix Items:&r&r&r"
		""
		"The main feature of Apotheosis is Affixes, a means of strengthening any item you may find (from vanilla or other mods). Affixes are applied to an item, much like Enchantments, but have very different rules. Each affix item has a Rarity, which controls what types of affixes it will receive and how strong they are. "
		""
		""
		"&5&n&lFinding Affix Items:&r&r&r"
		""
		"Affix Items can be found in many ways. They're located in loot chests, and will be dropped by random entities that spawn in your world. The rarity of the affix items you'll find will depend on your &lWorld Tier&r."
		""
		"Once you've found some affix items, you can break them down in the Salvaging Table to obtain Rarity Materials, a currency which will allow you to make your own affix items in the Reforging Table. Though you'll also need a couple Gems, which you can find from similar sources."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&5&n&lWorld Tiers:&r&r&r"
		""
		"Apotheosis adds &lWorld Tiers&r, a progression system for you, your gear, and your enemies. You can access the World Tier Selection screen by pushing the hotkey (default: &cCTRL+T&r)."
		""
		"There are five World Tiers in total, from lowest to highest difficulty:"
		""
		"1. &aHaven&r - The start of your journey, and the easier tier."
		""
		"2. &6Frontier&r - The first tier of increased difficulty, where you'll start to see more affix items and stronger enemies."
		""
		"3. &bAscent&r - For experienced adventurers, this tier has even stronger enemies still."
		""
		"4. &dSummit &r- Only available after slaying the Wither, Epic Gear is commonly found in this Tier"
		""
		"5. &4Pinnacle&r - The final and most difficult tier; but also the best source of Mythic items."
		""
		"Progressing through the tiers requires that you complete the Unlock Criteria for each one; these get progressively more difficult, but are quite worthwhile."
		""
		"Increasing your World Tier will allow you to get better loot, and will give you some direct bonuses, but will also increase the strength of every enemy in your world."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For more detailed information, refer to the guidebook, &5The Chronicle of Shadows.&r If you lose the one given as a reward. You can create another one with a book and a gold ingot."
	]
	quest.6C1EA08DCA40B73F.quest_subtitle: "All things that should have been."
	quest.6C1EA08DCA40B73F.title: "Apotheosis"
	quest.6C7278A53D2842F7.quest_desc: [
		"&fBy channeling the power of &e&lAmbrosium Shards&r&f through an &a&lAltar&r&f, you can transform raw &d&lGravitite Ore&r&f into &d&lEnchanted Gravitite&r&f."
		""
		"&fThis mystical material has gravity-defying properties and is used to craft powerful tools, armor, and blocks that can even lift themselves into the air."
	]
	quest.6C7278A53D2842F7.quest_subtitle: "&f&lUse an &a&lAltar&r&f &lto obtain &d&lEnchanted Gravitite&r&f"
	quest.6C7278A53D2842F7.title: "&7&lQuest: Enchanted Gravitite Creation"
	quest.6C8C8CC1BA55878B.quest_desc: ["&fPlace a &b&lBook of Lore&r&f inside another &b&lBook of Lore&r&f."]
	quest.6C8C8CC1BA55878B.title: "&7&lQuest: Lore-ception!"
	quest.6C93EB7A89510C96.quest_desc: [
		"In this modpack, quests are optional. Mods are not gated behind completing any quests!"
		""
		"Some quest have multiple pages so be on the look out, so you don't miss any important info."
		""
		"There are not quests on everything in this modpack, so explore and discover all the secrets this modpack has to offer. Quest are simply here to stimulate your adventure and guide you, earning you rewards along the way. "
		""
		"Hover your mouse over the left side of the quest screen (white triangle) to access more Quests."
		""
		"You can also click and drag to move the quest screen around, and CTRL + The Scroll Wheel to zoom in and out."
	]
	quest.6C93EB7A89510C96.quest_subtitle: "Read my description!"
	quest.6CC83F9AF65E8327.quest_desc: ["These Mushrooms look pretty normal... "]
	quest.6CC83F9AF65E8327.title: "Veil Mushroom Bog"
	quest.6D64048230FBA067.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Octohost&r is actually 2 Mobs working together! To Kill you!"
		""
		"It has the &9Symbiocto&r which controls the &9Drowned Host&r."
		""
		"&9Symbiocto&r has 8 &4Hearts&r and no Armor. When on its own, it will just Shoot &0Ink&r at you. On Death they will Drop &0Ink Sacs&r."
		""
		"The &9Drowned Host&r acts like a normal &9Drowned&r. They have 10 &4Hearts&r as well as 2 Armor Points. &9Drowned Host&r can Spawn with Armor and Weapons which they can use."
		""
		"When together, they will use their Attacks on you at the same time. The &9Symbiocto&r will Shoot you with &0Ink&r while the &9Drowned Host&r will use Weapons or Fists to Hit you."
	]
	quest.6D64048230FBA067.title: "&9Octohost"
	quest.6DBA786BA0C971FD.quest_subtitle: "Holder's Defense and Sp. Defense is boosted by 50% if they are still able to evolve."
	quest.6DEA367FA2A4EB57.quest_desc: ["The &6Charm of Keeping I&r will prevent you from losing the items in your main hand and off-hand, as well as any armor you're wearing when you die."]
	quest.6DEA367FA2A4EB57.title: "&6Charm of Keeping I"
	quest.6E7AC2D38E3A121C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Ancient City&r is only the most dangerous Structure in &2&lVanilla Minecraft&r. So of course that is just the start to &3&lDeeper and Darker&r! "
		""
		"Here we can find &3Sculk&r galore, along with Loot and the &9&lWarden&r. We'll also find the Portal Frame made of &8Reinforced Deepslate&r."
		""
		"But until then, Loot all you can! And be careful of the..."
	]
	quest.6E7AC2D38E3A121C.title: "Visit an &6Ancient City&r"
	quest.6EE7C27AECB2B03C.quest_subtitle: "Raises the holder's Attack and Sp. Atk by 2 stages when holder is hit by a super effective move."
	quest.6F09A59BBB0C9308.quest_desc: ["Sabrina's psychic powers awakened as a child, fracturing her personality. Cold and calculating, she battles as if she can read your mind."]
	quest.6F09A59BBB0C9308.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 59"
	quest.6F09A59BBB0C9308.title: "Sabrina"
	quest.6F15919BECA3065F.quest_desc: [
		"&fThe &6&lWedding Ring&r&f symbolizes love and commitment, the key to starting your new family in &6&lMinecraft Comes Alive: Reborn&r&f. Once your relationship with a villager reaches &c&l100 Hearts&r&f or more, you can gift this ring to them to get married."
		""
		"&fTo craft it, use the same pattern as the &6&lMatchmaker's Ring&r&f: Place &6&l8 Gold Ingots&r&f around the edges of the crafting grid, leaving the center empty."
		""
		"&fNote: This item only works when gifted to a villager with whom you share a strong relationship."
		""
		"&fOnce married, new interactions and family options will become available."
		""
		"&fForge your bond, share your life, and let your story begin together."
	]
	quest.6F15919BECA3065F.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCraft a &6&lWedding Ring&r&f and prepare to marry your true love&r"
	quest.6F15919BECA3065F.title: "&6&lQuest: Craft the Wedding Ring"
	quest.6F2BBC6D860739C8.quest_desc: [
		"The &bBurning Arena&r is a giant Colosseum-esque Arena within the &4Nether&r."
		""
		"You'll arrive at the peaceful but hot 1st floor, on the 2nd floor you'll find &b|gnited Revenants&r which you'll need to kill for &bBurning Ashes&r."
		""
		"Which can then be used on the 3rd floor, in the Altar to summon the &b&lIgnis&r!"
		""
		"Looking for Loot? check above the 3rd floor!"
	]
	quest.6F2BBC6D860739C8.title: "&bBurning Arena&r: Home of the &b&lIgnis&r"
	quest.6F7071050766287B.quest_desc: [
		"&bGlowing Roots&r spawn in &bBlooming Caverns&r."
		""
		"They don't do anything."
	]
	quest.6F7071050766287B.title: "&bGlowing Roots"
	quest.6F92395551585052.quest_desc: [
		"&fA &c&lHarness&r&f allows you to ride and control a Happy Ghost. &a&lCustomize its color&r&f by using different wool colors during crafting. &b&lYou can re-dye it&r&f anytime in the crafting grid or remove it with Shears."
		""
		"&fCraft your first &c&lHarness&r&f and prepare to take flight."
	]
	quest.6F92395551585052.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCraft a &c&lHarness&r&f&l using 8 &6&lLeather&r&f&l and 2 &f&lGlass Blocks&r&f&l, and 1 &6&lWool Block"
	quest.6F92395551585052.title: "&6&lQuest: Craft a Harness"
	quest.7007B6DC65FCDB84.quest_desc: [
		"To find these we'll need a little archeology!"
		""
		"In the giant shaft you'll take to get to the &e&lAncient Remnant&r, there are 3 rooms on the sides of it."
		""
		"2 of these rooms have Suspicious Sand which you can use a Brush on to get Loot! Including the &eNecklace of Desert&r."
		""
		"Then, Right Click the &e&lAncient Remnant&r with the &eNecklace of Desert&r to resurect it!"
	]
	quest.7007B6DC65FCDB84.title: "&eNecklace of the desert"
	quest.703C645B9FD9515C.quest_desc: [
		"The smallest and weakest of the &cRot Mobs&r."
		""
		"These have 5 Hearts."
		""
		"Like all &cRot Mobs&r they will target &2Stoneborns&r and &7Forgottens&r and will drop &cUtheric Shards&r."
	]
	quest.703C645B9FD9515C.title: "&cRotling&r"
	quest.70833FCBB5879138.title: "&l&cNether Bounty:&r&e Wither Skeletons"
	quest.70F1326CC1916E34.quest_desc: [
		"FTBChunks lets you claim chunks to secure your builds and valuables. Once claimed, these chunks will be protected from damage by other players and mobs."
		""
		"&nHow to Claim Chunks.&r"
		"Open your map (default: &cM&r). Hold right-click and drag to select the chunks you wish to claim. When you release right-click, choose the option \"Claim Selected\". If you wish to force-load a chunk, simply right-click the claimed chunk and choose the option \"Forceload Selected\". Right-click a claimed chunk and select the option \"Unclaim Selected\" to unclaim a chunk."
	]
	quest.70F1326CC1916E34.quest_subtitle: "Protect your base with FTBChunks"
	quest.7125E67E0FE9BA2C.quest_desc: [
		"&fMoa Eggs can be found throughout the &b&lAether&r&f, often guarded by their majestic parents."
		""
		"&fThese colorful eggs hold the key to taming your own flying companion, an essential ally for exploring the skylands."
		""
		"&fAdult &b&lMoas&r&f lay an egg of their respective color every five to ten minutes, so keep an eye on them if you want to collect your own."
	]
	quest.7125E67E0FE9BA2C.quest_subtitle: "&f&lHave a &b&lMoa Egg&r&f in your inventory"
	quest.7125E67E0FE9BA2C.title: "&7&lQuest: Egg of the Skies"
	quest.7130247B52A42CE0.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Poison-type moves."
	quest.718786CD52340FFA.quest_subtitle: "The Third Upgrade"
	quest.718786CD52340FFA.title: "&eGold Backpack"
	quest.7194CBAA70C4A575.quest_desc: [
		"&dVoid Scatter Arrows&r are Crafted with a Spectral Arrow and a &dVoid Jaw&r."
		""
		"They can be shot by any Bow or Crossbow. When they hit any Mob or Block they will break apart."
		""
		"When they break apart, many parts will be thrown around the area, damaging whatever they hit!"
	]
	quest.7194CBAA70C4A575.title: "&dVoid Scatter Arrows"
	quest.71B1B53A03A16296.quest_desc: ["&bPortable Fluid Interfaces&r are used with &aContraptions&r that are using &bFluid Tanks&r. \\n\\nIn order to access the &bFluid Tanks&r you'll need two &bPortable Fluid Interfaces&r, one connected to the &aContraption&r and one connected to &bFluid Pipes&r. \\n\\nThe &bPortable Fluid Interfaces&r will need a 1 or 2 Block gap between a meeting point in order for them to work. \\n\\nIf we have all that, the &bPortable Fluid Interface&r connected to the &aContraption&r will stop the &aContraption&r to either take &bFluids&r in or out from the second &bPortable Fluid Interface&r to add it to the &bFluid Tanks&r within the &aContraption&r."]
	quest.71B1B53A03A16296.title: "&bPortable Fluid Interfaces"
	quest.71EA263526E14B1B.quest_desc: ["Boats with Chests are Boats with Chests on them. You can open the chest while you're in the Boat or you can right-click on it. Only one person can ride in the Boat at a time."]
	quest.71EA263526E14B1B.title: "Boats with Chests"
	quest.7242F591DA474B37.quest_desc: ["&bFluids &fand &bLiquids&r aren't the most important in every aspect of &6&lCreate&r, but luck is, you'll most likely run into them anyways! \\n\\nYou'll need to learn the difficult path of &bFluid Logistics&r in order to use and move them. \\n\\nAnd to start, you'll need &cCopper&r!"]
	quest.7242F591DA474B37.title: "&b&lFluid Logistics"
	quest.72537968598AB884.quest_desc: ["&6Engineer's Goggles are perfect for you little know-it-alls. \\n\\nWhen worn it will tell just about everything the Block or &6Machine&r has to tell! \\n\\nStressometers will tell how much Stress is given and how much it can take. Speedometers will tell how much Speed is within your system. \\n\\n&dSteam Boilers&r will tell how big, how much &9Water&r, and how much Heat they have. \\n\\nOther &6Machines&r, like &6Deployers&r or &6Mechanical Presses&r, will show how much Stress Units is being used up."]
	quest.72537968598AB884.title: "&6Engineer's Goggles"
	quest.725F96A97E888C87.quest_subtitle: "Causes a Pokémon that makes direct contact with the holder to take damage."
	quest.728737C55AF5EB56.quest_desc: [
		"&9Ceraunus&r is the Anchor Weapon &9&lScylla&r herself uses!"
		""
		"With just 2 &9Essence of the Storm&r and 3 &9Lacrima&r we can Craft it! Just in a different order than you would for &9Astrape&r."
		""
		"You can swing the Anchor around like a Mace, with a very long delay. Or use it for special attacks!"
		""
		"Hold Right Click to toss the Anchor in front of you. When it hits a Mob, it will Damage them and hit them back."
		""
		"You can also Hold Shift Right Click to instead of throwing the Anchor, you throw &9Waves&r in an array in front of you!"
	]
	quest.728737C55AF5EB56.title: "&9Ceraunus"
	quest.72C7698072BF0F1D.quest_desc: ["The &dHand Crank&r is the simplest and worst form of &dRotational Power&r generation. \\n\\nWhen you hold Right Click it'll move &e&oClockwise&r and if you hold Shift Right Click it will move &9&oCounter-Clockwise&r. \\n\\nIt only gives a tiny bit of Stress Units and will stop after you quit holding it."]
	quest.72C7698072BF0F1D.quest_subtitle: "Manual Power!"
	quest.72C7698072BF0F1D.title: "&dHand Crank"
	quest.72DCE154E1714890.quest_desc: [
		"To see &6Mechanical Saws&r on their own, check out the second Page! This one talks about them in &aContraptions&r. \\n\\nWhen moved in a &aContraption&r, the &6Mechanical Saw&r will break any Tree that it comes in contact with! It will need to hit the bottom of the Tree and break all of the Logs on the lowest part of the Tree. \\n\\nOnce it breaks those Logs, the entire Tree will be cut down into Item form. \\n\\nIf the &aContraption&r has an Inventory, the Tree parts will be collected into it. If not, the Tree will remain in nature... on the ground."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Mechanical Saw&r can also do other tasks when not used in a &aContraption&r. Instead they can be placed down and used with &dRotational Power&r. \\n\\nThe &6Saw&r can also cut down Trees that are near them. Yes, they'll still need to cut down the lowest Logs. \\n\\nBut it can be used as a &7Stonecutter&r/Woodcutter as well! To use it like that it'll need to be placed faced up, like normal. \\n\\nThen, we can either feed it Blocks from our Hands (with the correct protection on) or through &eBelts&r. Logs will be Stripped and Stone Blocks will be Cut. \\n\\nIf the Block has multiple Recipes through the Cutter, you can Filter which one you want by placing that Block in the &6Mechanical Saw's&r Filter."
	]
	quest.72DCE154E1714890.title: "&6Mechanical Saw"
	quest.72FEC10BAC4B10F8.quest_desc: ["Picture the Ancient Sea. Okay now remove all Kelp from it and remove all &bGwibs&r and &bGwiblings&r."]
	quest.72FEC10BAC4B10F8.title: "Dead Sea"
	quest.73046386296DF85F.quest_desc: ["Knightmetal Armor&r can be crafted with Knightmetal Ingots and has a chance of being found in &2Knight Phantom&r chests."]
	quest.73046386296DF85F.title: "Knightmetal Armor"
	quest.73656735CE67C0F0.quest_subtitle: "Doubles the Attack and Sp. Atk of Pikachu when held."
	quest.737DC37E4310090C.quest_desc: ["&8Chain Conveyors&r won't do much on their own. They need another &8Chain Conveyor&f, &8Chains&f, and &dRotational Power&r! \\n&8Chain Conveyors&r will need another &8Chain Conveyor&r near by in order to attach to them with &8Chains&r. \\n\\nThe &8Chains&r will need to be Right Clicked onto 1 &8Chain Conveyor&r then done the same to another you want to connect it to. \\n\\nOnce, one is given &dRotational Power&r, the &8Chains&r will move at the same Speed. Don't worry about Direction, there'll be 2 &8Chains&r! \\n\\nWhen the &8Chains&r are a moving, you can connect to them with a &6Wrench&r to move with the &8Chains&r, you can either press Shift or switch Items to drop off the &8Chain&r. \\n\\nYou can also place &ePackages&r on them, but without the &eItem&r described in the next Quest, they will just go around in a circle!"]
	quest.737DC37E4310090C.title: "&8Chain Conveyor"
	quest.73B0830A01411CC5.quest_subtitle: "Increases the amount of experience earned by the holder in battle."
	quest.73BD43E15A1FD921.quest_desc: [
		"&bBlooming Moss&r comes from the... you guessed it! &bBlooming Caverns&r! "
		""
		"It will spawn on the ground just waiting for you to collect it."
		""
		"They don't spread like normal &2Moss&r nor do they have any Recipes."
	]
	quest.73BD43E15A1FD921.title: "&bBlooming Moss"
	quest.73DF3424DDA073CA.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lKanto Trainer Progression — Radical Red"
		""
		"&fFollow the custom battle line of Radical Trainers to take on Kanto’s most iconic Gym Leaders and rivals!"
		""
		"&9Want to switch to the Radical Red trainer path?  "
		"&rYou can reset your current series by exchanging a &6Emerald&r to switch tracks at any time!"
	]
	quest.73DF3424DDA073CA.title: "&6Kanto Trainer Progression"
	quest.7415FC5300A9E907.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Flying-type moves."
	quest.74502B0B40C88ACB.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the critical hit ratio of a Farfetch'd or Sirfetch'd that holds it by two stages."
	quest.749FAB52D80E38EC.quest_desc: [
		"Do you want to make the &aOverworld&r feel more like the &9Twilight Forest&r?"
		""
		"You can use this powder on animals in the Overworld to convert them into their &9Twilight Forest&r variants."
		""
		"You can find this in dungeon chests in the &9Twilight Forest&r."
	]
	quest.74A1E59031CD0D3B.quest_desc: [
		"&3Sculk Leeches&r can sometimes spawn from broken Ancient Vases."
		""
		"It acts as a little surprise for you when 2 spawn out!"
		""
		"They only have 2 &4Hearts&r and will attack you despise that."
		""
		"On death they will drop &3Soul Dust&r."
	]
	quest.74A1E59031CD0D3B.title: "&3Sculk Leech"
	quest.750F633ED97FBE95.quest_desc: [
		"When the &2Peacock Feather Fan&r is used, entities in front of the player will be pushed backwards"
		""
		"These can occasionally be found in some &2Hollow Hill&r and &eLich Tower&r loot chests."
	]
	quest.750F633ED97FBE95.quest_subtitle: "A Glorified Leafblower"
	quest.753A398477B256C9.quest_desc: [
		"&9Warden Armor&r is direct upgrade to &cNetherite&r. Just use a &9Warden Upgrade Template&r, a &9Reinforced Echo Shard&r, and a piece of &cNetherite Armor&r to make it."
		""
		"Each piece has 1 more Armor Point and 1 more Armor Protection compared to its &cNetherite&r counterpart."
	]
	quest.753A398477B256C9.title: "&9Warden&r Armor"
	quest.754B8F1FBCD983C5.quest_desc: ["&eStock Tickers&r can be set to the &eNetwork&r by Right Clicking the &eStock Link &fwith the &eStock Ticker&r in Hand. \\n\\nThen, place down the &eStock Ticker&r and give it a &eStock Keeper&r by either placing down a &cBlaze Burner&r or a Mob on a Seat nearby. \\n\\nYou'll know they are a &eStock Keeper&r by their stereotypical &aGreen&r Visor. We can now Right Click the &eStock Keeper&r to view and order &eItems&r from our &eNetwork&r. \\n\\nWhen you order &eItems&r, they'll be placed into a &ePackage &ffrom a &ePackager &fbelow the &eStock Link&r."]
	quest.754B8F1FBCD983C5.title: "&eStock Ticker"
	quest.7567D4A1FAE5783D.quest_desc: ["Auto-smelt items in the Backpack."]
	quest.7567D4A1FAE5783D.title: "&eAuto-Blasting Upgrade"
	quest.757F99DB30B2BD1E.quest_desc: [
		"With a Diamond tier pickaxe, you'll be able to mine &dObsidian&r. Obsidian can be used to create a portal to the &cNether&r."
		""
		"The portal frame can be many different sizes, but most go with the basic 'Door' shape. This is a hollow 4x5 shape using a minimum of 10 Obsidian. You don't have to use Obsidian for the corners, just the portal frame itself!"
		""
		"Use flint and steel and light anywhere inside the hollow part. Then just stand inside the portal to be teleported to the &cNether&r."
	]
	quest.757F99DB30B2BD1E.title: "&cTo The Nether&r!"
	quest.758C593B69691A5C.quest_desc: ["Shift-Right Click an inventory to empty."]
	quest.759BD70B51105E78.quest_subtitle: "Provides a chance for the holder to survive a potential KO attack, leaving it with 1 HP."
	quest.75B14A09FE39EDDA.quest_desc: ["Do you like your &aContraptions&r going only on a straight line? Then, the &aGantry Carriage&r is perfect for you! \\n\\nPlace down the &aGantry Shafts&r down in the line you wish your &aContraption&r to go and give it &dRotational Power&r. \\n\\nThen, place down your &aGantry Carriage&r on top of the &aGantry &fand&a Shaft&r and it will move along with it. \\n\\nYou can &aGlue&r Blocks and &6Machines&r on top of the &aGantry Carriage&r to also move with it! \\n\\nThe &aGantry Shafts&r can be stopped by giving it a &4Redstone Signal&r. Do you also notice how they look like those poles Barbershops have?"]
	quest.75B14A09FE39EDDA.quest_subtitle: "Barbershop Poles"
	quest.75B14A09FE39EDDA.title: "&aGantry Carriage"
	quest.75CBB5BD8C1DFEA1.quest_desc: ["The &8Basin&r is similar to the &eDepot&r, but can hold &eItems&r and &bFluids&r. \\n\\nThis will be helpful for using the &6Mechanical Mixer&r to Mix and Brew. \\n\\nAnd with the &6Mechanical Press&r to Autocraft!"]
	quest.75CBB5BD8C1DFEA1.title: "&8Basin"
	quest.760730B7747C31A8.quest_desc: [
		"The Wither is the second Minecraft Boss, this one being more elective."
		""
		"You'll have to build the Wither to spawn him in. Using 4 Soul Sand in a T shape and placing 3 Wither Skeleton Skulls on top will spawn him in!"
		""
		"He has 300 Hearts and will fly around shooting Wither Skulls at Players or Mobs."
		""
		"When taken to half Health he will gain a shield against Projectiles and will need to be killed with a Sword or Axe."
		""
		"Once you kill him he'll drop: Nether Star, chance at a Withering Soul, and a ton of Corail Items."
	]
	quest.7615360CC8A65B7A.quest_desc: [
		"&3Sculk Vines&r are the &3Sculk&r version of &4Weeping Vines&r."
		""
		"They can spawn within &bBlooming Caverns&r and &9Deeplands&r."
	]
	quest.7615360CC8A65B7A.title: "&3Sculk Vines"
	quest.7699FB1A1B0C82D1.quest_desc: ["Here you'll find all of the rewards you can get by slaying enemies."]
	quest.7699FB1A1B0C82D1.quest_subtitle: "Killing All The Things"
	quest.7699FB1A1B0C82D1.title: "Bounty Board"
	quest.769F8CAB4CAC5BE1.quest_desc: [
		"This one is quite unique in its spawning! After you kill the &b&lIgnis&r, there's a chance &bIgnited Berserkers&r will spawn in Nether Fortresses."
		""
		"They are just like &bRevenants&r just instead of Shields they have Swords! Their Swords won't protect against damage like the Shields do, instead they deal more damage."
		""
		"They have much less health, at 65 &4Hearts&r and will drop Dying Embers when killed. 4 Dying Embers can be Crafted into 1 &bBurning Ashes&r"
	]
	quest.769F8CAB4CAC5BE1.title: "&bIgnited Berserker"
	quest.76B6896A7AB0A5E2.quest_desc: [
		"&fKnowledge is power, especially in a world as mysterious as the &b&lAether&r&f."
		""
		"&fThe &b&lBook of Lore&r&f is your personal guide to understanding every block, item, and creature you encounter among the clouds."
		""
		"&fIt provides &a&lin-game information&r&f about Aether content, helping you identify materials, mobs, and special mechanics as you discover them."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lHow to Craft It"
		""
		"&fYou will need:"
		""
		"&6&lBook ×1"
		""
		"&f&7&lFlint&r&f ×1 or &e&lGlowstone Dust&r&f ×1 or &b&lAmbrosium Shard&r&f ×1"
		""
		"&fCrafting any of these combinations with a book will grant you a &b&lBook of Lore&r&f."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lHow It Works"
		""
		"&fRight-click while holding the &b&lBook of Lore&r&f to open it."
		""
		"&fInside, you will find detailed entries for Aether blocks, items, and entities, automatically added as you encounter them in the world."
		""
		"&fIt is the perfect companion for explorers and scholars alike."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&f&lPro Tip"
		""
		"&fKeep your &b&lBook of Lore&r&f handy while adventuring."
		""
		"&fWhen you find a strange new block or item, check its entry before experimenting, the &b&lAether&r&f hides plenty of surprises."
	]
	quest.76B6896A7AB0A5E2.quest_subtitle: "&f&lCraft a &b&lBook of Lore&r&f to learn about the items and secrets of the &b&lAether&r&f"
	quest.76B6896A7AB0A5E2.title: "&7&lQuest: Craft the Book of Lore"
	quest.76BCAF88EB33B84F.quest_desc: [
		"&9Urchinkin&r are small pests who for some reason live in &9Acropolis&r."
		""
		"They have 6 &4Hearts&r with no Armor. Thankfully pretty weak."
		""
		"They have a few Attacks, if they are near you they will Hit you. If there is some distance they will roll at you. When they roll, tons of their &9Spikes&r will be shot out, doing Damage to anyone they hit!"
		""
		"On death they won't Drop anything unique. Besides more &9Spikes&r to Damage you, that's all."
	]
	quest.76BCAF88EB33B84F.title: "&9Urchinkin"
	quest.76CBFA38D021AC95.quest_desc: ["&dWindmills&r are a little more complicated than &9Water Wheels&r, but they also come with more customization and of course Speed and Stress Units! \\n\\nFirst, you'll need the heart of the &dWindmill&r, the &dWindmill Bearing&r. This Block will send the &dRotational Power&r out of it. It is also what we'll use to turn on the &dWindmill&r! \\n\\nThen, you'll need the Blocks to make the actual &dWindmill&r part. Blocks will automatically stick to the &dBearing&r, but to the rest of the &dWindmill&r you'll need &aGlue&r. Besides &dWindmill Sails&r, those attach automatically! \\n\\nWe'll also need atleast 8 &dWindmill Sail&r like Blocks, those being the &dWindmill Sails&r or Wool. The more we have, the faster the &dWindmill&r spins! \\n\\nOnce it is all set, just Right Click the &dBearing&r with an Empty Hand to start it up."]
	quest.76CBFA38D021AC95.title: "&dWindmills"
	quest.770C94D18B5072DB.quest_desc: [
		"The Nature's Compass gives you a list of biomes you can search for."
		""
		"Select a biome, then hit 'Search.' You'll see some info in the top left, and the compass will point in the direction of the biome."
		""
		"The Explorer's Compass works the same but works for structures, instead of biomes."
	]
	quest.770C94D18B5072DB.quest_subtitle: "Helps Find Biomes/Structures"
	quest.770C94D18B5072DB.title: "Compasses for Searching"
	quest.7719567EAB6AABC0.quest_desc: [
		"The &4Mechanical Fusion Anvil&r will be needed to make combinations of &4&lCataclysm&r Items."
		""
		"You can place it down like a normal Anvil, but this one doesn't have Durability... thankfully!"
		""
		"Check JEI for Recipes, you place 1 Item in the Left Slot and the other in the Middle Slot to get the final product in the Right Slot."
	]
	quest.7719567EAB6AABC0.title: "&4Mechanical Fusion Anvil"
	quest.77382D4114E901CB.quest_desc: ["The &bHose Pulley&r is used to take and place full Source Blocks of &bFluids&r, yes not just &9Water&r. \\n\\nFirst, set how far the &bHose&r actually goes down or up with the &8Shaft&r at one side. Either with a &6Cog&f, &8Shaft&r, or &dHand Crank&r which is easiest. \\n\\nThen, on the other side of the &bHose Pulley&r we can put some &bFluid Pipes&r. With &bMechanical Pumps&r we can choose whether the &bHose Pulley&r picks up &bFluid&r Sources or place them down. \\n\\nThe &bHose Pulley&r only has an Inventory of 1.5 Buckets or 1500mB, but the &bFluids&r can be &bPiped&r into other Inventories or &bTanks&r! \\n\\nIf the &9Water&r Source is infinite, the &bHose Pulley&r won't take out Source Blocks, but will keep taking &bFluid&r out. \\n\\nThis will also work with &cLava&r Source Blocks, but those aren't infinite. So you might want to check out &c&lThe Nether&r for that as it is pretty much infinite there!"]
	quest.77382D4114E901CB.title: "&bHose Pulley"
	quest.776EEBB5981B556B.quest_desc: [
		"&4&lCataclsym&r is a mod which adds new bosses, dungeons, and of course loot!"
		""
		"There is no certain pattern of which bosses to kill first, but some are stronger than others, and some give loot that will help against the others."
		""
		"Check out the Eyes to find the specific Structures you'll need to locate!"
	]
	quest.776EEBB5981B556B.title: "&4&lCataclysm"
	quest.779DC1CC07C7AD60.quest_desc: ["Increases stack size in the Backpack by 16."]
	quest.779DC1CC07C7AD60.title: "&dStack Upgrade Tier 4"
	quest.77BE3D9D274F72F1.quest_desc: ["&5Train Stations&r are the most important Blocks for &5Trains&r! We need them for making &5Trains&f, breaking down &5Trains&r, and Scheduling them! \\n\\nTo use them, you'll need to select a &7Train Track&r with them. Hold the &5Train Station&r in your Hand and Right Click a &7Train Track&r. \\n\\nI don't know the max distance a &5Train Station&r can be placed, it is atleast 10 Blocks! (I don't have that much room to test). \\n\\nOnce placed you can Rename it with the Text Bar at the top. \\n\\nYou can also Click \"Create New Train\", to start making your first &5Train&r. After you Clicked it, one of the &7Tracks&r will appear &9Blue&r, this is the &7Track&r you can place &5Boogeys&r on. \\n\\nRight Click that &7Track&r with a &5Train Casing&r to make a &5Boogey&r, AKA &5Train Wheels&r. Right Click the actual Wheels to change its design. Then you can..."]
	quest.77BE3D9D274F72F1.title: "&5Train Stations"
	quest.7818F76D690B4E80.quest_subtitle: "Holder immediately switches out if struck by a damaging move."
	quest.78656C89EEE80DB5.quest_desc: ["&eBrass Tunnels&r work like &eAndesite Tunnels&r just with so many more configurations! \\n\\nFirst, we now get Filters! These are per side: if you Filter the Input side, only that Filter &eItem&r will be allowed to move throught the &eTunnel&r. If you Filter the Output sides, then only those &eItems&r will come out of its side. \\n\\nNow we can also line &eBrass Tunnels&r together. This will allow them to take all the same Inputs but Filter them out to certain &eBelts&r! \\n\\nAt the top of the &eTunnel&r we'll find the option to change its Distribution Modes. I won't explain them in too much detail, our Quests have limited space, instead I'll summarize! \\n\\nSplit: will split the &eItem&r stacks evenly per how many &eBelts&r it will go to. Forced Split: will make sure every &eBelt&r will get an even amount, while normal Split might skip some. Round Robin: will alternate individually between each &eBelt&r. Forced Round Robin: won't skip some &eItems&r and instead will wait, everyone gets a turn! Prefer Nearest: will send the &eItems&r to the closest Output. Randomize: it sends the &eItems&r randomly to different Outputs. Synchronize Inputs: will only Output when every &eBrass Tunnel&r has an &eItem&r waiting to Input."]
	quest.78656C89EEE80DB5.title: "&eBrass Tunnel"
	quest.786BF007CE45212B.quest_desc: ["The &4Eye of Mech&r will take you to the &4Ancient Factory&r to fight &4&lThe Harbinger&r."]
	quest.786BF007CE45212B.title: "&4Eye of Mech&r"
	quest.787BB1C7445D74D7.quest_desc: [
		"&eRegalium&r is the Emerald equivalent in &2&lUndergarden&r."
		""
		"It can't be made into Armor or Tools but it can be used to trade with &2Stoneborns&r for other Items."
	]
	quest.787BB1C7445D74D7.title: "&eRegalium&r"
	quest.788A38DB17BD0DFB.quest_subtitle: "Restore the ancestor of all birds!"
	quest.788A38DB17BD0DFB.title: "The Wings of Prehistory"
	quest.78B846D1B139DA91.quest_desc: [
		"The &5Deeplings&r are an ancient race of sea monsters who live and guard the &5Sunken City&r. They have their own rankings: Anglers, Brutes, Priests, and Warlocks. "
		""
		"&5Deeplings&r are the most basic, only having 13 &4Hearts&r and a Coral Spear."
		""
		"&5Deepling Anglers&r are the next ones, they have 15 &4Hearts&r and hold a Fishing Rod with a &5Lionfish&r attached. The &5Lionfish&r will attack you and give you Poison, they have 6 &4Hearts&r."
		""
		"&5Deepling Brutes&r have 60 &4Hearts&r and hold a Coral Bardiche, which they will use to charge at you in the Water."
		""
		"&5Deepling Warlocks &fand &5Priests&r both have 45 &4Hearts&r and both hold Athame. The &5Priests&r have a ranged attack they can use, while &5Warlocks&r do not!"
	]
	quest.78B846D1B139DA91.title: "&5Deeplings&r"
	quest.790B76A0DA7CDAFD.quest_desc: [
		"&7Scintlings&r are little innocent Slugs found everywhere in the &2&lUndergarden&r."
		""
		"They act like Snow Golems as in they leave a trail wherever they walk. Just this one is more Gooey... "
		""
		"On death they drop Scintling Goo, but you can just farm it from their trails, so why kill them!"
	]
	quest.790B76A0DA7CDAFD.title: "&7Scintling&r"
	quest.791546F389E7FAA4.quest_desc: ["A new power is rising in the skies: the &6&lBrass Boss&r&f, a guardian of the deepest secrets of the &b&lAether&r&f. Its strength surpasses all who came before, a true trial even for veteran sky warriors. Stand against this mechanical menace and prove that no &c&lstorm&r&f, &c&lflame&r&f, or &c&lfury&r&f can break your resolve."]
	quest.791546F389E7FAA4.quest_subtitle: "&f&lDefeat the mighty &6&lBrass Boss&r&f &lin the &b&lAether's&r&f&f &lfinal challenge"
	quest.791546F389E7FAA4.title: "&7&lQuest: Defeat the Brass Boss"
	quest.791E220804B97FB0.quest_desc: [
		"Forgotten Fields are the Plains of the &2&lUndergarden&r. "
		""
		"They don't have Trees but they have plenty of Rocks, Flowers, and Mobs!"
		""
		"They do not spawn &7Forgottens&r though"
	]
	quest.791E220804B97FB0.title: "Forgotten Fields"
	quest.7921C762586B0A86.quest_desc: [
		"&4The Watchers&r... well they watch the &4Ancient Factory&r. They'll attack anything they see (Player wise) with their 'fricken laser beams!' and Blades if they are close enough."
		""
		"They have 12 and a half &4Hearts&r, can fly, and are weak to EMP attacks as well."
		""
		"Like &4The Prowler&r they drop redstone and iron on death."
	]
	quest.7921C762586B0A86.title: "&4The Watchers&r"
	quest.7A050B1A909CC8CD.quest_desc: [
		"The &bBulwark of the Flame&r can be used like a normal Shield but also has a special effect."
		""
		"When Holding Right Click and Shift, letting go will let you charge at whatever is infront of you, like how goats do."
		""
		"Whatever gets hit will take Damage and if pinched against a wall will also get stunned."
	]
	quest.7A050B1A909CC8CD.title: "&bBulwark of the Flame"
	quest.7A7F0869DE427522.quest_desc: [
		"Hit \"&eJ&r\" to open your party summary."
		""
		"If you have not chose a starter it will ask you to select one. before you can view your party."
	]
	quest.7A7F0869DE427522.quest_subtitle: "Every great adventure starts with a choice. Select your starter Pokémon and begin your journey!"
	quest.7A7F0869DE427522.title: "The Beginning of Your Journey"
	quest.7A92C213217218E3.quest_desc: [
		"Who knows what happened to bring this &5City&r under the &9Water&r, but clearly it is! You'll easily notice it by the Stone Bricks sticking out of the &9Water&r."
		""
		"The first and biggest room is the City Center, the giant dome! This is where the &5Altar of the Abyss&r is."
		""
		"Off of the rooms you'll find hallways which lead to other buildings in the &5City&r. Prisons holding &5Coralussus&r and even Treasure Rooms holding tons of precious Loot!"
		""
		"All around the &5City&r you will find its inhabitants, the &5Deeplings&r. "
	]
	quest.7A92C213217218E3.title: "&5Sunken City&r: Home of &5&lThe Leviathan&r"
	quest.7AABA3B3EAD75D20.quest_desc: ["Blaine is a fiery quiz master with a passion for riddles. His volcanic temper is only matched by the heat of his Fire-types."]
	quest.7AABA3B3EAD75D20.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 76"
	quest.7AABA3B3EAD75D20.title: "Blaine"
	quest.7AC25C502EBF4A86.quest_desc: [
		"Skeletons have different varients, like Zombies do!"
		""
		"Strays- spawn in Cold Biomes."
		"Bogged- spawn in Swamps and Trial Chambers."
		"Murks- spawn underwater in Coral Reefs."
		"Verdants- spawn in Jungles."
	]
	quest.7AC25C502EBF4A86.title: "Skeleton Variants"
	quest.7B5E9723F8BEE3F1.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Aptrgangr&r is the mini boss within the &3Frosted Prison&r."
		""
		"They have 800 &4Hearts&r and will attack you with their giant Axe."
		""
		"They can swing their Axe like normal, or they might smash it on the ground near you. When they do that, lasers will spawn damaging all in their path. They also have a charge attack similar to the &eKobolediator&r!"
		""
		"On death they will drop Black Steel Ingots and Nuggets, and Rotten Flesh and Bones."
	]
	quest.7B5E9723F8BEE3F1.title: "&3Aptrgangr"
	quest.7BA25CE95CCAB080.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crystallized Amber&r spawns within &cOvercast Columns&r."
		""
		"You'll need Silk Touch to grab them."
	]
	quest.7BA25CE95CCAB080.title: "&6Crystallized Amber"
	quest.7BE97C935B651AD2.quest_desc: [
		"The &dVoid &4Assault Shoulder Weapon &d(V.&4A.S.W.)&r is just like the Wither version but better!"
		""
		"Now it only shoots &dVoid &4Howitzers&r which will do more Damage and cause &dVoid Runes&r to come out of the ground, in the area the &4Howitzer&r hit."
		""
		"Just at the cost of the long cooldown, but we've got time to wait."
		""
		"It can crafted by combining the &4W.A.S.W.&r and a &dVoid Core&r in the &4Mechanical Infusion Anvil&r."
	]
	quest.7BE97C935B651AD2.title: "&dVoid &4Assault Shoulder Weapon"
	quest.7C010DBAEDEF8C3F.quest_desc: [
		"A giant Green Jungle with huge Gronglegrowth Trees."
		""
		"On those Trees you can find &eGronglets&r!"
	]
	quest.7C010DBAEDEF8C3F.title: "Gronglegrowth"
	quest.7C4EA3E09D1BE3F9.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Wrath of the &eDesert&r is a combination of the &3Cursed Bow&r and &eSandstorm in a Bottle&r."
		""
		"This Bow doesn't shoot Arrows like normal, instead it will shoot &3Cursed &eSandstorms&r! "
		""
		"Three of them to be exact! "
		""
		"It also doesn't need Arrows to shoot, which is also nice."
	]
	quest.7C4EA3E09D1BE3F9.title: "&3Wrath of the &eDesert"
	quest.7C689E53C8E7971A.quest_desc: [
		"The &3&lOtherside&r is the birthplace of &3Sculk &fand &3Sculk creatures&r, including the &9&lWarden&r."
		""
		"Here you'll find many of his distant cousins, but don't worry there's also a few plus-sides to the &3&lOtherside&r!"
		""
		"There's plenty of new Building Blocks and Items we can find and &3Sculk&r everywhere for tons of &aXP&r!"
	]
	quest.7C689E53C8E7971A.title: "The &3&lOtherside"
	quest.7C7A1DDB1D72221C.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the power of the holder's Normal-type moves."
	quest.7C8CDD259495A31A.quest_desc: ["&eTunnels&r at the most basic level, will cover your &eBelts&r. This will make it so the &eItems&r can't be picked up, and hopefully the Mobs won't leave. \\n\\nIf you place another &eBelt&r moving perpendicular to the &eBelt&r the &eTunnel&r is on, the &eTunnel&r will filter 1 &eItem&r from the Stack of &eItems&r to the perpendicular &eBelt&r, while leaving the rest of the &eItems&r on the first &eBelt&r. \\n\\nIf there is just 1 &eItem&r, it will move through the &eTunnel&r like normal."]
	quest.7C8CDD259495A31A.title: "&eAndesite Tunnel"
	quest.7CBFC36BE695DF97.quest_desc: ["In the &9Twilight Forest&r, there are a bunch of new creatures to discover."]
	quest.7CBFC36BE695DF97.title: "The Silence of the Forest"
	quest.7CF8DA7614EF2E5E.quest_desc: [
		"&9Shattered&r spawn in quite a few Biomes in the &3&lOtherside&r."
		""
		"They act like mini &9&lWardens&r, being Blind relying on &3Sculk&r to find Enemies. They also attack all non-&3Sculk&r Mobs."
		""
		"&9Shattereds&r have 50 &4Hearts&r and pack quite a punch! So careful to not attract too many."
		""
		"If you can kill them, they'll drop &9Sculk Bones&r. These will be needed for a few Recipes."
	]
	quest.7CF8DA7614EF2E5E.title: "&9Shattered"
	quest.7D67058592EE5958.quest_desc: ["The Cannon will build the structures from Schematics, taking materials from nearby chests and using gunpowder as fuel."]
	quest.7D68FCB1C928FF9A.quest_desc: ["Adds the ability to pump liquids from the Tank Upgrade."]
	quest.7D7ECA49130AE980.quest_desc: ["A true rock-solid Trainer, Brock became a Gym Leader to support his many younger siblings. His dedication is unbreakable — just like his Onix!"]
	quest.7D7ECA49130AE980.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 14"
	quest.7D7ECA49130AE980.title: "Brock"
	quest.7DF2A4F06CA578EB.quest_desc: [
		"Indigo Mushroom Bog is much more filled Bog than the Blood Mushroom Bog."
		""
		"Of course it has Indigo Mushrooms but also Mini Smogstem Trees and ponds of Virulent Mix."
	]
	quest.7DF2A4F06CA578EB.title: "Indigo Mushroom Bog"
	quest.7E4D2B68862ACCFF.quest_subtitle: "Restores 1/8 HP to holder based on damage dealt by moves to opponents."
	quest.7EAEACEBE00D4850.quest_desc: [
		"&3Draugrs&r are similar to &5Deeplings&r as they have rankings. The &3Draugr&r rankings are: &3Draugr&r, &3Royal Draugr&r, and &3Elite Draugr&r."
		""
		"Normal &3Draugr&r have 14 &4Hearts&r and carry Black Steel Swords and Axes. These drop Rotten Flesh, Bones, and rarely Black Steel Nuggets."
		""
		"Next in line are &3Royal Draugr&r. These have 15 &4Hearts&r and carry Black Steel Targes along with the Swords and Axes. They drop the same Items as normal &3Draugrs&r."
		""
		"Last is the &3Elite Draugr&r. These switch between Black Steel Swords and Crossbows, depending on how far you are from them. They have 16 &4Hearts&r and drop, of course, the same loot!"
	]
	quest.7EAEACEBE00D4850.title: "&3Draugrs"
	quest.7EEEEDD5FF31ACD3.quest_desc: ["The &eSmart Chute&r is a &eChute&r with the options to Filter."]
	quest.7EEEEDD5FF31ACD3.title: "&eSmart Chute"
	quest.7F0F7111552F95A9.quest_desc: ["Okay we got our fully Assembled &5Train&r, now how do we use it? \\n\\nIf you are Controlling it, you'll need to Right Click the &5Train Controls&r. \\n\\nThen, you can Hold W to move Forward or Hold S to go Backwards. No, &5Trains&r don't turn like Cars do, they just follow the &7Tracks&r. \\n\\nGoing Forward you'll pick up a lot of Speed, you can see it in the Bar that replaces your &aExperience Bar&r. Backwards won't give as much Speed. \\n\\nIf you are getting near a &5Train Station&r and not moving at the speed of light, you can Hold Space to stop the &5Train&f at the &5Station&r. This is helpful for disassembling them or even connecting more &5Boogeys&r."]
	quest.7F0F7111552F95A9.title: "Controlling your &5Train"
	quest.7F4EFF677C47EE89.quest_desc: ["Trash Cans act as a way to destroy unwanted items, liquid, and power."]
	quest.7F4EFF677C47EE89.quest_subtitle: "Getting Rid of The Excess"
	quest.7F4EFF677C47EE89.title: "Trash Cans"
	quest.7F5F94706E1C599C.quest_desc: ["Misty isn’t just a Gym Leader — she dreams of becoming the world’s greatest Water-type Trainer. Fierce and stylish, she’s as unpredictable as the ocean."]
	quest.7F5F94706E1C599C.quest_subtitle: "&bRecommended: ~Lv 27"
	quest.7F5F94706E1C599C.title: "Misty"
	quest.7F6234196FF40B77.quest_desc: [
		"&fThe &a&lGarden Awakens&r&f update for Vanilla Backport brings a hauntingly beautiful new biome: the &a&lPale Garden&r&f. Venture into a quiet, eerie forest&r&f of Pale Oaks, Pale Moss, and whispering Eyeblossoms."
		""
		"&fBut beware, hidden within the trees lies the &c&lSculking Heart&r&f and its terrifying guardian, the &c&lSculking Mob&r&f. A new world of mystery, beauty, and danger awaits you beneath the pale canopy."
	]
	quest.7F6234196FF40B77.quest_subtitle: "&f&lBegin your exploration of the mysterious &a&lPale Garden&r&f&l biome"
	quest.7F8E50FA436DB4E6.quest_desc: ["&dEncased Chain Drives&r will act similar to &eBelts&r, by connecting &8Shafts&r to each other in a row. \\n\\nThere is quite a few differences though, like that &dEncased Chain Drives&r can be used with a &6Wrench&r to rotate. They also need to be placed directly next to other &dChain Drives&r to keep &dRotating&r. \\n\\nLike &eBelts&r though, they keep the same Speed and Stress Units as the original &8Shaft&r. Plus they keep the same direction!"]
	quest.7F8E50FA436DB4E6.title: "&dEncased Chain Drives"
	quest.7FA69CDDEEE70318.quest_desc: ["Adds a Sawmill GUI to the Backpack."]
	quest.7FB37FD5673413DA.quest_desc: [
		"Simply put an Enchanted Item in the Left Slot and a Book in the Middle Slot. Then, the Enchants will go to the Right Slot in Book form!"
		""
		"You can also use Enchanted Books instead of the Item to split up its Enchantments."
	]
	quest.7FB37FD5673413DA.title: "&l&bDis-Enchanting Table"
	quest.7FB4F525ECE051AF.quest_desc: [
		"Whether you are an experienced modded player, or a complete noob to MC, everyone has to make a &2Wooden Pickaxe&r."
		""
		"Pickaxes allow you to break most stone and metal blocks. This wooden one won't last long, so make sure to gather some &3Cobblestone&r with it!"
	]
	quest.7FB4F525ECE051AF.title: "Your First Pick"
	quest.7FED13E6E2559749.quest_desc: [
		"Not much change from &cNetherite&r to &9Warden&r for these Tools."
		""
		"Only real change is higher Attack Damage for all of them."
	]
	quest.7FED13E6E2559749.title: "&9Warden&r Tools"
	quest.7FF5C72E1046D769.quest_subtitle: "Boosts the critical-hit ratio of the holder's moves."
